msgid "Logos, @TeX{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:9690
#, no-wrap
msgid "@TeX{} logo"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:9691
#, no-wrap
msgid "@LaTeX{} logo"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:9696
msgid ""
"Use the @code{@@TeX@{@}} command to generate `@TeX{}'.  In a printed manual, "
"this is a special logo that is different from three ordinary letters.  In "
"other output formats, it just looks like @samp{TeX}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:9701
msgid ""
"Similarly, use the @code{@@LaTeX@{@}} command to generate `@LaTeX{}', which "
"is even more special in printed manuals (and different from the incorrect "
"@code{La@@TeX@{@}}.  In other output formats, the result is just "
"@samp{LaTeX}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:9704
msgid ""
"The spelling of these commands is unusual for Texinfo, in that they use both "
"uppercase and lowercase letters."
msgstr ""

