#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14317
msgid "Format with @command{texi2dvi}"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14318
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2dvi @r{(shell script)}"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14319
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2pdf @r{(shell script)}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14320
#, no-wrap
msgid "DVI, output in"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14321
#, no-wrap
msgid "PDF output"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14322
#, no-wrap
msgid "Output, in PDF"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14328
msgid ""
"The @command{texi2dvi} program takes care of all the steps for producing a "
"@TeX{} DVI file from a Texinfo document.  Similarly, @command{texi2pdf} "
"produces a PDF file@footnote{@dfn{PDF} stands for `Portable Document "
"Format'.  It was invented by Adobe Systems for document interchange, based "
"on their PostScript language.}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14331
msgid ""
"To run @command{texi2dvi} or @command{texi2pdf} on an input file "
"@file{foo.texi}, do this (where @samp{prompt$ } is your shell prompt):"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14335
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"prompt$ @kbd{texi2dvi foo.texi}\n"
"prompt$ @kbd{texi2pdf foo.texi}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14339
msgid ""
"As shown in this example, the file names given to @command{texi2dvi} and "
"@command{texi2pdf} must include any extension, such as @samp{.texi}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14342
msgid ""
"For a list of all the options, run @samp{texi2dvi --help}.  Some of the "
"options are discussed below."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14343
#, no-wrap
msgid "--pdf@r{, for @command{texi2dvi}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14344
#, no-wrap
msgid "pdftexi2dvi"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14353
msgid ""
"With the @option{--pdf} option, @command{texi2dvi} produces PDF output "
"instead of DVI, by running @command{pdftex} instead of @command{tex}.  "
"Alternatively, the command @command{texi2pdf} is an abbreviation for running "
"@samp{texi2dvi --pdf}.  The command @command{pdftexi2dvi} is also provided "
"as a convenience for AUC-@TeX{} (@pxref{Top,,, auctex, AUC-@TeX{}}), as it "
"prefers to merely prepend @samp{pdf} to DVI producing tools to have PDF "
"producing tools."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14354
#, no-wrap
msgid "--dvipdf@r{, for @command{texi2dvi}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14355
#, no-wrap
msgid "dvipdfmx"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14362
msgid ""
"With the @option{--dvipdf} option, @command{texi2dvi} produces PDF output by "
"running @TeX{} and then a DVI-to-PDF program: if the @env{DVIPDF} "
"environment variable is set, that value is used, else the first program "
"extant among @code{dvipdfmx}, @code{dvipdfm}, @code{dvipdf}, @code{dvi2pdf}, "
"@code{dvitopdf}.  This method generally supports CJK typesetting better than "
"@command{pdftex}."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14363
#, no-wrap
msgid "--ps@r{, for @command{texi2dvi}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14364
#, no-wrap
msgid "dvips"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14369
msgid ""
"With the @option{--ps} option, @command{texi2dvi} produces PostScript "
"instead of DVI, by running @command{tex} and then @command{dvips} "
"(@pxref{Top,,, dvips, Dvips}).  (Or the value of the @env{DVIPS} environment "
"variable, if set.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14370
#, no-wrap
msgid "--language@r{, for @command{texi2dvi}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14371
#, no-wrap
msgid "@LaTeX{}, processing with @command{texi2dvi}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14378
msgid ""
"@command{texi2dvi} can also be used to process @LaTeX{} files.  Normally "
"@command{texi2dvi} is able to guess the input file language by its contents "
"and file name extension; however, if it guesses wrong you can explicitly "
"specify the input language using @option{--language=@var{lang}} command line "
"option, where @var{lang} is either @samp{latex} or @samp{texinfo}."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14379
#, no-wrap
msgid "--command@r{, for @command{texi2dvi}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14389
msgid ""
"One useful option to @command{texi2dvi} is @samp{--command=@var{cmd}}.  This "
"inserts @var{cmd} on a line by itself at the start of the file in a "
"temporary copy of the input file, before running @TeX{}.  With this, you can "
"specify different printing formats, such as @code{@@smallbook} "
"(@pxref{@code{@@smallbook}}), @code{@@afourpaper} (@pxref{A4 Paper}), or "
"@code{@@pagesizes} (@pxref{@code{@@pagesizes}}), without actually changing "
"the document source.  (You can also do this on a site-wide basis with "
"@file{texinfo.cnf}; @pxref{Preparing for @TeX{}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14395
msgid ""
"The option @option{-E} (equivalently, @option{-e} and @option{--expand}) "
"does Texinfo macro expansion using @command{texi2any} instead of the @TeX{} "
"implementation (@pxref{Macro Details}).  Each implementation has its own "
"limitations and advantages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14401
msgid ""
"@command{texi2dvi} takes the @option{--build=@var{mode}} option to specify "
"where the @TeX{} compilation takes place, and, as a consequence, how "
"auxiliary files are treated.  The build mode can also be set using the "
"environment variable @env{TEXI2DVI_BUILD_MODE}.  The valid values for "
"@var{mode} are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14403
#, no-wrap
msgid "local"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14406
msgid ""
"Compile in the current directory, leaving all the auxiliary files around.  "
"This is the traditional TeX use."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14407
#, no-wrap
msgid "tidy"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14410
msgid ""
"Compile in a local @code{*.t2d} directory, where the auxiliary files are "
"left.  Output files are copied back to the original file."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14412
msgid "Using the @samp{tidy} mode brings several advantages:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14413
#, no-wrap
msgid "the current directory is not cluttered with plethora of temporary files."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14414
#, no-wrap
msgid "clutter can be even further reduced using @option{--build-dir=dir}: all"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14416
msgid "the @code{*.t2d} directories are stored there."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14416
#, no-wrap
msgid "clutter can be reduced to zero using, e.g.,"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14418
msgid ""
"@option{--build-dir=/tmp/\\$USER.t2d} or @option{--build-dir=\\$HOME/.t2d}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14418
#, no-wrap
msgid "the output file is updated after every successful @TeX{} run, for"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14421
msgid ""
"sake of concurrent visualization of the output.  In a @samp{local} build the "
"viewer stops during the whole @TeX{} run."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14421
#, no-wrap
msgid "if the compilation fails, the previous state of the output file"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14423
msgid "is preserved."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14423
#, no-wrap
msgid "@acronym{PDF} and @acronym{DVI} compilation are kept in separate"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14426
msgid ""
"subdirectories preventing any possibility of auxiliary file incompatibility."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14432
msgid ""
"On the other hand, because @samp{tidy} compilation takes place in another "
"directory, occasionally @TeX{} won't be able to find some files (e.g., when "
"using @code{\\graphicspath}): in that case, use @option{-I} to specify the "
"additional directories to consider."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14433
#, no-wrap
msgid "clean"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14436
msgid ""
"Same as @samp{tidy}, but remove the auxiliary directory afterwards.  Every "
"compilation therefore requires the full cycle."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14438
#, no-wrap
msgid "etex"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14444
msgid ""
"@command{texi2dvi} will use @command{etex} if it is available, because it "
"runs faster in some cases, and provides additional tracing information when "
"debugging @file{texinfo.tex}.  Nevertheless, this extended version of @TeX{} "
"is not required, and the DVI output is identical."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14445
#, no-wrap
msgid "file recorder for @TeX{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14446
#, no-wrap
msgid "@samp{\\openout} line in log file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14452
msgid ""
"@command{texi2dvi} attempts to detect auxiliary files output by @TeX{}, "
"either by using the @option{-recorder} option, or by scanning for "
"@samp{\\openout} in the log file that a run of @TeX{} produces.  You may "
"control how @command{texi2dvi} does this with the "
"@env{TEXI2DVI_USE_RECORDER} environment variable.  Valid values are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14454
#, no-wrap
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14456
msgid "use the @option{-recorder} option, no checks."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14457
#, no-wrap
msgid "no"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14459
msgid "scan for @samp{\\openout} in the log file, no checks."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14460
#, no-wrap
msgid "yesmaybe"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14464
msgid ""
"check whether @option{-recorder} option is supported, and if yes use it, "
"otherwise check for tracing @samp{\\openout} in the log file is supported, "
"and if yes use it, else it is an error."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14465
#, no-wrap
msgid "nomaybe"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14468
msgid ""
"same as @samp{yesmaybe}, except that the @samp{\\openout} trace in log file "
"is checked first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14472
msgid ""
"The default is @samp{nomaybe}.  This environment variable is provided for "
"troubleshooting purposes, and may change or disappear in the future."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14474 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14476
#, no-wrap
msgid "Format with @command{tex}/@command{texindex}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14476
msgid "@nodedescription Formatting with explicit shell commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14478
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shell formatting with @command{tex} and @command{texindex}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14479
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formatting with @command{tex} and @command{texindex}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14480
#, no-wrap
msgid "DVI file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14485
msgid ""
"You can do the basic formatting of a Texinfo file with the shell command "
"@command{tex} followed by the name of the Texinfo file.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14488
#, no-wrap
msgid "tex foo.texi\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14496
msgid ""
"@TeX{} will produce a @dfn{DVI file} as well as several auxiliary files "
"containing information for indices, cross-references, etc.  The DVI file "
"(for @dfn{DeVice Independent} file) can be printed on virtually any device, "
"perhaps after a further conversion (see the previous section)."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14497
#, no-wrap
msgid "texindex"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14504
msgid ""
"The @command{tex} formatting command itself does not sort the indices; it "
"writes an output file of unsorted index data.  To generate a printed index "
"after running the @command{tex} command, you first need a sorted index to "
"work from.  The @command{texindex} command sorts indices.  "
"(@command{texi2dvi}, described in the previous section, runs @command{tex} "
"and @command{texindex} as necessary.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14506
#, no-wrap
msgid "Names of index files"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14507
#, no-wrap
msgid "Index file names"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14515
msgid ""
"@command{tex} outputs unsorted index files under names following a standard "
"convention: the name of your main input file with any @samp{.texi} or "
"similar extension replaced by the two letter index name.  For example, the "
"raw index output files for the input file @file{foo.texi} would be, by "
"default, @file{foo.cp}, @file{foo.vr}, @file{foo.fn}, @file{foo.tp}, "
"@file{foo.pg} and @file{foo.ky}.  Those are exactly the arguments to give to "
"@command{texindex}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14517
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wildcards"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14518
#, no-wrap
msgid "Globbing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14522
msgid ""
"Instead of specifying all the unsorted index file names explicitly, it's "
"typical to use @samp{??} as shell wildcards and give the command in this "
"form:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14525
#, no-wrap
msgid "texindex foo.??\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14534
msgid ""
"This command will run @command{texindex} on all the unsorted index files, "
"including any two letter indices that you have defined yourself using "
"@code{@@defindex} or @code{@@defcodeindex}.  You can safely run "
"@samp{texindex foo.??} even if there are files with two letter extensions "
"that are not index files, such as @samp{foo.el}.  The @command{texindex} "
"command reports but otherwise ignores such files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14541
msgid ""
"For each file specified, @command{texindex} generates a sorted index file "
"whose name is made by appending @samp{s} to the input file name; for "
"example, @file{foo.cps} is made from @file{foo.cp}.  The @code{@@printindex} "
"command looks for a file with that name (@pxref{Printing Indices & Menus}).  "
"@TeX{} does not read the raw index output file, and @command{texindex} does "
"not alter it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14545
msgid ""
"After you have sorted the indices, you need to rerun @command{tex} on the "
"Texinfo file.  This regenerates the output file, this time with up-to-date "
"index entries."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14548
msgid ""
"Finally, you may need to run @command{tex} one more time, to get the page "
"numbers in the cross-references correct."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14551
msgid ""
"To summarize, this is a five-step process.  (Alternatively, it's a one-step "
"process: run @command{texi2dvi}; see the previous section.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14557
msgid ""
"Run @command{tex} on your Texinfo file.  This generates a DVI file (with "
"undefined cross-references and no indices), and the raw index files (with "
"two letter extensions)."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14561
msgid ""
"Run @command{texindex} on the raw index files.  This creates the "
"corresponding sorted index files (with three letter extensions)."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14567
msgid ""
"Run @command{tex} again on your Texinfo file.  This regenerates the DVI "
"file, this time with indices and defined cross-references, but with page "
"numbers for the cross-references from the previous run, generally incorrect."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14570
msgid "Sort the indices again, with @command{texindex}."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14574
msgid ""
"Run @command{tex} one last time.  This time the correct page numbers are "
"written for the cross-references."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14576
#, no-wrap
msgid "pdftex"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14580
msgid ""
"To generate PDF, you can run the @command{pdftex} program instead of plain "
"@command{tex}.  That is, run @command{pdftex foo.texi} instead of @samp{tex "
"foo.texi} in the examples above."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14582 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14583
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formatting Partial Documents"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14585
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formatting partial documents"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14586
#, no-wrap
msgid "Partial documents, formatting"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14587
#, no-wrap
msgid "Chapters, formatting one at a time"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14588
#, no-wrap
msgid "Auxiliary files, omitting"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14589
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pointer validation @subentry suppressing"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14590 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15817
#, no-wrap
msgid "novalidate"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14598
msgid ""
"Sometimes you may wish to print a document while you know it is incomplete, "
"or to print just one chapter of a document.  In such a case, the usual "
"auxiliary files that @TeX{} creates and warnings @TeX{} gives about "
"undefined cross-references are just nuisances.  You can avoid them with the "
"@code{@@novalidate} command, which you must give @emph{before} any "
"sectioning or cross-reference commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14600
msgid "Thus, the beginning of your file would look approximately like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14605
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@novalidate\n"
"@dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14611
msgid ""
"@code{@@novalidate} also turns off validation in @command{texi2any}, just "
"like its @code{--no-validate} option (@pxref{Invoking @command{texi2any}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14617
msgid ""
"Furthermore, you need not run @command{texindex} each time after you run "
"@command{tex}.  The @command{tex} formatting command simply uses whatever "
"sorted index files happen to exist from a previous use of "
"@command{texindex}.  If those are out of date, that is usually ok while you "
"are creating or debugging a document."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14619 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14620
#, no-wrap
msgid "Details of @command{texindex}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14622
#, no-wrap
msgid "Braces, in index entries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14629
msgid ""
"In Texinfo version 6, released in 2015, the @command{texindex} program was "
"completely reimplemented.  The principal functional difference is that index "
"entries beginning with a left brace or right brace (@samp{@{} resp.@: "
"@samp{@}}) can work properly.  For example, these simple index entries are "
"processed correctly, including the ``index initial'' shown in the index:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14635
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@cindex @@@{\n"
"@@cindex @@@}\n"
"...\n"
"@@printindex cp\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14637
#, no-wrap
msgid "Literate programming, with Texinfo and @command{awk}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14638
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo, and literate programming"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14639
#, no-wrap
msgid "Robbins, Arnold"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14640
#, no-wrap
msgid "texiwebjr"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14641
#, no-wrap
msgid "ti.twjr"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14648
msgid ""
"Although not a matter of functionality, readers may be interested to know "
"that the new @command{texindex} is a literate program (@url{https://"
"en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Literate_programming}) using Texinfo for documentation "
"and (portable) @command{awk} for code.  A single source file, @file{texindex/"
"ti.twjr} in this case, produces the runnable program, a printable document, "
"and an online document."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14654
msgid ""
"The system is called TexiWeb Jr.@: and was created by Arnold Robbins, who "
"also wrote the new @command{texindex}.  Not coincidentally, he is also the "
"long-time maintainer of @command{gawk} (GNU Awk, @pxref{Top,,, gawk, The GNU "
"Awk User's Guide}).  The file @file{texindex/Makefile.am} shows example "
"usage of the system."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14656 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14658
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14659
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preparing for @TeX{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14658
msgid "@nodedescription What to do before you use @TeX{}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14660
#, no-wrap
msgid "@TeX{} input initialization"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14661
#, no-wrap
msgid "@sortas{profile init} @file{.profile} initialization file"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14662
#, no-wrap
msgid "@sortas{cshrc init} @file{.cshrc} initialization file"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14663
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialization file for @TeX{} input"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14671
msgid ""
"@TeX{} needs to find the @file{texinfo.tex} file that the @samp{\\input "
"texinfo} command on the first line reads.  The @file{texinfo.tex} file tells "
"@TeX{} how to handle @@-commands; it is included in all standard GNU "
"distributions.  The latest version released for general use is available "
"from the usual GNU servers and mirrors:"
msgstr ""

#. type: display
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14675
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@uref{https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/texinfo/texinfo.tex}\n"
"@uref{https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/texinfo/texinfo.tex}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14679
msgid ""
"The latest development version is available from the Texinfo source "
"repository:"
msgstr ""

#. type: display
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14682
#, no-wrap
msgid "@uref{https://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/texinfo.git/plain/doc/texinfo.tex}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14684
#, no-wrap
msgid "texinfo.tex@r{, installing}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14691
msgid ""
"@file{texinfo.tex} is essentially a standalone file, so, if you need or want "
"to try a newer version than came with your system, it nearly always suffices "
"to download it and put it anywhere that @TeX{} will find it.  You can "
"replace any existing @file{texinfo.tex} with a newer version (of course "
"saving the original in case of disaster)."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14692
#, no-wrap
msgid "epsf.tex@r{, installing}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14696
msgid ""
"Also, you should install @file{epsf.tex}, if it is not already installed "
"from another distribution.  More details are at the end of the description "
"of the @code{@@image} command (@pxref{Images})."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14697
#, no-wrap
msgid "European Computer Modern fonts @subentry installing"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14698
#, no-wrap
msgid "EC fonts, installing"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14699
#, no-wrap
msgid "CM-Super fonts @subentry installing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14703
msgid ""
"To use quotation marks other than those used in English, you'll need to have "
"the European Computer Modern fonts (e.g., @file{ecrm1000}) and (for PDF "
"output) CM-Super fonts (@pxref{Inserting Quotation Marks})."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14704
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{feymr10} @subentry installing"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14705
#, no-wrap
msgid "Euro font, installing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14708
msgid ""
"To use the @code{@@euro} command, you'll need the @samp{feym*} fonts (e.g., "
"@file{feymr10}).  @xref{@code{@@euro}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14711
msgid ""
"All of the above files should be installed by default in a reasonable @TeX{} "
"installation."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14712
#, no-wrap
msgid "texinfo.cnf @r{installation}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14713
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customizing of @TeX{} for Texinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14714
#, no-wrap
msgid "Site-wide Texinfo configuration file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14724
msgid ""
"Optionally, you may create a file @file{texinfo.cnf} for site "
"configuration.  When processing a Texinfo file, @TeX{} looks for this file "
"in its search path, which includes the current directory and standard "
"installation directories.  You can use this file for local conventions.  For "
"example, if @file{texinfo.cnf} contains the line @samp{@@afourpaper} "
"(@pxref{A4 Paper}), then all Texinfo documents will be processed with that "
"page size in effect.  If you have nothing to put in @file{texinfo.cnf}, you "
"do not need to create it."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14725
#, no-wrap
msgid "Environment variable @code{TEXINPUTS}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14726
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXINPUTS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14733
msgid ""
"You can set the @code{TEXINPUTS} environment variable to allow @TeX{} to "
"find @file{texinfo.cnf}.  (This also works for @file{texinfo.tex} and any "
"other file @TeX{} might read).  For example, if you are using a Bourne shell-"
"compatible shell (@code{sh}, @code{bash}, @code{ksh}, @dots{}), your "
"@file{.profile} file could contain the lines:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14737
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"TEXINPUTS=.:/home/me/mylib:\n"
"export TEXINPUTS\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14745
msgid ""
"These settings would cause @TeX{} first to look for an @file{\\input} file "
"in the current directory, indicated by the @samp{.}, then in a hypothetical "
"user @samp{me}'s @file{mylib} directory, and finally in the system "
"directories.  (A leading, trailing, or doubled @samp{:} indicates searching "
"the system directories at that point.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14747
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overfull hboxes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14749
msgid "@nodedescription What are and what to do with overfull hboxes."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14749
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overfull ``hboxes''"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14750
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overfull @samp{hboxes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14751
#, no-wrap
msgid "@samp{hbox}, overfull"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14752
#, no-wrap
msgid "Final output"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14759
msgid ""
"@TeX{} is sometimes unable to typeset a line within the normal margins.  "
"This most often occurs when @TeX{} comes upon what it interprets as a long "
"word that it cannot hyphenate, such as an electronic mail network address or "
"a very long identifier.  When this happens, @TeX{} prints an error message "
"like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14762
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overfull @@hbox (20.76302pt too wide)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14764
#, no-wrap
msgid "hbox"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14768
msgid ""
"(In @TeX{}, lines are in ``horizontal boxes'', hence the term, ``hbox''.  "
"@samp{@@hbox} is a @TeX{} primitive not used in the Texinfo language.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14773
msgid ""
"@TeX{} also provides the line number in the Texinfo source file and the text "
"of the offending line, which is marked at all the places that @TeX{} "
"considered hyphenation.  @xref{Debugging with @TeX{}}, for more information "
"about typesetting errors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14778
msgid ""
"If the Texinfo file has an overfull hbox, you can rewrite the sentence so "
"the overfull hbox does not occur, or you can decide to leave it.  A small "
"excursion into the right margin often does not matter and may not even be "
"noticeable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14783
msgid ""
"If you have many overfull boxes and/or an antipathy to rewriting, you can "
"coerce @TeX{} into greatly increasing the allowable interword spacing, thus "
"(if you're lucky) avoiding many of the bad line breaks, like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14784
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\emergencystretch"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14789
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@tex\n"
"\\global\\emergencystretch = .9\\hsize\n"
"@@end tex\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14797
msgid ""
"(You should adjust the fraction as needed.)  This huge value for "
"@code{\\emergencystretch} cannot be the default, since then the typeset "
"output would generally be of noticeably lower quality; its default value is "
"@samp{.15\\hsize}.  @code{\\hsize} is the @TeX{} dimension containing the "
"current line width."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14798
#, no-wrap
msgid "Black rectangle in hardcopy"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14799
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rectangle, black in hardcopy"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14800
#, no-wrap
msgid "Box, ugly black in hardcopy"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14801
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ugly black rectangles in hardcopy"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14806
msgid ""
"For any overfull boxes you do have, @TeX{} will print a large, ugly, black "
"rectangle beside the line that contains the overfull hbox unless told "
"otherwise.  This is so you will notice the location of the problem if you "
"are correcting a draft."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14807
#, no-wrap
msgid "finalout"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14811
msgid ""
"To prevent such a monstrosity from marring your final printout, write the "
"following in the beginning of the Texinfo file on a line of its own, before "
"the @code{@@maketitle} or @code{@@titlepage} command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14814
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@finalout\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14816 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14818
#, no-wrap
msgid "Printing Japanese and Chinese"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14818
msgid "@nodedescription XeTeX or LuaTeX required."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14820
#, no-wrap
msgid "Chinese language"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14821
#, no-wrap
msgid "Japanese language"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14824
msgid ""
"Texinfo comes with support files for processing input in the Japanese and "
"Chinese languages."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14825
#, no-wrap
msgid "Japanese with Xe@TeX{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14826
#, no-wrap
msgid "Japanese with LuaTeX"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14832
msgid ""
"For Japanese, you use the @file{texinfo-ja.tex} file. Your main input file "
"should begin with a @samp{\\input texinfo-ja} line, rather than the standard "
"@w{@samp{\\input texinfo}}.  Use the UTF-8 character encoding as usual.  You "
"must process the files with either Xe@TeX{} or LuaTeX."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14833
#, no-wrap
msgid "Chinese with Xe@TeX{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14839
msgid ""
"For Chinese, you use the @file{texinfo-zh.tex} file. Your main input file "
"should begin with a @samp{\\input texinfo-zh} line, rather than the standard "
"@w{@samp{\\input texinfo}}.  Use the UTF-8 character encoding as usual.  You "
"must process the files with Xe@TeX{}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14844
msgid ""
"For example, you would run @samp{PDFTEX=xetex texi2pdf @var{my-input-"
"file.texi}} to use Xe@TeX{} to produce PDF output.  You may have to install "
"Xe@TeX{} (or LuaTeX), the @samp{zhspacing} package, and/or font packages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14848
msgid ""
"Neither Japanese nor Chinese is supported with the standard @TeX{} (or "
"pdf@TeX{}) program, as it cannot support the fonts and thousands of glyphs "
"needed for these languages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14853
msgid ""
"The Texinfo distribution comes with a couple of sample files that you can "
"use to test support for these languages: @samp{short-sample-ja.texi} for "
"Japanese, and @samp{short-sample-zh.texi} for Chinese."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14854
#, no-wrap
msgid "Xe@TeX{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14855
#, no-wrap
msgid "LuaTeX"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14859
msgid ""
"For more information on these extensions to @TeX{}, see @uref{https://"
"tug.org/xetex/, the Xe@TeX{} home page} and @uref{https://www.luatex.org/, "
"the LuaTeX website}."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14861
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generic Translator @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14863
msgid "@nodedescription @command{texi2any}, an all-purpose converter."
msgstr ""

#. type: chapter
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14863
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{texi2any}: The Translator for Texinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14868
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} is the generic translator for Texinfo that can produce "
"different output formats and is highly customizable.  It supports these "
"formats:"
msgstr ""

#. type: display
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14877
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Info (by default, or with @option{--info}),\n"
"HTML (with @option{--html}),\n"
"EPUB 3 (with @option{--epub3}),\n"
"plain text (with @option{--plaintext}),\n"
"@LaTeX{} (with @option{--latex}),\n"
"DocBook (with @option{--docbook}),\n"
"Texinfo XML (with @option{--xml}).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14882
msgid ""
"@command{makeinfo} is an alias for @command{texi2any}.  By default, both "
"@command{texi2any} and @command{makeinfo} generate Info output; indeed, "
"there are no differences in behavior based on the name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14890
msgid ""
"Beside these default formats, command line options to @command{texi2any} can "
"change many aspects of the output.  Beyond that, initialization files "
"provide even more control over the final output---nearly anything not "
"specified in the Texinfo input file.  Initialization files are written in "
"Perl, and anything which can be specified on the command line can also be "
"specified within a initialization file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14901
msgid ""
"Two functionally equivalent implementations of @command{texi2any} can be "
"built in GNU Texinfo, one in Perl and another in compiled native code (in "
"C).  The native code implementation is still experimental.  The Perl program "
"can use Perl extension modules in compiled native code, while the native "
"code program embeds a Perl interpreter for the parts that require Perl."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14905
msgid ""
"In the default case, the Perl implementation is installed.  You can select "
"the experimental C implementation instead at build time by passing the "
"@option{--enable-using-c-texi2any} option to @command{configure}."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14907
#, no-wrap
msgid "Invoking @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14909
msgid "@nodedescription Running the translator from a shell."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14909
#, no-wrap
msgid "Invoking @command{texi2any} from a Shell"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14912
msgid "Invoking makeinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14912
#, no-wrap
msgid "makeinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14913
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2any"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14919
msgid ""
"To process a Texinfo file, invoke @command{texi2any} followed by the name of "
"the Texinfo file.  Also select the format you want to output with the "
"appropriate command line option (default is Info).  Thus, to create the Info "
"file for Bison, type the following to the shell:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14922
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2any --info bison.texi\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14926
msgid ""
"You can specify more than one input file name; each is processed in turn.  "
"If an input file name is @samp{-}, standard input is read."
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14929
msgid "@command{makeinfo} Options"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14929
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{makeinfo} options"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14930
#, no-wrap
msgid "Options for @command{makeinfo}"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14932
msgid "@command{texi2any} Options"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14932
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{texi2any} options"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14933
#, no-wrap
msgid "Options for @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14938
msgid ""
"The @command{texi2any} program accepts many options.  Perhaps the most basic "
"are those that change the output format.  By default, @command{texi2any} "
"outputs Info."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14942
msgid ""
"Each command line option is either a long name preceded by @samp{--} or a "
"single letter preceded by @samp{-}.  You can use abbreviations for the long "
"option names as long as they are unique."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14946
msgid ""
"For example, you could use the following shell command to create an Info "
"file for @file{bison.texi} in which lines are filled to only 68 columns:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14949
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2any --fill-column=68 bison.texi\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14952
msgid "You can write two or more options in sequence, like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14955
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2any --no-split --fill-column=70 @dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14960
msgid ""
"(This would keep the Info file together as one possibly very long file and "
"would also set the fill column to 70.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14962
msgid "The options are (approximately in alphabetical order):"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14964 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14965
#, no-wrap
msgid "--commands-in-node-names"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14969
msgid ""
"This option now does nothing, but remains for compatibility.  (It used to "
"ensure that @@-commands in node names were expanded throughout the document, "
"especially @code{@@value}.  This is now done by default.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14970 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14971
#, no-wrap
msgid "--conf-dir=@var{dir}"
msgstr ""

#.  @xref{Loading
#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14978
msgid ""
"Prepend @var{dir} to the directory search list for finding customization "
"files that may be loaded with @option{--init-file} (see below).  The "
"@var{dir} value can be a single directory, or a list of several directories "
"separated by the usual path separator character (@samp{:} on Unix-like "
"systems, @samp{;} on Windows)."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14979
#, no-wrap
msgid "--css-include=@var{file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14980
#, no-wrap
msgid "--css-include"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14985
msgid ""
"When producing HTML, literally include the contents of @var{file}, which "
"should contain Cascading Style Sheets specifications, in the @samp{<style>} "
"block of the HTML output.  If @var{file} is @samp{-}, read standard input.  "
"@xref{HTML CSS}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14986
#, no-wrap
msgid "--css-ref=@var{url}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14987
#, no-wrap
msgid "--css-ref"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14991
msgid ""
"When producing HTML, add a @samp{<link>} tag to the output which references "
"a cascading style sheet at @var{url}.  This allows using standalone style "
"sheets."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14992 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14994
#, no-wrap
msgid "-D @var{var}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14993
#, no-wrap
msgid "-D '@var{var} @var{value}'"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:14998
msgid ""
"Cause the Texinfo variable @var{var} to be defined.  This is equivalent to "
"@code{@@set @var{var}} in the Texinfo file (@pxref{@code{@@set @@clear "
"@@value}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15003
msgid ""
"The argument to the option is always one word to the shell; if it contains "
"internal whitespace, the first word is taken as the variable name and the "
"remainder as the value.  For example, @code{-D 'myvar someval'} is "
"equivalent to @code{@@set myvar someval}."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15004 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15005
#, no-wrap
msgid "--docbook"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15007
msgid "Generate DocBook output (rather than Info)."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15008
#, no-wrap
msgid "--document-language=@var{lang}"
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15009 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15796
#, no-wrap
msgid "--document-language"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15014
msgid ""
"Use @var{lang} to translate Texinfo keywords which end up in the output "
"document.  The default is the locale specified by the "
"@code{@@documentlanguage} command if there is one, otherwise English "
"(@pxref{@code{@@documentlanguage}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15015 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15016
#, no-wrap
msgid "--dvi"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15019
msgid ""
"Generate a TeX DVI file using @command{texi2dvi}, rather than Info "
"(@pxref{@command{texi2any} Printed Output})."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15020 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15021
#, no-wrap
msgid "--dvipdf"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15024
msgid ""
"Generate a PDF file using @command{texi2dvi --dvipdf}, rather than Info "
"(@pxref{@command{texi2any} Printed Output})."
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15025 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15027
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15794
#, no-wrap
msgid "--enable-encoding"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15026 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15028
#, no-wrap
msgid "--disable-encoding"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15035
msgid ""
"By default, or with @option{--enable-encoding}, output accented and special "
"characters in Info and plain text output based on the document encoding.  "
"With @option{--disable-encoding}, 7-bit ASCII transliterations are output.  "
"Also obeyed in other output formats for index keys sorting and for some "
"plain text output."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15036 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15037
#, no-wrap
msgid "--epub3"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15039
msgid "Generate EPUB 3 output."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15040 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15042
#, no-wrap
msgid "--error-limit=@var{limit}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15041 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15043
#, no-wrap
msgid "-e @var{limit}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15047
msgid ""
"Report @var{limit} errors before aborting (on the assumption that continuing "
"would be useless); default 100."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15048 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15050
#, no-wrap
msgid "--fill-column=@var{width}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15049 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15051
#, no-wrap
msgid "-f @var{width}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15059
msgid ""
"Specify the maximum number of columns in a line; this is the right-hand edge "
"of a line.  Paragraphs that are filled will be filled to this width.  "
"(Filling is the process of breaking up and connecting lines so that lines "
"are the same length as or shorter than the number specified as the fill "
"column.  Lines are broken between words.) The default value is 72."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15060 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15062
#, no-wrap
msgid "--footnote-style=@var{style}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15061 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15063
#, no-wrap
msgid "-s @var{style}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15070
msgid ""
"Set the footnote style to @var{style}: either @samp{end} for the end node "
"style (the default) or @samp{separate} for the separate node style.  The "
"value set by this option overrides the value set in a Texinfo file by a "
"@code{@@footnotestyle} command (@pxref{Footnote Styles})."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15075
msgid ""
"In Info, when the footnote style is @samp{separate}, @command{texi2any} "
"makes a new node containing the footnotes found in the current node.  When "
"the footnote style is @samp{end}, @command{texi2any} places the footnote "
"references at the end of the current node."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15080
msgid ""
"In HTML, when the footnote style is @samp{end}, or if the output is not "
"split, footnotes are put at the end of the output.  If set to "
"@samp{separate}, and the output is split, they are placed in a separate file."
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15081 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15083
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15807
#, no-wrap
msgid "--force"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15082 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15084
#, no-wrap
msgid "-F"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15088
msgid ""
"Ordinarily, if the input file has errors, the output files are not created.  "
"With this option, they are preserved."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15089 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17165
#, no-wrap
msgid "--help"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15090 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15092
#, no-wrap
msgid "-h"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15091
#, no-wrap
msgid "--help@r{, for @command{texi2any}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15095
msgid ""
"Print a message with available options and basic usage, then exit "
"successfully."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15096 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15097
#, no-wrap
msgid "--html"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15102
msgid ""
"Generate HTML output (rather than Info).  By default, the HTML output is "
"split into one output file per node, and the split output is written into a "
"subdirectory based on the name of the input file.  @xref{Generating HTML}."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15103 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15104
#, no-wrap
msgid "-I @var{dir}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15112
msgid ""
"Append @var{dir} to the directory search list for finding files that are "
"included using the @code{@@include} command.  By default, @command{texi2any} "
"searches the current directory and the input file path leading directory if "
"there is one (and it is not the current directory).  The @var{dir} value can "
"be a single directory or a list of several directories separated by the "
"usual path separator character (@samp{:} on Unix-like systems, @samp{;} on "
"Windows)."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15113 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15114
#, no-wrap
msgid "--ifdocbook"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15115 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15116
#, no-wrap
msgid "--ifhtml"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15117 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15118
#, no-wrap
msgid "--ifinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15119 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15120
#, no-wrap
msgid "--iflatex"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15121 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15122
#, no-wrap
msgid "--ifplaintext"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15123 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15124
#, no-wrap
msgid "--iftex"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15125 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15126
#, no-wrap
msgid "--ifxml"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15133
msgid ""
"For the given format, process @samp{@@if@var{format}} and "
"@samp{@@@var{format}} commands, and do not process "
"@samp{@@ifnot@var{format}}, regardless of the format being output.  For "
"instance, if @option{--iftex} is given, then @samp{@@iftex} and @samp{@@tex} "
"blocks will be read, and @samp{@@ifnottex} blocks will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15134 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15135
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-ifdocbook"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15136 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15137
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-ifhtml"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15138 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15139
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-ifinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15140 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15141
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-iflatex"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15142 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15143
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-ifplaintext"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15144 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15145
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-iftex"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15146 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15147
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-ifxml"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15154
msgid ""
"For the given format, do not process @samp{@@if@var{format}} and "
"@samp{@@@var{format}} commands, and do process @samp{@@ifnot@var{format}}, "
"regardless of the format being output.  For instance, if @option{--no-"
"ifhtml} is given, then @samp{@@ifhtml} and @samp{@@html} blocks will not be "
"read, and @samp{@@ifnothtml} blocks will be."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15156 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15157
#, no-wrap
msgid "--info"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15163
msgid ""
"Generate Info output.  By default, if the output file contains more than "
"about 300,000 bytes, it is split into shorter subfiles of about that size.  "
"The name of the output file and any subfiles is determined by the input file "
"name, or by @code{@@setfilename}, if present (@pxref{Setting the Output File "
"Name}).  @xref{Tag and Split Files}."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15164 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15165
#, no-wrap
msgid "--init-file=@var{file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15173
msgid ""
"Load @var{file} as code to modify the behavior and output of the generated "
"manual.  It is customary to use the @code{.pm} or the @code{.init} "
"extensions for these customization files, but that is not enforced; the "
"@var{file} name can be anything.  The @option{--conf-dir} option (see above) "
"can be used to add to the list of directories in which these customization "
"files are searched for."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15174 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15175
#, no-wrap
msgid "--internal-links=@var{file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15176
#, no-wrap
msgid "Internal links, of HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15181
msgid ""
"In HTML mode, output a tab-separated file containing three columns: the "
"internal link to an item, the type of the item and the name of the item or "
"the term corresponding to the item which was indexed or entered."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15183
msgid "The items output are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15184
#, no-wrap
msgid "output units"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15188
msgid ""
"Output units are the main unit of output documents.  Output units contain "
"the content associated with a node or a sectioning command.  The item name "
"is the associated node or a sectioning command name."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15188
#, no-wrap
msgid "sectioning commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15191
msgid ""
"The command name without @code{@@}, adjusted for raise/lowersections is "
"prepended to the item name."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15191
#, no-wrap
msgid "nodes, anchors and floats"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15193
msgid "The type of the element is the command name without @code{@@}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15193
#, no-wrap
msgid "index entries"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15195
msgid "The type of the element is the name of the index."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15200
msgid ""
"The items are in the natural sorting order for the given element.  This dump "
"can be useful for post-processors."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15201 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15202
#, no-wrap
msgid "--latex"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15204
msgid "Generate @LaTeX{} output."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15205 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15207
#, no-wrap
msgid "--macro-expand=@var{file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15206 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15208
#, no-wrap
msgid "-E @var{file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15213
msgid ""
"Output the Texinfo source, with all Texinfo macros expanded, to @var{file}.  "
"Normally, the result of macro expansion is used internally by "
"@command{texi2any} and then discarded."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15214 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15215
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-headers"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15216
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node separators, omitting with @option{--no-headers}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15217
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generating plain text files with @option{--no-headers}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15218
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menus, omitting with @option{--no-headers}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15221
msgid "Do not include menus or node separator lines in the output."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15226
msgid ""
"When generating Info, this is the same as using @option{--plaintext}, "
"resulting in a simple plain text file.  Furthermore, output is to standard "
"output unless overridden with @option{-o}.  (This behavior is for backward "
"compatibility.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15227
#, no-wrap
msgid "Navigation links, omitting"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15232
msgid ""
"When generating HTML, and output is split, also output navigation links only "
"at the beginning of each file.  If output is not split, do not include "
"navigation links at the top of each node at all.  @xref{Generating HTML}."
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15233 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15235
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15244 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15825
#, no-wrap
msgid "--node-files"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15234 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15236
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-node-files"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15244
msgid ""
"With @option{--node-files}, when generating HTML, create redirection files "
"for anchors and any nodes not already output with the file name "
"corresponding to the node name (@pxref{HTML Xref Node Name Expansion}).  "
"This makes it possible for section- and chapter-level cross-manual "
"references to succeed (@pxref{HTML Xref Configuration})."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15251
msgid ""
"If the output is split, this is enabled by default.  If the output is not "
"split, @option{--node-files} enables the creation of the redirection files, "
"in addition to the monolithic main output file.  @option{--no-node-files} "
"suppresses the creation of redirection files in any case.  This option has "
"no effect with any output format other than HTML@.  @xref{Generating HTML}."
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15252 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15254
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15819
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-validate"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15253 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15255
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-pointer-validate"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15256
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pointer validation"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15261
msgid "Pointer Validation"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15261
msgid ""
"Suppress the pointer-validation phase of @command{texi2any}---a dangerous "
"thing to do.  This can also be done with the @code{@@novalidate} command "
"(@pxref{Formatting Partial Documents})."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15265
msgid ""
"If you do not suppress pointer validation, @command{texi2any} will check the "
"validity of cross-references and menu entries in the Texinfo file, as well "
"as node pointers if they are given explicitly."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15282
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If a `Next', `Previous', or `Up' node reference is a reference to a\n"
"node in the current file and is not an external reference such as to\n"
"@file{(dir)}, then the referenced node must exist.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15285
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every node except the `Top' node must have an `Up' pointer.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15290
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The node referenced by an `Up' pointer must itself reference the\n"
"current node through a menu item, unless the node referenced by `Up'\n"
"has the form @samp{(@var{file})}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15293 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15294
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15822
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-warn"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15297
msgid "Suppress warning messages (but not error messages)."
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15298 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15828
#, no-wrap
msgid "--number-footnotes"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15299 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15300
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-number-footnotes"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15305
msgid ""
"With @option{--no-number-footnotes}, suppress automatic footnote numbering.  "
"By default, footnotes are numbered sequentially within a node, i.e., the "
"current footnote number is reset to 1 at the start of each node."
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15306 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15308
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15831
#, no-wrap
msgid "--number-sections"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15307 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15309
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-number-sections"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15315
msgid ""
"With @option{--number-sections} (the default), output chapter, section, and "
"appendix numbers as in printed manuals.  This works only with hierarchically "
"structured manuals.  You should specify @code{--no-number-sections} if your "
"manual is not normally structured."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15317 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15319
#, no-wrap
msgid "--output=@var{file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15318 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15320
#, no-wrap
msgid "-o @var{file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15328
msgid ""
"Specify that the output should be directed to @var{file}.  This overrides "
"any file name specified in a @code{@@setfilename} command found in the "
"Texinfo source.  If neither @code{@@setfilename} nor this option are "
"specified, the input file name is used to determine the output name.  "
"@xref{Setting the Output File Name}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15331
msgid ""
"If @var{file} is @samp{-}, output goes to standard output and @samp{--no-"
"split} is implied."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15338
msgid ""
"If @var{file} is a directory or ends with a @samp{/} the usual rules are "
"used to determine the output file name (namely, use @code{@@setfilename} or "
"the input file name) but the files are written to the @var{file} directory.  "
"For example, @samp{texi2any -o bar/ foo.texi}, with or without @option{--no-"
"split}, will write @file{bar/foo.info}, and possibly other files, under "
"@file{bar/}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15343
msgid ""
"When generating HTML and output is split, @var{file} is used as the name for "
"the directory into which all files are written.  For example, @samp{texi2any "
"-o bar --html foo.texi} will write @file{bar/index.html}, among other files."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15349
msgid ""
"When generating EPUB a container directory for the files and directories "
"needed for the EPUB format is created, as well as the EPUB output file.  If "
"@var{file} corresponds to a directory, the container directory is placed "
"within @var{file}.  The EPUB output file is never put in this directory.  If "
"@var{file} corresponds to a file, it is used for the EPUB output file name."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15350
#, no-wrap
msgid "--output-indent=@var{val}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15351
#, no-wrap
msgid "--outputindent"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15354
msgid ""
"This option now does nothing, but remains for compatibility.  (It used to "
"alter indentation in XML/DocBook output.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15355 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15356
#, no-wrap
msgid "-P @var{path}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15359
msgid ""
"Prepend @var{path} to the directory search list for @code{@@include}.  See "
"@samp{-I} above."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15360 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15362
#, no-wrap
msgid "--paragraph-indent=@var{indent}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15361 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15363
#, no-wrap
msgid "-p @var{indent}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15368
msgid ""
"Set the paragraph indentation style to @var{indent}.  The value set by this "
"option overrides the value set in a Texinfo file by an "
"@code{@@paragraphindent} command (@pxref{@code{@@paragraphindent}}).  The "
"value of @var{indent} is interpreted as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15373
msgid ""
"Preserve any existing indentation (or lack thereof) at the beginnings of "
"paragraphs."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15374
#, no-wrap
msgid "@samp{0} or @samp{none}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15376
msgid "Delete any existing indentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: var{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15377
#, no-wrap
msgid "num"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15379
msgid "Indent each paragraph by @var{num} spaces."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15383
msgid ""
"The default is to indent by two spaces, except for paragraphs following a "
"section heading, which are not indented."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15384 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15385
#, no-wrap
msgid "--pdf"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15388
msgid ""
"Generate a PDF file using @command{texi2dvi --pdf}, rather than Info "
"(@pxref{@command{texi2any} Printed Output})."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15389 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15390
#, no-wrap
msgid "--plaintext"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15391
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plain text output with @option{--plaintext}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15392
#, no-wrap
msgid "ASCII text output with @option{--plaintext}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15393
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generating plain text files with @option{--plaintext}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15394
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node separators, omitting with @option{--plaintext}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15395
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menus, omitting with @option{--plaintext}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15396
#, no-wrap
msgid "@file{INSTALL} file, generating"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15402
msgid ""
"Output a plain text file (rather than Info): do not include menus or node "
"separator lines in the output.  This results in a straightforward plain text "
"file that you can (for example) send in email without complications, or "
"include in a distribution (for example, an @file{INSTALL} file)."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15406
msgid ""
"With this option the output goes to standard output by default, instead of "
"to a file with a name based on the input file name or @code{@@setfilename}; "
"this can be overridden with @option{-o}."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15407 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15408
#, no-wrap
msgid "--ps"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15411
msgid ""
"Generate a PostScript file using @command{texi2dvi --ps}, rather than Info "
"(@pxref{@command{texi2any} Printed Output})."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15412 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15414
#, no-wrap
msgid "--set-customization-variable @var{var}=@var{value}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15413 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15415
#, no-wrap
msgid "-c @var{var}=@var{value}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15423
msgid ""
"Set the customization variable @var{var} to @var{value}.  The @code{=} is "
"optional, but both @var{var} and @var{value} must be quoted to the shell as "
"necessary so the result is a single word.  Many aspects of "
"@command{texi2any} behavior and output may be controlled by customization "
"variables, beyond what can be set in the document by @@-commands and with "
"other command line switches.  @xref{Customization Variables}."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15424 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15426
#, no-wrap
msgid "--split=@var{how}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15425 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15427
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-split"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15428
#, no-wrap
msgid "Splitting of output files"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15429
#, no-wrap
msgid "Output file splitting"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15436
msgid "Splitting Output"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15436
msgid ""
"When generating Info, by default large output files are split into smaller "
"subfiles, of approximately 300k bytes.  When generating HTML, by default "
"each output file contains one node (@pxref{Generating HTML}).  @option{--no-"
"split} suppresses this splitting of the output."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15441
msgid ""
"Alternatively, @option{--split=@var{how}} may be used to specify at which "
"level the HTML output should be split.  The possible values for @var{how} "
"are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15446
msgid ""
"The output is split at @code{@@chapter} and other sectioning @@-commands at "
"this level (@code{@@appendix}, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15449
msgid "The output is split at @code{@@section} and similar."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15452
msgid "The output is split at every node.  This is the default."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15457
msgid ""
"Plain text output can be split similarly to HTML@.  This may be useful for "
"extracting sections from a Texinfo document and making them available as "
"separate files."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15458 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15459
#, no-wrap
msgid "--split-size=@var{num}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15464
msgid ""
"Keep Info files to at most @var{num} characters if possible; default is "
"300,000.  (However, a single node will never be split across Info files.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15465 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15466
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15847
#, no-wrap
msgid "--trace-includes"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15473
msgid ""
"Print the name of each included file to standard output, including any "
"indirectly included files.  An include file is printed only if it was "
"actually found.  When this option is given, @command{texi2any} does not "
"output in any output format.  (The purpose of this option is to make it "
"easier to collect the sources of a Texinfo manual.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15474 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15475
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15850
#, no-wrap
msgid "--transliterate-file-names"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15481
msgid ""
"Enable transliteration of non-ASCII characters in node and sectioning "
"commands names for the purpose of file name and sectioning commands "
"identifiers creation.  The file names and identifiers obtained that way are "
"platform and processor dependent.  @xref{HTML Xref 8-bit Character "
"Expansion}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15487
msgid ""
"Redirection files for anchors and nodes are not affected, therefore if "
"@option{--node-files} is enabled, files with non-translitered names are "
"created too.  It is recommended to have non-translitered file names created "
"for nodes such that cross-references to the generated manual succeed.  "
"@xref{@option{--node-files}}. @xref{HTML Xref Configuration}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15488
#, no-wrap
msgid "-U @var{var}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15491
msgid ""
"Cause @var{var} to be undefined.  This is equivalent to @code{@@clear "
"@var{var}} in the Texinfo file (@pxref{@code{@@set @@clear @@value}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15492 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15493
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15853
#, no-wrap
msgid "--verbose"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15498
msgid ""
"Cause @command{texi2any} to display messages saying what it is doing.  "
"Normally, @command{texi2any} only outputs messages if there are errors or "
"warnings."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15499 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17283
#, no-wrap
msgid "--version"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15500 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15502
#, no-wrap
msgid "-V"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15501
#, no-wrap
msgid "--version@r{, for @command{texi2any}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15504
msgid "Print the version number, then exit successfully."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15505 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15506
#, no-wrap
msgid "--Xopt @var{str}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15509
msgid ""
"Pass @var{str} (a single shell word) to @command{texi2dvi}; may be repeated "
"(@pxref{@command{texi2any} Printed Output})."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15510 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15511
#, no-wrap
msgid "--xml"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15513
msgid "Generate Texinfo XML output (rather than Info)."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15517
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{texi2any} Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15519
msgid "@nodedescription Control over output format and XS use."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15519
#, no-wrap
msgid "Environment Variables Recognized by @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15521
#, no-wrap
msgid "Environment variable @code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15525
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} also reads the environment variable "
"@env{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} to determine the output format, if not "
"overridden by a command line option.  The value should be one of:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15528
#, no-wrap
msgid "docbook  dvi  dvipdf  epub3  html  info  latex  pdf  plaintext  ps  xml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15531
msgid "If not set or otherwise specified, Info output is the default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15535
msgid ""
"@code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} may take some other special values, which do "
"not correspond to any command-line settable output format (@pxref{Output "
"Format Selection})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15539
msgid ""
"The customization variable of the same name is also read; if set, that "
"overrides an environment variable setting, but not a command-line option.  "
"@xref{Output Format Selection}."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15540
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXINFO_XS"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15541
#, no-wrap
msgid "Perl extension modules (XS)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15551
msgid ""
"You can control the Perl @command{texi2any} implementation's use of Perl "
"extension modules by setting the @env{TEXINFO_XS} environment variable.  "
"These modules are compiled native code that the interpreted Perl code can "
"use.  Ideally, these extension modules should just work, and the only "
"noticeable difference they should make is that @command{texi2any} finishes "
"running sooner.  However, you can use this environment variable for the "
"purposes of troubleshooting: for example, if you have problems with the "
"output of @command{texi2any} varying depending on whether the extension "
"modules are in use."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15554
msgid ""
"The following values of @env{TEXINFO_XS} are recognized by "
"@command{texi2any}:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15556
#, no-wrap
msgid "default"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15559
msgid ""
"The default behavior.  Try to load extension modules, and silently fall back "
"to the interpreted Perl implementations if this fails."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15560
#, no-wrap
msgid "warn"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15563
msgid ""
"Try to load extension modules, and if this fails, give a warning message "
"before falling back to the interpreted Perl implementations."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15564
#, no-wrap
msgid "required"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15567
msgid ""
"Try to load extension modules, and if this fails, give a message and abort."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15568
#, no-wrap
msgid "debug"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15570
msgid "Try to load extension modules, printing many messages while doing so."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15571
#, no-wrap
msgid "omit"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15573
msgid "Do not use extension modules."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15581
msgid ""
"You can disable the use of the native code implementation in the Perl "
"@command{texi2any} implementation for the main processing steps more "
"finely.  If native code modules are not used for a step, they cannot be used "
"for the following steps.  Three steps are distinguished, each associated "
"with an environment variable:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15583
#, no-wrap
msgid "parsing"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15584
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXINFO_XS_PARSER"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15588
msgid ""
"Corresponds to the conversion of Texinfo input into an internal tree format "
"used for further processing.  Set @env{TEXINFO_XS_PARSER} to @samp{0} to "
"disable the use of the native code implementation of the parser module."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15588 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15908
#, no-wrap
msgid "structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15589
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXINFO_XS_STRUCTURE"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15593
msgid ""
"Corresponds to the determination of sectioning and node structures.  Set "
"@env{TEXINFO_XS_STRUCTURE} to @samp{0} to disable the use of the native code "
"implementation of Perl modules in that step."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15593
#, no-wrap
msgid "conversion"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15594
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXINFO_XS_CONVERT"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15598
msgid ""
"Set @env{TEXINFO_XS_CONVERT} to @samp{0} to disable the use of the native "
"code for conversion of the tree to output format.  Note that many output "
"formats do not have a native code implementation for this step."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15603
msgid ""
"This may be useful for working around bugs or incompatibilities between the "
"native code implementation and the implementation in pure Perl code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15611
msgid ""
"The C @command{texi2any} implementation uses only native code for the "
"@emph{parsing} and @emph{structure} steps.  For the @emph{conversion} step, "
"native code is used if possible.  If Perl code is called, the program always "
"try to load available Perl extension modules.  Failing to load an extension "
"is reported and the program aborts.  Setting @env{TEXINFO_XS} to "
"@code{debug} may still be useful to get more information.  Setting "
"@env{TEXINFO_XS} to @code{omit} with the C @command{texi2any} implementation "
"is an error."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15612
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXINFO_C_EMBED_PERL"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15613
#, no-wrap
msgid "Embedded Perl in C @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15619
msgid ""
"You can control the C @command{texi2any} implementation's use of embedded "
"Perl, by setting the @env{TEXINFO_C_EMBED_PERL} environment variable to "
"@samp{0} to disable the use of embedded Perl.  Set with care, as HTML "
"customization initialization files, conversion to most output formats and "
"optimal index sorting require Perl."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15621 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15623
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{texi2any} Printed Output"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15623
msgid "@nodedescription Calling @command{texi2dvi}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15625
#, no-wrap
msgid "Printed output, through @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15626
#, no-wrap
msgid "Output, printed through @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15637
msgid ""
"To justify the name Texinfo-to-@emph{any}, @command{texi2any} has basic "
"support for creating printed output in the various formats: @TeX{} DVI, PDF, "
"and PostScript.  This is done via the simple method of executing the "
"@command{texi2dvi} program when those output formats are requested, after "
"checking the validity of the input to give users the benefit of "
"@command{texi2any}'s error checking.  If you don't want such error checking, "
"perhaps because your manual plays advanced @TeX{} tricks together with "
"@file{texinfo.tex}, just invoke @command{texi2dvi} directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15645
msgid ""
"The output format options for this are @option{--dvi}, @option{--dvipdf}, "
"@option{--pdf}, and @option{--ps}.  @xref{Format with @command{texi2dvi}}, "
"for more details on these options and general @command{texi2dvi} operation.  "
"In addition, the @option{--verbose}, @option{--silent}, and @option{--quiet} "
"options are passed on if specified; the @option{-I} and @option{-o} options "
"are likewise passed on with their arguments, and @option{--debug} without "
"its argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15651
msgid ""
"The only option remaining that is related to the @command{texi2dvi} "
"invocation is @option{--Xopt}.  Here, just the argument is passed on and "
"multiple @option{--Xopt} options accumulate.  This provides a way to "
"construct an arbitrary command line for @command{texi2dvi}.  For example, "
"running"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15654
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2any --Xopt -t --Xopt @@afourpaper --pdf foo.texi\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15658
msgid "is equivalent to running"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15661
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2dvi -t @@afourpaper --pdf foo.texi\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15665
msgid "except for the validity check."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15671
msgid ""
"Although one might wish that other options to @command{texi2any} would take "
"effect, they don't.  For example, running @samp{texi2any --no-number-"
"sections --dvi foo.texi} still results in a DVI file with numbered "
"sections.  (Perhaps this could be improved in the future, if requests are "
"received.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15675
msgid ""
"The actual name of the command that is invoked is specified by the "
"@code{TEXI2DVI} customization variable (@pxref{Customization Variables for "
"Multiple Formats}).  As you might guess, the default is @samp{texi2dvi}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15678
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} itself does not generate any normal output when it "
"invokes @command{texi2dvi}, only diagnostic messages."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15680 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15682
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15682
msgid "@nodedescription Configuring @command{texi2any}."
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15684 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17895
#, no-wrap
msgid "Warning"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15688
msgid ""
"These customization variable names and meanings may change in any Texinfo "
"release.  We always try to avoid incompatible changes, but we cannot "
"absolutely promise, since needs change over time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15693
msgid ""
"Many aspects of the behavior and output of @command{texi2any} may be "
"modified by modifying so-called @dfn{customization variables}.  These fall "
"into a few general categories:"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15698
msgid ""
"Those associated with @@-commands; for example, @code{@@documentlanguage}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15705
msgid ""
"Those associated with command-line options; for example, the customization "
"variable @code{SPLIT} is associated with the @option{--split} command-line "
"option. @code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} is set based on output format command "
"line options and allows specifying the output format."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15709
msgid ""
"Those affecting the global behavior of @command{texi2any}, in particular "
"Texinfo code parsing."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15714
msgid ""
"Those associated with particular output formats.  (Variables only relevant "
"for HTML output are documented in @ref{HTML Output Customization}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15717
msgid "Those relevant for multiple output formats."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15725
msgid ""
"You may set customization variables on the command line using @code{--set-"
"customization-variable '@var{var} @var{value}'} (quoting the variable/value "
"pair to the shell) or @code{--set-customization-variable @var{var}"
"=@var{value}} (using @code{=}).  A special @var{value} is @samp{undef}, "
"which sets the variable to this special ``undefined'' Perl value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15727
msgid "The sections below give the details for each of these."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15737
msgid "Commands: Customization Variables for @@-Commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15737
msgid "Options: Customization Variables and Options."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15737
msgid "Format: Output Format Selection."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15737
msgid "Global: Global Customization Variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15737
msgid "Info: Info and Plaintext Customization Variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15737
msgid "LaTeX: @LaTeX{} Customization Variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15737
msgid "Other: Other Formats Customization Variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15737
msgid "Formats: Customization Variables for Multiple Formats"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15740 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15741
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customization Variables for @@-Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15743
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customization variables for @@-commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15744
#, no-wrap
msgid "@sortas{at} @@-commands @subentry customization variables for"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15748
msgid ""
"Each of the following @@-commands has an associated customization variable "
"with the same name (minus the leading @code{@@}):"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15765
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@afivepaper            @@afourpaper        @@afourlatex\n"
"@@afourwide             @@allowcodebreaks   @@bsixpaper\n"
"@@contents              @@codequotebacktick\n"
"@@codequoteundirected   @@deftypefnnewline  @@documentdescription\n"
"@@documentencoding      @@documentlanguage  @@evenfooting\n"
"@@evenfootingmarks      @@evenheading       @@evenheadingmarks\n"
"@@everyfooting          @@everyfootingmarks @@everyheading\n"
"@@everyheadingmarks     @@exampleindent     @@firstparagraphindent\n"
"@@fonttextsize          @@footnotestyle     @@frenchspacing\n"
"@@headings              @@kbdinputstyle     @@microtype\n"
"@@novalidate            @@oddfooting        @@oddfootingmarks\n"
"@@oddheading            @@oddheadingmarks   @@pagesizes\n"
"@@paragraphindent       @@setfilename       @@setchapternewpage\n"
"@@shortcontents         @@smallbook         @@summarycontents\n"
"@@urefbreakstyle        @@xrefautomaticsectiontitle\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15773
msgid ""
"Setting such a customization variable to a value @samp{foo} is similar to "
"executing @code{@@@var{cmd} foo}.  It is not exactly the same, though, since "
"any side effects of parsing the Texinfo source are not redone.  Also, some "
"variables do not take Texinfo code when generating particular formats, but "
"an argument that is already formatted.  This is the case, for example, for "
"HTML for @code{documentdescription}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15777
msgid ""
"Note that if @command{texi2any} is invoked to process the file with @TeX{} "
"(e.g., with the @option{--pdf} option), then these customization variables "
"may not be passed on to @TeX{}."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
