#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15858
msgid ""
"Setting such a customization variable to a value @samp{foo} is essentially "
"the same as specifying the @code{--@var{opt}=foo} if the option takes an "
"argument, or @code{--@var{opt}} if not."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15860 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15861
#, no-wrap
msgid "Output Format Selection"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15868
msgid ""
"The customization variable @code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} takes the value of "
"the format output by @command{texi2any}.  This can be one of the usual "
"output formats that can be specified with options, or various other special "
"output formats:"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15871
#, no-wrap
msgid "dvi"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15872
#, no-wrap
msgid "dvipdf"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15873
#, no-wrap
msgid "epub3"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15875
#, no-wrap
msgid "info"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15876
#, no-wrap
msgid "pdf"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15877
#, no-wrap
msgid "plaintext"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15878
#, no-wrap
msgid "ps"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15886
msgid ""
"These correspond to the command-line options (and "
"@code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} environment variable values) of the same name.  "
"The @code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} customization variable value is set when "
"command-line options (or @code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} environment variable "
"values) set the output format.  @xref{Invoking @command{texi2any}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15887
#, no-wrap
msgid "tree representation, for debugging"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15888
#, no-wrap
msgid "debugging document, with tree representation"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15889
#, no-wrap
msgid "debugtree"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15892
msgid ""
"Instead of generating a regular output format, output a text representation "
"of the tree obtained by parsing the input texinfo document."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15893
#, no-wrap
msgid "parse"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15895
msgid "Do only Texinfo source parsing; there is no output."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15896
#, no-wrap
msgid "plaintexinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15901
msgid ""
"Output the Texinfo source with all the macros, @code{@@include} and "
"@code{@@value@{@}} expanded.  This is similar to setting @option{--macro-"
"expand}, but instead of being output in addition to the normal conversion, "
"output of Texinfo is the main output."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15902
#, no-wrap
msgid "raw text output"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15903
#, no-wrap
msgid "rawtext"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15907
msgid ""
"Output raw text, with minimal formatting.  For example, footnotes are "
"ignored and there is no paragraph filling.  This is used by the parser for "
"file names and copyright text in HTML comments, for example."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15911
msgid ""
"Do only Texinfo source parsing and determination of the document structure; "
"there is no output."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15912
#, no-wrap
msgid "SXML output"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15913
#, no-wrap
msgid "S-expressions, output format"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15914
#, no-wrap
msgid "texinfosxml"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15917
msgid ""
"Output the document in TexinfoSXML representation, a syntax for writing XML "
"data using Lisp S-expressions."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15918
#, no-wrap
msgid "spell checking"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15919
#, no-wrap
msgid "word counting"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15920
#, no-wrap
msgid "detexinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15921
#, no-wrap
msgid "stripping Texinfo commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15922
#, no-wrap
msgid "textcontent"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15927
msgid ""
"Output the text content only, stripped of commands; this is useful for spell "
"checking or word counting, for example.  The trivial @code{detexinfo} script "
"setting this is in the @file{util} directory of the Texinfo source as an "
"example.  It's one line:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15930
#, no-wrap
msgid "exec texi2any -c TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT=textcontent \"$@@\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15934 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15935
#, no-wrap
msgid "Global Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15939
msgid ""
"This table gives the customization variables which affect the global "
"behavior of @command{texi2any}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15941
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHECK_MISSING_MENU_ENTRY"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15945
msgid ""
"When a @code{@@menu} block occurs in a node, check if there is a menu entry "
"for all subordinate nodes in the document sectioning structure.  On by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15946
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHECK_NORMAL_MENU_STRUCTURE"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15951
msgid ""
"Warn if the node pointers (either explicitly or automatically set)  are not "
"consistent with the order of node menu entries.  This is a more thorough "
"structure check than that provided by @code{CHECK_MISSING_MENU_ENTRY}.  On "
"by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15952
#, no-wrap
msgid "COLLATION_LANGUAGE"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15958
msgid ""
"By default, @command{texi2any} sorts document indices according to the "
"@dfn{Unicode Collation Algorithm} (defined in @uref{http://www.unicode.org/"
"reports/tr10/, Unicode Technical Standard #10}), without language-specific "
"collation tailoring.  If set, use the language for linguistic tailoring of "
"index sorting."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15962
msgid ""
"Currently, @command{texi2any} gives no warning if there is no support for "
"linguistic tailoring due to either missing software or missing support for "
"the specified language."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15966
msgid ""
"In Perl, the @code{Unicode::Collate::Locale} module is used for linguistic "
"tailoring; therefore if this module is not installed, the variable will be "
"silently ignored."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15969
msgid ""
"If @code{USE_UNICODE_COLLATION} is set to @samp{0}, there is no Unicode "
"collation and so no linguistic tailoring either."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15971
msgid ""
"See also the @code{DOCUMENTLANGUAGE_COLLATION} variable, described below."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15972
#, no-wrap
msgid "COMMAND_LINE_ENCODING"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15976
msgid ""
"Encoding used to decode and encode command-line arguments.  Default is based "
"on the locale encoding.  This may affect file names inserted into output "
"files or error messages printed by the program."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15979
msgid ""
"Note that some file and directory names from the command line may not be "
"decoded immediately, and may not be decoded at all."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15983
msgid ""
"It is also used to encode command-line argument passed to commands called "
"from @command{texi2any}.  For example, @command{latex2html} will be called "
"from @command{texi2any} if @code{HTML_MATH} is set to @samp{l2h}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15984
#, no-wrap
msgid "CPP_LINE_DIRECTIVES"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15987
msgid ""
"Recognize @code{#line} directives in a ``preprocessing'' pass "
"(@pxref{External Macro Processors}); on by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15988
#, no-wrap
msgid "DEBUG"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15993
msgid "If set, debugging output is generated; default is off (zero)."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:15994
#, no-wrap
msgid "DOC_ENCODING_FOR_INPUT_FILE_NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16000
msgid ""
"If set, use the input Texinfo document encoding information for the encoding "
"of input file names, such as file names specified as @code{@@include} or "
"@code{@@verbatiminclude} arguments.  If unset, use the locale encoding "
"instead.  Default is set, except on MS-Windows where the locale encoding is "
"used by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16004
msgid ""
"Note that this is for file names only; the default encoding or "
"@code{@@documentencoding} is always used for the encoding of file content "
"(@pxref{@code{@@documentencoding}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16006
msgid "The @code{INPUT_FILE_NAME_ENCODING} variable overrides this variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16007
#, no-wrap
msgid "DOC_ENCODING_FOR_OUTPUT_FILE_NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16012
msgid ""
"If set, use the input Texinfo document encoding information for the encoding "
"of output file names, such as files specified with @option{--output}.  If "
"unset, use the locale encoding instead.  Default is unset, so files names "
"are encoded using the current locale."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16015
msgid ""
"Note that this is for file names only; @code{OUTPUT_ENCODING_NAME} is used "
"for the encoding of file content."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16017
msgid "The @code{OUTPUT_FILE_NAME_ENCODING} variable overrides this variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16018
#, no-wrap
msgid "DOCUMENTLANGUAGE_COLLATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16023
msgid ""
"If set, try to use the language specified in a @code{@@documentlanguage} "
"directive for language-specific tailoring of index sorting.  See also the "
"@code{COLLATION_LANGUAGE} variable, described above.  "
"(@xref{@code{@@documentlanguage}}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16024
#, no-wrap
msgid "DUMP_STRUCTURE"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16028
msgid ""
"For debugging.  If set, the tree constructed upon parsing a Texinfo document "
"and determining the document structure is output to the file; if set to "
"@samp{-} output to standard error.  Default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16029
#, no-wrap
msgid "DUMP_TEXI"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16033
msgid ""
"For debugging.  If set, no conversion is done, only parsing and macro "
"expansion.  If the option @option{--macro-expand} is set, the Texinfo source "
"is also expanded to the corresponding file.  Default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16034
#, no-wrap
msgid "DUMP_TREE"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16041
msgid ""
"For debugging.  If set, the tree constructed upon parsing a Texinfo document "
"is output to the file; if set to @samp{-} output to standard error.  For "
"backward compatibility, for one release, also output to standard error if "
"set to @samp{1}.  Default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16042
#, no-wrap
msgid "FORMAT_MENU"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16050
msgid ""
"If set to @samp{menu}, output Texinfo menus.  This is the default for Info.  "
"@samp{sectiontoc} is the default setting for HTML, where instead of the "
"contents of @code{@@menu} blocks being output, a list of subordinate "
"sections is output in each node.  Set to @samp{menu_no_detailmenu} instead "
"of @samp{menu} in HTML if you want menus but no automatically generated "
"@code{@@detailmenu} in the Top node master menu.  If set to @samp{nomenu}, "
"do not output menus."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16053
msgid ""
"This variable is set to @samp{nomenu} when generating DocBook, or when "
"@option{--no-headers} is specified."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16056
#, no-wrap
msgid "HANDLER_FATAL_ERROR_LEVEL"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16063
#, no-wrap
msgid "IGNORE_SPACE_AFTER_BRACED_COMMAND_NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16066
msgid ""
"If set, spaces are ignored after an @@-command that takes braces.  Default "
"true, matching the @TeX{} behavior."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16067
#, no-wrap
msgid "Encoding @subentry input file names"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16068
#, no-wrap
msgid "INPUT_FILE_NAME_ENCODING"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16075
msgid ""
"Encoding used for input file names.  This variable overrides any encoding "
"from the document or current locale.  Normally, you do not need to set this "
"variable, but it can be used if file names are in a certain character "
"encoding on a filesystem.  An alternative is to set "
"@code{DOC_ENCODING_FOR_INPUT_FILE_NAME} to @samp{0} to use the locale "
"encoding.  See also @code{OUTPUT_FILE_NAME_ENCODING}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16076
#, no-wrap
msgid "LOCALE_ENCODING"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16079
msgid ""
"Locale encoding obtained from the system.  You should not need to explicitly "
"set this variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16080
#, no-wrap
msgid "MAX_MACRO_CALL_NESTING"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16084
msgid ""
"The maximal number of recursive calls of @@-commands defined through "
"@code{@@rmacro}; default 100000.  The purpose of this variable is to avoid "
"infinite recursions."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16085
#, no-wrap
msgid "MESSAGE_ENCODING"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16088
msgid ""
"Encoding used to encode messages output by @command{texi2any}.  Default is "
"based on the locale encoding."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16089
#, no-wrap
msgid "NO_INDEX"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16093
msgid ""
"If set, index entries are not recorded and @@-commands related to indices, "
"such as @code{@@printindex}, @code{@@synindex} or @code{@@defindex} have no "
"effect.  Default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16094
#, no-wrap
msgid "NO_USER_COMMANDS"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16098
msgid ""
"If set, definitions of user-defined @@-command are ignored.  @code{@@alias}, "
"@code{@@definfoenclose}, @code{@@defindex}, @code{@@macro} and similar @@-"
"commands have no effect.  Default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16099
#, no-wrap
msgid "OUTPUT_ENCODING_NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16106
msgid ""
"Normalized encoding name used for output files.  Should be a usable charset "
"name in HTML, typically one of the preferred IANA encoding names.  By "
"default, if an input encoding is set (typically through "
"@code{@@documentencoding}), this information is used to set the output "
"encoding name, otherwise the output encoding is based on the default "
"encoding.  @xref{@code{@@documentencoding}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16107
#, no-wrap
msgid "Encoding @subentry output file names"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16108
#, no-wrap
msgid "OUTPUT_FILE_NAME_ENCODING"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16111
msgid ""
"Encoding used for output file names.  This variable overrides any encoding "
"from the document or current locale."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16115
msgid ""
"Normally, you do not need to set this variable, but it can be used if file "
"names should be created in a certain character encoding on a filesystem.  "
"See also @code{INPUT_FILE_NAME_ENCODING}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16116
#, no-wrap
msgid "PACKAGE"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16117
#, no-wrap
msgid "PACKAGE_VERSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16118
#, no-wrap
msgid "PACKAGE_AND_VERSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16119
#, no-wrap
msgid "PACKAGE_URL"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16120
#, no-wrap
msgid "PACKAGE_NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16125
msgid ""
"The implementation's short package name, package version, package name and "
"version concatenated, package URL@:, and full package name, respectively.  "
"By default, these variables are all set through Autoconf, Automake, and "
"@code{configure}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16126
#, no-wrap
msgid "PREFIX"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16132
msgid ""
"The output file prefix, which is prepended to some output file names.  By "
"default it is set by @code{@@setfilename} or from the input file "
"(@pxref{Setting the Output File Name}).  How this value is used depends on "
"the value of other customization variables or command line options, such as "
"whether the output is split.  The default is unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16133
#, no-wrap
msgid "PROGRAM"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16136
msgid ""
"Name of the program used.  By default, it is set to the name of the program "
"launched, with a trailing @samp{.pl} removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16137 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:21625
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi-elements-by-size"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16138
#, no-wrap
msgid "Longest nodes, finding"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16139
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sorting nodes by size"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16140
#, no-wrap
msgid "SORT_ELEMENT_COUNT"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16147
msgid ""
"If set, the name of a file to which a list of elements (nodes or sections, "
"depending on the output format) is dumped, sorted by the number of lines "
"they contain after removal of @@-commands; default unset.  This is used by "
"the program @code{texi-elements-by-size} in the @file{util/} directory of "
"the Texinfo source distribution (@pxref{texi-elements-by-size})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16148
#, no-wrap
msgid "SORT_ELEMENT_COUNT_WORDS"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16151
msgid ""
"When dumping the elements-by-size file (see preceding item), use word counts "
"instead of line counts; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16152
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEST"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16162
msgid ""
"If set to a positive integer, some variables which are normally dynamically "
"generated anew for each run (date, program name, version) are set to fixed "
"and given values.  Some file names may also have the directory part "
"removed.  Also code that gives more reproducible output may be selected.  "
"This is useful to compare the output to a reference file, as is done for the "
"tests.  Features not selected in the default case but interesting for tests "
"are also enabled.  For example, code related to memory release and checks on "
"released memory.  If the value is higher, more checks are enabled, which may "
"require additional Perl modules installation.  The default is undef."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16163
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16168
msgid ""
"The generated output format.  Set from command line with options such as "
"@option{--html}, as the @env{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} environment variable "
"value (@pxref{@command{texi2any} Environment Variables}) or as a "
"customization option.  @xref{Output Format Selection}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16176
msgid ""
"The value set in the @code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} variable is in general the "
"same as the name used to set the format, but not always.  If the format is "
"set to @code{xml}, with @option{--xml}, with the @env{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} "
"environment variable or with a customization variable the "
"@code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} customization variable is set to a more "
"specific output format name @code{texinfoxml}.  That kind of difference in "
"naming should not have any user-visible consequence."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16177
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREE_TRANSFORMATIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16182
msgid ""
"The associated value is a comma separated list of transformations that can "
"be applied to the Texinfo tree prior to outputting the result.  If more than "
"one is specified, the ordering is irrelevant; each is always applied at the "
"necessary point during processing."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16187
msgid ""
"By default, the tree transformations @samp{move_index_entries_after_items} "
"and @samp{relate_index_entries_to_table_entries} are executed for HTML and "
"DocBook output.  Here's an example of updating the master menu in a document:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16194
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"texi2any \\\n"
"  -c TREE_TRANSFORMATIONS=regenerate_master_menu \\\n"
"  -c TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT=plaintexinfo \\\n"
"  mydoc.texi \\\n"
"  -o /tmp/out\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16201
msgid ""
"(Caveat: Since @samp{plaintexinfo} output expands Texinfo macros and "
"conditionals, it's necessary to remove any such differences before "
"installing the updates in the original document. This may be remedied in a "
"future release)."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16205
msgid ""
"The following transformations are currently supported (many are used in the "
"@code{pod2texi} utility distributed with Texinfo; @pxref{Invoking "
"@command{pod2texi}}):"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16207
#, no-wrap
msgid "complete_tree_nodes_menus"
msgstr ""

#. type: ftable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16210
msgid ""
"Add menu entries or whole menus for nodes associated with sections of any "
"level, based on the sectioning tree."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16211
#, no-wrap
msgid "complete_tree_nodes_missing_menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: ftable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16214
msgid ""
"Add whole menus for nodes associated with sections without menu.  The menus "
"are based on the sectioning tree."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16215
#, no-wrap
msgid "fill_gaps_in_sectioning"
msgstr ""

#. type: ftable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16219
msgid ""
"Adds empty @code{@@unnumbered...} sections in a tree to fill gaps in "
"sectioning.  For example, an @code{@@unnumberedsec} will be inserted if a "
"@code{@@chapter} is followed by a @code{@@subsection}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16220
#, no-wrap
msgid "insert_nodes_for_sectioning_commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: ftable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16222
msgid "Insert nodes for sectioning commands lacking a corresponding node."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16223
#, no-wrap
msgid "move_index_entries_after_items"
msgstr ""

#. type: ftable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16228
msgid ""
"In @code{@@enumerate} and @code{@@itemize}, move index entries appearing "
"just before an @code{@@item} to just after the @code{@@item}.  Comment lines "
"between index entries are moved too.  As mentioned, this is always done for "
"HTML and DocBook output."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16229
#, no-wrap
msgid "regenerate_master_menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: ftable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16233
msgid ""
"Update the Top node master menu, either replacing the (first)  "
"@code{@@detailmenu} in the Top node menu, or creating it at the end of the "
"Top node menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16234
#, no-wrap
msgid "relate_index_entries_to_table_entries"
msgstr ""

#. type: ftable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16239
msgid ""
"In @code{@@table}, @code{@@vtable} and @code{@@ftable}, reassociate the "
"index entry information from an index @@-command appearing right after an "
"@code{@@item} line with the first element of the @code{@@item}.  Remove the "
"index @@-command from the tree."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16242
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_SETFILENAME_EXTENSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16246
msgid ""
"Default is on for Info, off for other output.  If set, use exactly what "
"@code{@@setfilename} gives for the output file name, including the "
"extension.  You should not need to explicitly set this variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16247
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unicode::Collate"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16248
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_UNICODE_COLLATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16257
msgid ""
"By default, @command{texi2any} sorts document indices according to the "
"@dfn{Unicode Collation Algorithm} (defined in @uref{http://www.unicode.org/"
"reports/tr10/, Unicode Technical Standard #10}), which performs a @dfn{multi-"
"level} ordering of strings containing Unicode code points.  (To do this, the "
"program uses the @code{Unicode::Collate} module, a standard part of Perl "
"installations.)  However, the use of this algorithm incurs noticeably longer "
"run times when processing manuals with large indices."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16259
msgid ""
"Set this variable to @samp{0} to use a simpler, faster sorting algorithm."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16264
msgid ""
"You may find this useful for speeding up @command{texi2any} if you don't "
"have many non-ASCII characters in index entry text, or if you don't care "
"about having the indices sorted correctly, especially when working on the "
"draft of a manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16266
#, no-wrap
msgid "Text::Unidecode"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16267
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_UNIDECODE"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16270
msgid ""
"If set to false, do not use the @code{Text::Unidecode} Perl module to "
"transliterate more characters from Perl code; default true."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16274 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16275
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info and Plaintext Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16279
msgid ""
"This table gives the customization variables which apply to Info and "
"Plaintext formats only."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16281
#, no-wrap
msgid "ASCII_DASHES_AND_QUOTES"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16287
msgid ""
"For Info output, when set, use plain ASCII characters to represent quotation "
"marks, hyphens and dashes when these are given in the Texinfo source as "
"@samp{-}, @samp{--}, @samp{---}, @samp{`}, @samp{``}, @samp{'}, and "
"@samp{''}, rather than UTF-8 directional quotation marks, en dashes, vel "
"sim.  On by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16288
#, no-wrap
msgid "ASCII_GLYPH"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16293
msgid ""
"For Info output, use ASCII output for glyph commands such as the copyright "
"sign (@command{@@copyright@{@}}, becoming @samp{(C)}), and the bullet symbol "
"(@command{@@bullet@{@}}, becoming @samp{*}), rather than other Unicode "
"sequences.  Off by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16294
#, no-wrap
msgid "ASCII_PUNCTUATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16299
msgid ""
"Avoid any unnecessary or gratuitous non-ASCII, UTF-8 sequences in the "
"output.  Implies both @code{ASCII_DASHES_AND_QUOTES} and @code{ASCII_GLYPH} "
"and additionally affects the output of commands such as @code{@@samp} which "
"output quotation marks."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16300
#, no-wrap
msgid "AUTO_MENU_DESCRIPTION_ALIGN_COLUMN"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16305
msgid ""
"For Info output, column at which to start a menu entry description provided "
"by @code{@@nodedescription} or @code{@@nodedescriptionblock}.  Undefined by "
"default, in which case 45% of the fill column value is used (@pxref{Invoking "
"@command{texi2any}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16306
#, no-wrap
msgid "AUTO_MENU_MAX_WIDTH"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16311
msgid ""
"Maximum number of columns in a menu entry line in Info when adding a "
"description from @code{@@nodedescription} or @code{@@nodedescriptionblock}.  "
"Undefined by default, in which case 10% more than the fill column value is "
"used (@pxref{Invoking @command{texi2any}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16312
#, no-wrap
msgid "CLOSE_DOUBLE_QUOTE_SYMBOL"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16317
msgid ""
"When a closing double quote is needed, for @samp{@@dfn} in Info, use this "
"character.  The default for Info is set the same as for "
"@code{OPEN_DOUBLE_QUOTE_SYMBOL}, except that the Unicode code is a closing "
"double quote (see below)."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16318
#, no-wrap
msgid "INDEX_SPECIAL_CHARS_WARNING"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16323
msgid ""
"If set, warn about @samp{:} in index entry, as not all Info readers may be "
"able to process these.  For Info and plaintext only.  Default false, because "
"parsing problems there don't prevent navigation; readers can still "
"relatively easily find their way to the node in question."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16324
#, no-wrap
msgid "INFO_MATH_IMAGES"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16331
msgid ""
"(Experimental.)  If set, convert the contents of @code{@@math} and "
"@code{@@displaymath} into images, and reference these in the produced Info "
"file.  This variable requires a working @TeX{} installation, the "
"@samp{preview} package of @LaTeX{}, as well as the @command{dvipng} "
"program.  It may be suitable for math-heavy documents that are unlikely to "
"be viewed in a text terminal."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16339
msgid ""
"This feature is marked as experimental as it would require extra support in "
"Info-viewing programs (currently, only the Info mode of Emacs) to view the "
"images correctly.  The images should be visible with existing versions of "
"Emacs, but they may be the wrong size or appear misaligned with surrounding "
"text.  It is possible that we will change the output for this option given "
"further feedback.  @xref{Info Format Image} for more details about how "
"images are currently output with this option."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16340
#, no-wrap
msgid "INFO_SPECIAL_CHARS_QUOTE"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16346
msgid ""
"If set, whenever there are problematic characters for Info output in places "
"such as node names or menu items, surround the part of the construct where "
"they appear with quoting characters, as described in @ref{Info Format "
"Specification}.  Default is set for Info and unset for plaintext.  "
"@xref{Node Line Requirements}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16347
#, no-wrap
msgid "INFO_SPECIAL_CHARS_WARNING"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16353
msgid ""
"If set, warn about problematic constructs for Info output (such as the "
"string @samp{::}) in node names, menu items, and cross-references.  If not "
"defined, set unless @code{INFO_SPECIAL_CHARS_QUOTE} is set.  Default is set "
"for Info and not defined for plaintext. Similar warnings in index entries "
"are covered by @code{INDEX_SPECIAL_CHARS_WARNING}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16354
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPEN_DOUBLE_QUOTE_SYMBOL"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16359
msgid ""
"When an opening double quote is needed, for @samp{@@dfn} output in Info, use "
"the specified character.  If @option{--disable-encoding} is set or the "
"document encoding is not UTF-8, @samp{\"} is used.  Otherwise, the Info "
"output uses a Unicode left double quote."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16363 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16364
#, no-wrap
msgid "@LaTeX{} Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16367
#, no-wrap
msgid "warning"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16370
msgid ""
"@LaTeX{} output customization is experimental.  Nothing is decided, "
"everything can change, and we would welcome any feedback."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16375
msgid ""
"This table gives the customization variables which apply to @LaTeX{} output "
"only."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16377
#, no-wrap
msgid "CLASS_BEGIN_USEPACKAGE"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16382
msgid ""
"If set, the corresponding text will replace the @LaTeX{} "
"@code{\\documentclass}, package imports that are always output and are "
"output right after @code{\\documentclass}, and package imports that depend "
"on the document encoding setting the input and font encoding "
"(@code{inputenc} and @code{fontenc})."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16384
msgid "The text replaced is along:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16395
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\documentclass@{book@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{amsfonts@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{amsmath@}\n"
"\\usepackage[gen]@{eurosym@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{textcomp@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{graphicx@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{etoolbox@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{titleps@}\n"
"\\usepackage[utf8]@{inputenc@}\n"
"\\usepackage[T1]@{fontenc@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16397
#, no-wrap
msgid "END_USEPACKAGE"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16402
msgid ""
"If set, the corresponding text will replace the package imports that depend "
"on the Texinfo commands used, and the last packages imports that are always "
"output and output after all the other packages imports.  The last package "
"imports corresponds to @samp{\\usepackage[hidelinks]@{hyperref@}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16406
msgid ""
"Here is an example of the corresponding text for a document with indices, "
"@code{@@need}, @code{@@multitable}, definition commands, @code{@@cartouche}, "
"lists, and @code{@@float}:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16417
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\usepackage@{imakeidx@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{needspace@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{array@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{embrac@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{expl3@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{tabularx@}\n"
"\\usepackage[framemethod=tikz]@{mdframed@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{enumitem@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{float@}\n"
"\\usepackage[hidelinks]@{hyperref@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16419
#, no-wrap
msgid "LATEX_FLOATS_FILE_EXTENSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16422
msgid ""
"Set new floats definition file extension for @LaTeX{} output.  Default "
"@samp{tfl}."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16426 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16427
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other Formats Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16431
msgid ""
"This table gives the customization which apply to specific formats only, for "
"formats without separate customization variables description section."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16433
#, no-wrap
msgid "TXI_MARKUP_NO_SECTION_EXTENT"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16436
msgid ""
"For XML@.  Do not include lower level sectioning commands inside upper-level "
"sectioning command markup.  Default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16437
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXI2DVI"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16440
msgid ""
"Name of the command used to produce PostScript, PDF, and DVI; default "
"@samp{texi2dvi}.  @xref{@command{texi2any} Printed Output}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16441
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXTCONTENT_COMMENT"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16445
msgid ""
"For stripped text content output (i.e., when @code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} is "
"set to @code{textcontent}).  If set, also output comments.  Default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16446
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXINFO_DTD_VERSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16449
msgid ""
"For XML@.  Version of the DTD used in the XML output preamble.  The default "
"is set based on a variable in @file{configure.ac}."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16453 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16454
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customization Variables for Multiple Formats"
msgstr ""

#.  old name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16457
msgid "Other Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16459
msgid "This table gives the customization which apply to multiple formats."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16461
#, no-wrap
msgid "CLOSE_QUOTE_SYMBOL"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16468
msgid ""
"When a closing quote is needed, e.g.@: for @code{@@samp} output, use this "
"character; default @code{&#8217;} in DocBook.  Undefined in the default case "
"in HTML and set to @code{&rsquo;} if @code{USE_NUMERIC_ENTITY} is not set, "
"to @code{&#8217;} if set, and to a quote character if "
"@code{OUTPUT_CHARACTERS} is set and the output encoding includes that "
"character."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16471
msgid ""
"The default for Info is set the same as for @code{OPEN_QUOTE_SYMBOL}, except "
"that the Unicode code is a closing quote (see below)."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16472
#, no-wrap
msgid "SystemLiteral"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16473
#, no-wrap
msgid "DOCTYPE"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16479
msgid ""
"For DocBook, HTML, XML@.  Specifies the @code{SystemLiteral}, the entity's "
"system identifier.  This is a URI which may be used to retrieve the entity, "
"and identifies the canonical DTD for the document.  The default value is "
"different for each of HTML, DocBook and XML."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16480
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXTENSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16483
msgid ""
"The extension added to the output file name.  The default is different for "
"each output format."
msgstr ""

#. type: code{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16484 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16491
#, no-wrap
msgid "NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16491
msgid ""
"If set do not output the Top node content.  The Top node is still parsed, "
"but the content is discarded.  Not set in the default case for HTML@.  Set "
"in the default case for EPUB@.  If @code{SHOW_TITLE} is @samp{undef}, "
"setting @code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT} also sets @code{SHOW_TITLE} for HTML."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16497
msgid ""
"Setting @code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT}, which removes the Top node and adds a "
"title page corresponds more to the formatting of a book.  Setting "
"@code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT} to false, with @code{SHOW_TITLE} remaining "
"@samp{undef}, and false, corresponds more to a document setup for browsing, "
"with a direct access to the information at the Top node."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16504
msgid ""
"For DocBook, @code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT} is set to true.  Setting "
"@code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT} to false causes the Top node content to be "
"output.  It is not recommended to output the Top node in DocBook as the "
"title and copying texts are always output.  This option is kept for DocBook "
"for compatibility, as before 2022 the Top node was output in DocBook.  It "
"could be removed in the future."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16505
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPEN_QUOTE_SYMBOL"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16512
msgid ""
"When an opening quote is needed, e.g., for @samp{@@samp} output, use the "
"specified character; default @code{&#8216;} for DocBook.  Undefined in the "
"default case in HTML and set to @code{&lsquo;} if @code{USE_NUMERIC_ENTITY} "
"is not set, to @code{&#8216;} if set, and to a quote character if "
"@code{OUTPUT_CHARACTERS} is set and the output encoding includes that "
"character."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16518
msgid ""
"For Info, the default depends on the enabled document encoding.  If "
"@option{--disable-encoding} is set or the document encoding is not UTF-8, "
"@samp{'} is used.  This character usually appears as an undirected single "
"quote on modern systems.  Otherwise, the Info output uses a Unicode left "
"quote."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16519
#, no-wrap
msgid "OUTPUT_CHARACTERS"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16525
msgid ""
"If not set, the default, output accented and special characters in HTML, XML "
"and DocBook using XML entities, and in @LaTeX{} using macros.  If set, "
"output accented characters in HTML, XML, DocBook and @LaTeX{} output and "
"special characters in HTML and @LaTeX{} output based on the document "
"encoding.  @xref{@code{@@documentencoding}}, and @ref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16527
#, no-wrap
msgid "TOP_NODE_UP"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16534
msgid ""
"Up node for the Top node; default @samp{(dir)}.  This node name is supposed "
"to be already formatted for the output format.  In HTML can be used in "
"attribute, so should not contain any element.  Used for HTML output only if "
"@code{TOP_NODE_UP_URL} is set to override the URL@:, see "
"@code{TOP_NODE_UP_URL} in @ref{HTML Customization Variables List}.  "
"@xref{File Names and Links Customization for HTML}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16535
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_NODES"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16539
msgid ""
"The main unit of output documents is an @dfn{output unit}.  Usually a node "
"is associated with a following sectioning command, while a sectioning "
"command is associated with a previous node; they both together make up the "
"output unit."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16543
msgid ""
"For Plaintext and HTML@.  Preferentially use nodes to decide where output "
"units are separated if @code{USE_NODES} is set.  If set to false, "
"preferentially use sectioning to decide where output units are separated.  "
"The default is true."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16544
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_NUMERIC_ENTITY"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16547
msgid ""
"For HTML, XML and DocBook@.  If set, use numeric entities instead of named "
"entities.  By default, set to true for DocBook output."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16551 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16553
#, no-wrap
msgid "Internationalization of Document Strings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16553
msgid "@nodedescription Translating program-inserted text."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16555
#, no-wrap
msgid "I18n, of document strings"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16556
#, no-wrap
msgid "Internationalization of document strings"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16557
#, no-wrap
msgid "Document strings, internationalization of"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16558
#, no-wrap
msgid "Output document strings, internationalization of"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16559
#, no-wrap
msgid "Translating strings in output documents"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16561
#, no-wrap
msgid "documentlanguage @r{customization variable}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16568
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} writes fixed strings into the output document at various "
"places: cross-references, page footers, the help page, alternate text for "
"images, and so on.  The string chosen depends on the value of the "
"@code{documentlanguage} at the time of the string being output "
"(@pxref{@code{@@documentlanguage}}, for the Texinfo command interface)."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16569
#, no-wrap
msgid "texinfo_document @r{Gettext domain}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16570
#, no-wrap
msgid "Perl format strings for translation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16580
msgid ""
"The Gettext framework with the @samp{texinfo_document} domain is used for "
"those strings (@pxref{Top,,, gettext, Gettext}).  Translated strings are "
"written as Texinfo, and may include @@-commands.  In translated strings, the "
"varying parts of the string are denoted by @samp{@{arg_name@}}, but not by "
"@code{%s} and the like.  (This convention is common for @code{gettext} in "
"Perl and is fully supported in GNU Gettext; @pxref{perl-format,, Perl Format "
"Strings, gettext, GNU Gettext}.)  For example, in the following, "
"@samp{@{section@}} will be replaced by the section name:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16583
#, no-wrap
msgid "see @{section@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16593
msgid "The expansion of a translation string is done like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16595
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, the string is translated.  The locale"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16597
msgid "is @var{documentlanguage}@code{.}@var{documentencoding}."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16600
msgid ""
"If the @var{documentlanguage} has the form @samp{ll_CC}, that is tried "
"first, and then just @samp{ll}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16601
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, in most cases, the string is expanded as Texinfo, and converted."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16604
msgid ""
"The arguments are substituted; for example, @samp{@{arg_name@}} is replaced "
"by the corresponding actual argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16608
msgid ""
"It is also possible for the string and the argument to be already "
"converted.  In that case, the arguments are simply substituted.  Similarly, "
"@samp{@{arg_name@}} is replaced by the corresponding actual argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16616
msgid ""
"In the following example, @samp{@{date@}}, @samp{@{program_homepage@}} and "
"@samp{@{program@}} are the arguments of the string.  Since they are used in "
"@code{@@uref}, their order is not predictable.  @samp{@{date@}}, "
"@samp{@{program_homepage@}} and @samp{@{program@}} are substituted after the "
"expansion:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16620
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Generated on @@emph@{@{date@}@} using\n"
"@@uref@{@{program_homepage@}, @@emph@{@{program@}@}@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16625
msgid ""
"This approach is admittedly a bit complicated.  Its usefulness is that it "
"supports specifying the formatting of the translated string independently of "
"the output format."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16627
msgid "For example, the @samp{@@pxref} translation string can be like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16630
#, no-wrap
msgid "see @{node_file_href@} section `@{section@}' in @@cite@{@{book@}@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16636
msgid ""
"which allows for specifying a string independently of the output format, "
"while nevertheless with rich formatting it may be translated appropriately "
"in many languages."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16638
#, no-wrap
msgid "libintl-perl @r{Gettext implementation}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16647
msgid ""
"If Perl is used for strings translation in @command{texi2any}, the "
"@code{libintl-perl} package is used as the @code{gettext} implementation; "
"more specifically, the pure Perl implementation is used, so Texinfo can "
"support consistent behavior across all platforms and installations, which "
"would not otherwise be possible.  @code{libintl-perl} is included in the "
"Texinfo distribution and always installed, to ensure that it is available if "
"needed.  It is also possible to use the system @code{libintl-perl} (the "
"choice can be made at build-time)."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16649 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16654
#, no-wrap
msgid "Invoking @command{pod2texi}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16651
msgid "@nodedescription Translating Perl Pod to Texinfo."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16651
#, no-wrap
msgid "Invoking @command{pod2texi}: Convert Pod to Texinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16653
#, no-wrap
msgid "pod2texi"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16655
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pod, converting to Texinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16656
#, no-wrap
msgid "Perl Pod, converting to Texinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16663
msgid ""
"The @command{pod2texi} program translates Perl Pod documentation file(s)  to "
"Texinfo.  There are two basic modes of operation: generating a standalone "
"manual from each input Pod, or (if @code{--base-level=1} or higher is given) "
"generating Texinfo subfiles suitable for use with @code{@@include}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16678
msgid ""
"The @command{pod2texi} program may be useful outside of the rest of Texinfo; "
"thus, the invocation of @command{pod2texi} is documented in the Pod language "
"using the man page format to follow the convention used in Perl standalone "
"programs, with a version on the web @url{https://www.gnu.org/software/"
"texinfo/manual/pod2texi.html} and a version included below.  The version "
"included in the manual is also an example of @command{pod2texi} use, as it "
"is converted from Pod using @command{pod2texi}."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16687
#, no-wrap
msgid "pod2texi manual page"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16689
msgid "@nodedescription @command{pod2texi} invocation in a manual page format."
msgstr ""

#. type: include
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16689
#, no-wrap
msgid "pod2texi.texi"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16692
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{texi2html}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16694
msgid "@nodedescription An ancestor of @command{texi2any}."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16694
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{texi2html}: Ancestor of @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16696
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2html"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16704
msgid ""
"Conceptually, the @command{texi2html} program is the parent of today's "
"@command{texi2any} program.  @command{texi2html} was developed "
"independently, originally by Lionel Cons in 1998; at the time, "
"@command{makeinfo} could not generate HTML@.  Many other people contributed "
"to @command{texi2html} over the years."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16709
msgid ""
"The present @command{texi2any} uses little of the actual code of "
"@command{texi2html}, and has quite a different basic approach to the "
"implementation (namely, parsing the Texinfo document into a tree), but "
"still, there is a family resemblance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16715
msgid ""
"By design, @command{texi2any} supports nearly all the features of "
"@command{texi2html} in some way.  However, we did not attempt to maintain "
"strict compatibility, so no @command{texi2html} executable is installed by "
"the Texinfo package.  An approximation can be run with an invocation like "
"this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16718
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2any --set-customization-variable TEXI2HTML=1 ...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16723
msgid ""
"but, to emphasize, this is @emph{not} a drop-in replacement for the previous "
"@command{texi2html}.  Here are the biggest differences:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16725
#, no-wrap
msgid "Most blatantly, the command line options of @command{texi2html}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16728
msgid ""
"are now customization variables, for the most part.  A table of approximate "
"equivalents is given below."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16729
#, no-wrap
msgid "The program-level customization API is very different in"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16731
msgid "@command{texi2any}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16732
#, no-wrap
msgid "Indices cannot be split."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:16742
msgid ""
"We do not intend to reimplement these differences.  Therefore, the route "
"forward for authors is alter manuals and build processes as necessary to use "
"the new features and methods of @command{texi2any}.  The @command{texi2html} "
"maintainers (one of whom is the principal author of @command{texi2any}) do "
"not intend to make further releases."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
