"Also like @samp{--delete}, but only entries if the Info file name matches "
"exactly; @code{.info} and/or @code{.gz} suffixes are @emph{not} ignored."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17239
#, no-wrap
msgid "--section=@var{sec}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17240
#, no-wrap
msgid "--section=@var{sec}@r{, for @command{install-info}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17246
msgid ""
"Put this file's entries in section @var{sec} of the directory.  If you "
"specify more than one section, all the entries are added in each of the "
"sections.  If you don't specify any sections, they are determined from "
"information in the Info file itself.  If the Info file doesn't specify a "
"section, the menu entries are put into the Miscellaneous section."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17247
#, no-wrap
msgid "--section @var{regex} @var{sec}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17248
#, no-wrap
msgid "--section @var{regex} @var{sec}@r{, for @command{install-info}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17250
msgid "Same as @samp{--regex=@var{regex} --section=@var{sec} --add-once}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17254
msgid ""
"@code{install-info} tries to detect when this alternate syntax is used, but "
"does not always guess correctly.  Here is the heuristic that @code{install-"
"info} uses:"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17258
msgid ""
"If the second argument to @code{--section} starts with a hyphen, the "
"original syntax is presumed."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17262
msgid ""
"If the second argument to @code{--section} is a file that can be opened, the "
"original syntax is presumed."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17265
msgid "Otherwise the alternate syntax is used."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17271
msgid ""
"When the heuristic fails because your section title starts with a hyphen, or "
"it happens to be a file that can be opened, the syntax should be changed to "
"@samp{--regex=@var{regex} --section=@var{sec} --add-once}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17272
#, no-wrap
msgid "--regex=@var{regex}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17273
#, no-wrap
msgid "--regex=@var{regex}@r{, for @command{install-info}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17278
msgid ""
"Put this file's entries into any section that matches @var{regex}.  If more "
"than one section matches, all of the entries are added in each of the "
"sections.  Specify @var{regex} using basic regular expression syntax, more "
"or less as used with @command{grep}, for example."
msgstr ""

