#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17291
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tag and Split Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17292
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tag Files and Split Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17294
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tag table"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17295
#, no-wrap
msgid "nonsplit Info file"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17296
#, no-wrap
msgid "split Info file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17300
msgid ""
"Info files always contain a @dfn{tag table}, to be able to jump to nodes "
"quickly.  Info files can be @dfn{nonsplit} (also called @dfn{unsplit}) or "
"@dfn{split}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17301
#, no-wrap
msgid "Indirect subfiles"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17311
msgid ""
"If the Info file contains less than about 300,000 characters the file should "
"be nonsplit.  In that case, the tag table should appear at the end of the "
"Info file.  If the Texinfo file contains more than about 300,000 characters, "
"Texinfo processors split the large Info file into shorter @dfn{indirect} "
"subfiles of about 300,000 characters each.  With @command{texi2any}, "
"splitting may be prevented by @option{--no-split}, and the default size of "
"300,000 characters may be modified with @option{--split-size} "
"(@pxref{Invoking @command{texi2any}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17316
msgid ""
"When a file is split, Info itself makes use of a shortened version of the "
"original file that contains just the tag table and references to the files "
"that were split off.  The split-off files are called @dfn{indirect} files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17322
msgid ""
"The split-off files have names that are created by appending @w{@samp{-1}}, "
"@w{@samp{-2}}, @w{@samp{-3}} and so on to the output file name, specified by "
"the @code{@@setfilename} command or the input file name.  The shortened "
"version of the original file continues to have the name specified by "
"@code{@@setfilename} or the input file name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17325
msgid ""
"At one stage in writing this document, for example, the Info file was saved "
"as the file @file{test-texinfo} and that file looked like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17331
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Info file: test-texinfo,    -*-Text-*-\n"
"produced by texinfo-format-buffer\n"
"from file: new-texinfo-manual.texinfo\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17336
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"^_\n"
"Indirect:\n"
"test-texinfo-1: 102\n"
"test-texinfo-2: 50422\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17344
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"test-texinfo-3: 101300\n"
"^_^L\n"
"Tag table:\n"
"(Indirect)\n"
"Node: overview^?104\n"
"Node: info file^?1271\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17349
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Node: printed manual^?4853\n"
"Node: conventions^?6855\n"
"@dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17358
msgid ""
"(But @file{test-texinfo} had far more nodes than are shown here.)  Each of "
"the split-off, indirect files, @file{test-texinfo-1}, @file{test-texinfo-2}, "
"and @file{test-texinfo-3}, is listed in this file after the line that says "
"@samp{Indirect:}.  The tag table is listed after the line that says "
"@samp{Tag table:}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17365
msgid ""
"In the list of indirect files, the number following the file name records "
"the cumulative number of bytes in the preceding indirect files, not counting "
"the file list itself, the tag table, or any permissions text in the first "
"file.  In the tag table, the number following the node name records the "
"location of the beginning of the node, in bytes from the beginning of the "
"(unsplit) output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17374
msgid ""
"If you are using @code{texinfo-format-buffer} to create Info files, you may "
"want to run the @code{Info-validate} command.  (The @command{texi2any} "
"command does such a good job on its own, you do not need @code{Info-"
"validate}.)  However, you cannot run the @kbd{M-x Info-validate} node-"
"checking command on indirect files.  For information on how to prevent files "
"from being split with @code{texinfo-format-buffer} and how to validate the "
"structure of the nodes, see @ref{Using @code{Info-validate}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17376 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17377
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Format FAQ"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17381
msgid ""
"Here are some questions that have been frequently asked on the project "
"mailing lists and elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17383
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why when I run @samp{info @var{foo}} do I get the same output as @samp{man @var{foo}}?"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17389
msgid ""
"Check that the Info manuals are installed.  Not all GNU/Linux distributions "
"install all the Info manuals by default.  This is regrettable, as often the "
"Info manual provides more information than the provided man page."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17390
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why not use HTML instead of Info?"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17399
msgid ""
"Manuals are rarely written in the Info format itself, but are generated from "
"Texinfo source by the @command{texi2any} program.  @command{texi2any} can "
"generate HTML as well as Info from Texinfo source. You can also access and "
"download HTML manuals from the GNU website (@uref{https://www.gnu.org/manual/"
"manual.html}).  Additionally, some GNU/Linux distributions provide packages "
"for the installation of HTML manuals."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17408
msgid ""
"Info still has some advantages over HTML for locally installed "
"documentation.  The Info browsers support index lookup and support for links "
"between locally installed manuals in multiple locations.  It's important to "
"have documentation installed locally on your machine rather than relying on "
"the Internet; this makes accessing documentation more reliable, and ensures "
"it matches installed versions of packages.  It's hoped that support for "
"browsing locally installed Texinfo documentation in some form of HTML can be "
"improved in the future."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17410
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why provide the command-line @command{info} program when the Emacs Info reader is better?"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17421
msgid ""
"The Emacs Info reader can display images, and fully supports using a mouse.  "
"There are not many differences among the Info readers besides that.  Command-"
"line @command{info} can be configured to change the default key bindings, as "
"well as change the color of cross-references and search results, and to "
"enable mouse scrolling support.  You should not need to be experienced with "
"the Emacs editor to use @command{info}.  (Some recommend another program "
"called @command{pinfo}, but this lacks in important features like index "
"lookup.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17429
msgid ""
"Some prefer to be able to scroll through the entire manual at once (as "
"happens with man pages), rather than being limited to a single `node' of "
"content at once.  Of course, there is no accounting for taste, but a single, "
"unstructured block of text becomes more awkward as a manual becomes longer "
"and more complicated.  (However, if you really want to, you can view an info "
"manual all at once in the @command{less} pager with @samp{info @var{foo} | "
"less}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17430
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why do I have `see' appearing in front of all of my links?"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17438
msgid ""
"By default, Emacs Info mode either changes the marker @samp{*note} for cross-"
"references to `see', or hides it completely.  Command-line @command{info} "
"does the same if @code{hide-note-references} is set.  Unfortunately, there "
"is no way to do this reliably, as both the @code{@@pxref} and @code{@@ref} "
"commands in Texinfo output this marker in the Info output, and the `see' "
"text is only appropriate for @code{@@pxref}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17439
#, no-wrap
msgid "Yes, but how do I get a plain link, with no extra markup?"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17444
msgid ""
"You can't.  Info is a plain text format that is displayed mostly as-is in "
"the viewers, and without the @samp{*note} text there would be nothing to "
"mark text as a link."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17449
msgid ""
"For output formats such as HTML, you can use the @code{@@link} command to "
"produce a plain link.  @xref{@code{@@link}}.  This does not produce a "
"working cross-reference in Info output or in a printed copy of the manual, "
"though."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17451
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why do lines containing links appear mysteriously short?"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17455
msgid ""
"This due to Emacs (or @command{info} with @code{hide-note-references} set to "
"@samp{On}) hiding @samp{*note} strings, as mentioned above."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17456
#, no-wrap
msgid "Can the Info format be extended to support fonts, colors or reflowable text?"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17461
msgid ""
"Any extension would be incompatible with existing Info-viewing programs.  "
"Extra markup added to Info files would be displayed to the user, making "
"files ugly and unreadable."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17467
msgid ""
"When Texinfo files are processed into Info files, information about which "
"Texinfo commands were used to markup text is lost.  Moreover, it is not "
"possible to reliably detect whether text can be reflowed (e.g.@: a paragraph "
"of prose), or whether line breaks should be kept (e.g.@: a code sample, or "
"poem)."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17471
msgid ""
"Info's core purpose is to display documentation on text terminals.  If you "
"want more, you are recommended to use the HTML output from "
"@command{texi2any} instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17475 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17477
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17479
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generating HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17477
msgid "@nodedescription Details on HTML output."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17480
#, no-wrap
msgid "Outputting HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17485
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} generates Info output by default, but given the @option{--"
"html} option, it will generate HTML, for web browsers and other programs.  "
"This chapter gives some details on such HTML output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17494
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} has many user-definable customization variables with "
"which you can influence the HTML output.  @xref{HTML Output Customization}.  "
"In particular, there is support for syntax highlighting in @code{@@example} "
"(@pxref{Syntax Highlighting}). You can also write so-called "
"@dfn{initialization files}, or @dfn{init files} for short, to modify almost "
"every aspect of HTML output.  Initialization files contain code and are "
"loaded by @option{--init-file} (@pxref{Invoking @command{texi2any}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17499
msgid ""
"Some initialization files are maintained with Texinfo and installed in the "
"default case.  For example, @file{chm.pm} produces the intermediate "
"compressed HTML Help format files that can be subsequently converted to the "
"CHM format."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17503
msgid ""
"The documentation of @command{texi2any} HTML output adaptation using "
"customization files is in a separate manual.  @xref{,,, texi2any_api, GNU "
"Texinfo @command{texi2any} Output Customization}."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17505 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17507
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Translation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17507
msgid "@nodedescription Details of the HTML output."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17509
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML translation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17514
msgid ""
"The HTML generated by @command{texi2any} generates standard HTML output.  "
"The output is intentionally quite plain for maximum portability and "
"accessibility."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17518
msgid ""
"You can customize the output via CSS (@pxref{HTML CSS}) or other means "
"(@pxref{HTML Output Customization}).  If you cannot accomplish a reasonable "
"customization, feel free to report that."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17519
#, no-wrap
msgid "Navigation bar, in HTML output"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17526
msgid ""
"@strong{Navigation bar:} By default, a navigation bar is inserted at the "
"start of each node, analogous to Info output.  If the @samp{--no-headers} "
"option is used, the navigation bar is only inserted at the beginning of "
"split files.  Header @code{<link>} elements in split output support Info-"
"like navigation with browsers which implement this feature."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17527
#, no-wrap
msgid "Escaping to HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17528
#, no-wrap
msgid "Raw HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17536
msgid ""
"@strong{Raw HTML}: @command{texi2any} will include segments of Texinfo "
"source between @code{@@ifhtml} and @code{@@end ifhtml} in the HTML output "
"(but not any of the other conditionals, by default).  Source between "
"@code{@@html} and @code{@@end html} is passed without change to the output "
"(i.e., suppressing the normal escaping of input @samp{<}, @samp{>} and "
"@samp{&} characters which have special significance in HTML)@.  "
"@xref{Conditional Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17537
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML output @subentry browser compatibility"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17544
msgid ""
"@strong{Standards}: It is intentionally not our goal, and not even always "
"possible, to pass through every conceivable validation test without any "
"diagnostics.  Different validation tests have different goals, often about "
"pedantic enforcement of some standard or another.  Our overriding goal is to "
"help users, not blindly comply with standards."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17548
msgid ""
"Please report output from an error-free run of @command{texi2any} which has "
"@emph{practical} browser or EPUB reader portability problems as a bug "
"(@pxref{Reporting Bugs})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17555
msgid ""
"In practice, the HTML produced by @command{texi2any} is slowly adjusted over "
"time towards the latest HTML standard, while also trying to keep "
"compatibility with earlier produced HTML.  We use transitional markup and "
"try to be slow enough to give time for the diverse HTML readers to adjust "
"(and for standards to reincorporate useful features that were "
"dropped@dots{})."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17557 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17559
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Splitting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17559
msgid "@nodedescription How HTML output is split."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17560
#, no-wrap
msgid "Split HTML output"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17561
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML output @subentry split"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17566
msgid ""
"When splitting output at nodes (which is the default), @command{texi2any} "
"writes HTML output into (basically) one output file per Texinfo source "
"@code{@@node}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17574
msgid ""
"Each output file name is the node name with spaces replaced by @samp{-}'s "
"and special characters changed to @samp{_} followed by their code point in "
"hex (@pxref{HTML Xref}).  This is to make it portable and easy to use as a "
"file name.  In the unusual case of two different nodes having the same name "
"after this treatment, they are written consecutively to the same file, with "
"HTML anchors so each can be referred to independently."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17581
msgid ""
"If @command{texi2any} is run on a system which does not distinguish case in "
"file names, nodes which are the same except for case (e.g., @samp{index} and "
"@samp{Index}) will also be folded into the same output file with anchors.  "
"You can also pretend to be on a case insensitive filesystem by setting the "
"customization variable @code{CASE_INSENSITIVE_FILENAMES}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17589
msgid ""
"It is also possible to split at chapters or sections with @option{--split} "
"(@pxref{Splitting Output}).  In that case, the file names are constructed "
"after the name of the node associated with the relevant sectioning command.  "
"Also, unless @option{--no-node-files} is specified, a redirection file is "
"output for every node in order to more reliably support cross-references to "
"that manual (@pxref{HTML Xref})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17596
msgid ""
"When splitting, the HTML output files are written into a subdirectory.  The "
"subdirectory name is derived from the base name (that is, any extension is "
"removed), with @code{_html} appended. For example, HTML output for "
"@file{gcc.texi} would be written into a subdirectory named "
"@samp{gcc_html/}.  The subdirectory name is based on @code{@@setfilename} or "
"on the input file name (@pxref{Setting the Output File Name})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17600
msgid ""
"In any case, the top-level output file within the directory is always named "
"@samp{index.html}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17606
msgid ""
"Monolithic output (@code{--no-split}) is named according to "
"@code{@@setfilename}, if present (with any @samp{.info} extension replaced "
"with @samp{.html}), @code{--output} (the argument is used literally), or "
"based on the input file name as a last resort (@pxref{Setting the Output "
"File Name})."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17608 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17610
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML CSS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17610
msgid "@nodedescription Influencing HTML output with Cascading Style Sheets."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17611
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML, and CSS"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17612
#, no-wrap
msgid "CSS, and HTML output"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17613
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cascading Style Sheets, and HTML output"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17618
msgid ""
"Cascading Style Sheets (CSS) is an Internet standard for influencing the "
"display of HTML documents: see @uref{http://www.w3.org/Style/CSS/}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17621
msgid ""
"By default, some CSS code is included to better implement the appearance of "
"some Texinfo environments.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17624
#, no-wrap
msgid "pre.display @{ font-family:inherit @}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17629
msgid ""
"The above tells the web browser to use the same font as the main document "
"inside @samp{<pre>} elements used for @code{@@display} environments.  By "
"default, the HTML @samp{<pre>} command uses a monospaced font."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17631
msgid "Please see the reference above for a full explanation of CSS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17635
msgid ""
"You can influence the CSS in the HTML output with two @command{texi2any} "
"options: @option{--css-include=@var{file}} and @option{--css-ref=@var{url}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17639
msgid ""
"The option @option{--css-ref=@var{url}} adds to each output HTML file a "
"@samp{<link>} tag referencing a CSS at the given @var{url}.  This allows "
"using external style sheets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17644
msgid ""
"The option @option{--css-include=@var{file}} includes the contents "
"@var{file} in the HTML output, as you might expect.  However, the details "
"are somewhat tricky, as described in the following, to provide maximum "
"flexibility."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17645
#, no-wrap
msgid "@samp{@@charset} specification, in CSS files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17649
msgid ""
"The CSS file first line may be a @samp{@@charset} directive.  If present, "
"this directive is used to determine the encoding of the CSS file.  The line "
"is not copied into the output."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17650
#, no-wrap
msgid "@samp{@@import} specifications, in CSS files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17656
msgid ""
"The CSS file may begin with so-called @samp{@@import} directives, which link "
"to external CSS specifications for browsers to use when interpreting the "
"document.  Again, a full description is beyond our scope here, but we'll "
"describe how they work syntactically, so we can explain how they are handled."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17657
#, no-wrap
msgid "Comments, in CSS files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17662
msgid ""
"There can be more than one @samp{@@import}, but they have to come first in "
"the file, with only whitespace and comments interspersed, no normal "
"definitions.  Comments in CSS files are delimited by @samp{/* ... */}, as in "
"C@.  An @samp{@@import} directive must be in one of these two forms:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17666
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@import url(http://example.org/foo.css);\n"
"@@import \"http://example.net/bar.css\";\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17672
msgid ""
"The crucial characters are the @samp{@@} at the beginning and the semicolon "
"terminating the directive.  When reading the CSS file, any such @samp{@@}-"
"directive is simply copied into the output, as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17674
#, no-wrap
msgid "If @var{file} contains only normal CSS declarations, it is"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17676
msgid "included after the default CSS, thus overriding it."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17677
#, no-wrap
msgid "If @var{file} begins with @samp{@@import} specifications (see"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17683
msgid ""
"below), then the @samp{import}'s are included first (they have to come "
"first, according to the standard), and then the default CSS is included.  If "
"you need to override the default CSS from an @samp{@@import}, you can do so "
"with the @samp{!@: important} CSS construct, as in:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17685
#, no-wrap
msgid "pre.example @{ font-size: inherit ! important @}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17687
#, no-wrap
msgid "If @var{file} contains both @samp{@@import} and inline CSS"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17690
msgid ""
"specifications, the @samp{@@import}'s are included first, then default CSS, "
"and lastly the inline CSS from @var{file}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17691
#, no-wrap
msgid "Any @@-directive other than @samp{@@import} and @samp{@@charset}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17694
msgid ""
"is treated as a CSS declaration, meaning the default CSS is included and "
"then the rest of the file is prepended."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17701
msgid ""
"If the CSS file is malformed or erroneous, the output is unspecified.  The "
"meaning of the CSS file is not interpreted in any way; the special @samp{@@} "
"and @samp{;} characters are looked for the text is blindly copied into the "
"output.  Comments in the CSS file may or may not be included in the output."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17702 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19647
#, no-wrap
msgid "NO_CSS"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17703 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19602
#, no-wrap
msgid "INLINE_CSS_STYLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17710
msgid ""
"By default, classes are added to the HTML elements and CSS rules for these "
"classes are output at the beginning of each HTML file.  Set the "
"@code{NO_CSS} customization variable to prevent classes being added and CSS "
"being used. Set @code{INLINE_CSS_STYLE} to have CSS code put in HTML "
"elements in the @code{style} attribute rather than at the beginning of the "
"output."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17711 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19688
#, no-wrap
msgid "SHOW_BUILTIN_CSS_RULES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17718
msgid ""
"Since @command{texi2any} only inserts CSS code needed by the HTML actually "
"output, the full list of CSS code potentially inserted is not visible in the "
"output document.  To get the full list of CSS rules, call @command{texi2any} "
"with the @code{SHOW_BUILTIN_CSS_RULES} customization variable set to output "
"the built-in default CSS rules on the standard output and exit, like:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17720
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2any -c SHOW_BUILTIN_CSS_RULES=1\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17723
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@documentdescription}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17725
msgid "@nodedescription Document summary for the HTML output."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17725
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@documentdescription}: Summary Text"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17727 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17733
#, no-wrap
msgid "documentdescription"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17728
#, no-wrap
msgid "Document description"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17729
#, no-wrap
msgid "Description of document"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17730
#, no-wrap
msgid "Summary of document"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17731
#, no-wrap
msgid "Abstract of document"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17732
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<meta>} HTML tag, and document description"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17741
msgid ""
"When producing HTML output for a document, a @samp{<meta>} element is "
"written in the @samp{<head>} to give some idea of the content of the "
"document.  By default, this @dfn{description} is the title of the document, "
"taken from the @code{@@settitle} command (@pxref{@code{@@settitle}}).  To "
"change this, use the @code{@@documentdescription} environment, as in:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17746
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@documentdescription\n"
"descriptive text.\n"
"@@end documentdescription\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17750
msgid ""
"This will produce the following output in the @samp{<head>} of the HTML:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17753
#, no-wrap
msgid "<meta name=description content=\"descriptive text.\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17756 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17758
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17761
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generating EPUB"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17758
msgid "@nodedescription Details on the EPUB output."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17760
#, no-wrap
msgid "EPUB, generating"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17762
#, no-wrap
msgid "Outputting EPUB"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17768
msgid ""
"EPUB is a format designed for reading electronic books on portable devices.  "
"@command{texi2any} generated EPUB 3.3 in 2024.  An EPUB file is a ZIP "
"archive container, holding informative files as well as the manual rendered "
"in HTML."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17769
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{Archive::Zip}, for EPUB file output"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17770
#, no-wrap
msgid "EPUB_CREATE_CONTAINER_FILE @subentry @r{avoiding} @code{Archive::Zip} @r{dependency}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17777
msgid ""
"The generation of the EPUB file depends on the @code{Archive::Zip} Perl "
"module being installed.  This dependency is checked at runtime.  By default, "
"trying to output EPUB without this dependency raises an error.  However, if "
"the EPUB output file is not generated, with the customization variable "
"@code{EPUB_CREATE_CONTAINER_FILE} set to 0, it is not an error if "
"@code{Archive::Zip} is not installed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17783
msgid ""
"The @command{texi2any} tests related to EPUB generation do not require the "
"installation of @code{Archive::Zip}, as they set "
"@code{EPUB_CREATE_CONTAINER_FILE} to 0 and keep the directory containing the "
"files and directories needed for the EPUB file by setting the "
"@code{EPUB_KEEP_CONTAINER_FOLDER} customization variable to 1."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17785
#, no-wrap
msgid "EPUB Output File and Directory"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17786
#, no-wrap
msgid "Container Directory and Output Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17788
#, no-wrap
msgid "Container directory for EPUB"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17789
#, no-wrap
msgid "EPUB Container directory"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17801
msgid ""
"A directory containing the files and directories needed for the EPUB format "
"is created when outputting EPUB@.  The name of this container directory is "
"derived from the base name of the input file (that is, any extension is "
"removed), with @code{_epub_package} postpended.  If an output directory is "
"specified, with @option{--output}, or with the @code{SUBDIR} customization "
"variable, the container directory is created in that directory instead of "
"the current directory.  At the beginning of a new run, the container "
"directory and all its contents are removed.  The container directory is also "
"removed after the final EPUB file has been generated in the default case."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17805
msgid ""
"The HTML files produced from the Texinfo manual are output in subdirectories "
"of the container directory.  Image files referred to from the Texinfo "
"manual, if found, are copied to subdirectories of the container directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17806
#, no-wrap
msgid "EPUB output file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17814
msgid ""
"The EPUB output file is a ZIP archive of the container directory.  The file "
"name is derived from the base name, with the @code{.epub} extension "
"postpended.  If an output file is specified, with @option{--output}, or with "
"the @code{OUTFILE} customization function, this file name is used instead.  "
"The output EPUB file is never placed in the directory specified by @option{--"
"output} or @code{SUBDIR}; only the container directory is placed there, as "
"explained just above."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17815 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19478
#, no-wrap
msgid "EPUB_CREATE_CONTAINER_FILE"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17816 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19482
#, no-wrap
msgid "EPUB_KEEP_CONTAINER_FOLDER"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17821
msgid ""
"The EPUB output file is not generated if the customization variable "
"@code{EPUB_CREATE_CONTAINER_FILE} is set to 0.  The container directory is "
"left after the final EPUB file has been generated if "
"@code{EPUB_KEEP_CONTAINER_FOLDER} is set."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17823
msgid "@xref{Invoking @command{texi2any}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17825 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17827
#, no-wrap
msgid "EPUB Cross-References"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17827
msgid "@nodedescription No cross-references in EPUB output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17838
msgid ""
"The EPUB format does not support references from an EPUB file to another "
"EPUB file.  Therefore any references to ``external'' Texinfo manuals should "
"resolve to an external URL@:.  @command{texi2any} produces these links with "
"HTML cross-reference configuration (@pxref{HTML Xref Configuration}).  Since "
"the links in the resulting EPUB are incorrect if no information is found for "
"the cross-references, @command{texi2any} issues a warning by default for "
"missing cross-references information.  If these warnings are unwanted, set "
"@code{CHECK_HTMLXREF} to 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17840
#, no-wrap
msgid "EPUB Conformance"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17841
#, no-wrap
msgid "Achieving strict EPUB conformance"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17846
msgid ""
"By default, @command{texi2any} produces EPUB expected by conformance "
"checkers as far as possible.  You may still need to adjust your Texinfo "
"manual to achieve full conformance to:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17847
#, no-wrap
msgid "Make sure that references to external manuals resolve to URLs"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17849
msgid "(@pxref{EPUB Cross-References})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17849
#, no-wrap
msgid "Avoid Texinfo code more forgiving than XHTML.  In general"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17855
msgid ""
"valid Texinfo is converted to valid XHTML, but there are exceptions.  For "
"example, you should avoid nested references and nested sectioning commands "
"and references, content before @code{@@table} first @code{@@item} and "
"omitting the second column of @code{@@table} @code{@@item}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17855
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remove spaces in Texinfo input file names."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17856
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remove form feeds that end up in output."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17860
#, no-wrap
msgid "EPUB HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17862
msgid "@nodedescription Variables set internally."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17862
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Generated for EPUB"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17866
msgid ""
"The HTML generated for EPUB is XHTML conformant, UTF-8 encoded, and "
"formatted without the usual HTML navigation headers and footers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17873
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} achieves this internally by setting customization "
"variables, such as @code{USE_XML_SYNTAX}, @code{HEADERS} or "
"@code{OUTPUT_ENCODING_NAME}.  Some features of printed output are used in "
"EPUB@.  In particular, the Top node does not appear in the EPUB output, "
"while a title page is generated.  This is obtained by setting "
"@code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT}.  @xref{HTML Output Customization}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17880
msgid ""
"The @code{OUTFILE} and @code{SUBDIR} customization variables values "
"correspond initially to the EPUB directory container and/or the EPUB output "
"file (@pxref{EPUB Output File and Directory}).  These customization "
"variables values are undefined or reset to the locations in the container "
"directory where the XHTML files are output for the HTML generation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17885
msgid ""
"This use of customization variables by @command{texi2any} is mentioned here "
"because resetting such variables is unusual; however, the variables reset "
"are used internally for the conversion, and should not interact with any "
"customization set by the user."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17887
#, no-wrap
msgid "Syntax Highlighting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17890
msgid "@nodedescription Use syntax highlighting in code excerpts."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17890
#, no-wrap
msgid "Code Examples Syntax Highlighting in HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17891 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17916
#, no-wrap
msgid "source-highlight"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17898
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Source highlighting is experimental; feedback is welcomed.  The syntax\n"
"of @code{HIGHLIGHT_SYNTAX} is very likely to change in future release.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17902 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19519
#, no-wrap
msgid "HIGHLIGHT_SYNTAX"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17903 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19529
#, no-wrap
msgid "HIGHLIGHT_SYNTAX_DEFAULT_LANGUAGE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17909
msgid ""
"You can use the @code{HIGHLIGHT_SYNTAX} variable for syntax highlighting of "
"source code in @code{@@example} blocks for the HTML output, with the help of "
"external software.  You can set @code{HIGHLIGHT_SYNTAX} to one of several "
"special values:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17911
#, no-wrap
msgid "highlight"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17914
msgid ""
"Use @command{highlight} from @url{http://www.andre-simon.de/doku/highlight/"
"en/highlight.php}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17914
#, no-wrap
msgid "pygments"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17916
msgid "Use @command{pygmentize} from @url{https://pygments.org/}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17918
msgid ""
"Use @command{source-highlight} (@pxref{,,,source-highlight, GNU Source-"
"highlight})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17925
msgid ""
"The first argument on an @code{@@example} line (@pxref{@code{@@example}})  "
"gives the name of the language used for syntax highlighting.  "
"@code{@@example} blocks without such an argument are only highlighted if "
"@code{HIGHLIGHT_SYNTAX_DEFAULT_LANGUAGE} if set, which variable gives the "
"language to use for highlighting such blocks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17935
msgid ""
"If you use a value for @code{HIGHLIGHT_SYNTAX} that is not listed above, it "
"is a template for a command line that is executed to highlight code.  This "
"gives you more control over the exact command-line options used for the "
"highlighting program, and allows you use other programs than those listed "
"above.  In this template, the name of the highlighted language is "
"substituted for occurrences of @samp{%l}, and @samp{%} is substituted for "
"@samp{%%}.  @command{texi2any} passes the content of each @code{@@example} "
"block (converted to simple text) on standard input, and the highlighted HTML "
"is read from the standard output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17941
msgid ""
"For example, if you set @code{HIGHLIGHT_SYNTAX} to @samp{colorcode -l=%l} "
"and there is an @samp{@@example C++} block in the document, the "
"@command{colorcode -l=C++} command line is executed with the "
"@samp{@@example} block passed to the standard input of the executed command, "
"and the result is read from the standard output of the executed command."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17943
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Xref"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17946
msgid "@nodedescription Standard algorithm for interoperability."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17946
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17947
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17948
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-references, in HTML output"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17954
msgid ""
"Cross-references between Texinfo manuals in HTML format become standard HTML "
"@code{<a>} links.  This section describes the algorithm used, so that "
"Texinfo can cooperate with other programs, such as @command{texi2html}, by "
"writing mutually compatible HTML files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17958
msgid ""
"This algorithm may or may not be used for links @emph{within} HTML output "
"for a Texinfo file.  Since no issues of compatibility arise in such cases, "
"we do not need to specify this."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17963
msgid ""
"We try to support references to such ``external'' manuals in both monolithic "
"and split forms.  A @dfn{monolithic} (mono) manual is entirely contained in "
"one file, and a @dfn{split} manual has a file for each node.  (@xref{HTML "
"Splitting}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17966
msgid "The algorithm was primarily devised by Patrice Dumas in 2003--04."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17973
msgid "Link Basics: HTML Xref Link Basics."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17973
msgid "Node Expansion: HTML Xref Node Name Expansion."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17973
msgid "Command Expansion: HTML Xref Command Expansion."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17973
msgid "8-bit Expansion: HTML Xref 8-bit Character Expansion."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17973
msgid "Configuration: HTML Xref Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17976
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Xref Link Basics"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17977
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Cross-reference Link Basics"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17978
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML cross-references @subentry link basics"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17983
msgid ""
"For our purposes, an HTML link consists of four components: a host name, a "
"directory part, a file part, and a target part.  We always assume the "
"@code{http} protocol.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17986
#, no-wrap
msgid "http://@var{host}/@var{dir}/@var{file}.html#@var{target}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17992
msgid ""
"The information to construct a link comes from the node name and manual name "
"in the cross-reference command in the Texinfo source (@pxref{Cross "
"References}), and from @dfn{external information} (@pxref{HTML Xref "
"Configuration})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:17997
msgid ""
"In the usual case of HTML manuals published on the World Wide Web, in order "
"to have working cross-references, external information is required to define "
"the values of @var{host} and @var{dir}.  This is detailed later on "
"(@pxref{HTML Xref Configuration})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18004
msgid ""
"If no external information is available for a manual, then defaults are used "
"for @var{host} and @var{dir} which correspond to cross-reference links among "
"a collection of manuals located side-by-side on a single host.  In this "
"case, @var{host} is hardwired to be the local host.  This could either be "
"the literal string @samp{localhost}, or be omitted entirely along with "
"@samp{http://}, according to the rules for HTML links."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18008
msgid ""
"The @var{dir} and @var{file} parts depend both on the relative split/mono "
"nature of the manual being processed, and on the manual to which the cross-"
"reference refers:"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18014
msgid ""
"If the present manual is split, and the referent manual is also split, the "
"directory is @samp{../@var{referent}_html/} and the file is the expanded "
"node name (described later)."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18018
msgid ""
"If the present manual is split, and the referent manual is mono, the "
"directory is @samp{../} and the file is @file{@var{referent}.html}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18023
msgid ""
"If the present manual is mono, and the referent manual is split, the "
"directory is @file{@var{referent}_html/} and the file is the expanded node "
"name."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18028
msgid ""
"If the present manual is mono, and the referent manual is also mono, the "
"directory is @file{./} (or just the empty string), and the file is "
"@file{@var{referent}.html}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18035
msgid ""
"The underlying idea is that there is one directory for Texinfo manuals in "
"HTML, and a given @var{manual} is either available as a monolithic file "
"@file{@var{manual}.html}, or as a split subdirectory @file{@var{manual}_html/"
"*.html}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18044
msgid ""
"Another rule, which only holds for file names, is that base file names are "
"truncated to 245 characters to allow for an extension to be appended and "
"still comply with the 255-character limit which is common to many "
"filesystems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18051
msgid ""
"Any directory part in the file name argument of the source cross reference "
"command is ignored.  Thus, @code{@@xref@{,,,../foo@}} and "
"@code{@@xref@{,,,foo@}} both use @samp{foo} as the manual name.  This is "
"because any such attempted hardwiring of the directory is very unlikely to "
"be useful for all the output formats that use the manual name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18053
msgid "Finally, the @var{target} part is always the expanded node name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18057
msgid ""
"Whether the present manual is output as split or mono is determined by how "
"you run @command{texi2any}; the default is to split, with the @option{--no-"
"split} option overriding this."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18062
msgid ""
"By default, @command{texi2any} generates links to a referent manual using "
"the same form as the present manual: if the present manual is generated as "
"split, then links to other manuals are to their split forms by default; "
"likewise for mono output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18068
msgid ""
"However, the form of the referent manual (mono or split) should usually be "
"specified in a configuration file (@pxref{HTML Xref Configuration}).  This "
"ensures that there is no mismatch between the format of the referent manual "
"that the generating software assumes, and the format it's actually present "
"in."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18070
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Xref Node Name Expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18071
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Cross-reference Node Name Expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18072
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML cross-references @subentry node name expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18073
#, no-wrap
msgid "node name expansion, in HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18074
#, no-wrap
msgid "expansion, of node names in HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18083
msgid ""
"As mentioned in the previous section, the key part of the HTML cross "
"reference algorithm is the conversion of node names in the Texinfo source "
"into strings suitable for XHTML identifiers and file names.  The "
"restrictions are similar for each: plain ASCII letters, numbers, and the "
"@samp{-} and @samp{_} characters are all that can be used.  (Although HTML "
"anchors can contain most characters, XHTML is more restrictive.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18089
msgid ""
"Cross-references in Texinfo can refer either to nodes, anchors "
"(@pxref{@code{@@anchor}}) or float labels (@pxref{@code{@@float}}).  "
"However, anchors and float labels are treated identically to nodes in this "
"context, so we'll continue to say ``node'' names for simplicity."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18093
msgid ""
"A special exception: the Top node (@pxref{The Top Node}) is always mapped to "
"the file @file{index.html}, to match web server software.  However, the HTML "
"@emph{target} is @samp{Top}.  Thus (in the split case):"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18097
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@xref@{Top,,, emacs, The GNU Emacs Manual@}.\n"
"@result{} <a href=\"../emacs_html/index.html#Top\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18103
msgid ""
"The standard ASCII letters (a-z and A-Z) are not modified.  All other "
"characters may be changed as specified below."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18107
msgid ""
"The standard ASCII numbers (0-9) are not modified except when a number is "
"the first character of the node name.  In that case, see below."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18111
msgid ""
"Multiple consecutive space, tab and newline characters are transformed into "
"just one space."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18114
msgid "Leading and trailing spaces are removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18118
msgid ""
"After the above has been applied, each remaining space character is "
"converted into a @samp{-} character."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18123
msgid ""
"Other ASCII 7-bit characters are transformed into @samp{_00@var{xx}}, where "
"@var{xx} is the ASCII character code in (lowercase) hexadecimal.  This "
"includes @samp{_}, which is mapped to @samp{_005f}."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18130
msgid ""
"If the node name does not begin with a letter, the literal string @samp{g_t} "
"is prefixed to the result.  (Due to the rules above, that string can never "
"occur otherwise; it is an arbitrary choice, standing for ``GNU Texinfo''.)  "
"This is necessary because XHTML requires that identifiers begin with a "
"letter."
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18138
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node A  node --- with _'%\n"
"@result{} A-node-_002d_002d_002d-with-_005f_0027_0025\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18141
msgid "Example translations of common characters:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18143
#, no-wrap
msgid "@samp{_} @result{} @samp{_005f}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18144
#, no-wrap
msgid "@samp{-} @result{} @samp{_002d}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18145
#, no-wrap
msgid "@samp{A  node} @result{} @samp{A-node}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18155
msgid ""
"On case-folding computer systems, nodes differing only by case will be "
"mapped to the same file.  In particular, as mentioned above, Top always maps "
"to the file @file{index.html}.  Thus, on a case-folding system, Top and a "
"node named `Index' will both be written to @file{index.html}.  Fortunately, "
"the targets serve to distinguish these cases, since HTML target names are "
"always case-sensitive, independent of operating system."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18157
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Xref Command Expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18158
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Cross-reference Command Expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18159
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML cross-references @subentry command expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18163
msgid ""
"Node names may contain @@-commands (@pxref{Node Line Requirements}).  This "
"section describes how they are handled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18165
msgid "First, comments are removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18168
msgid ""
"Next, any @code{@@value} commands (@pxref{@code{@@set @@value}}) and macro "
"invocations (@pxref{Invoking Macros}) are fully expanded."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18171
msgid ""
"Then, for the following commands, the command name and braces are removed, "
"and the text of the argument is recursively transformed:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18177
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@asis @@b @@cite @@code @@command @@dfn @@dmn @@dotless\n"
"@@emph @@env @@file @@i @@indicateurl @@kbd @@key\n"
"@@samp @@sansserif @@sc @@slanted @@strong @@sub @@sup\n"
"@@t @@U @@var @@verb @@w\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18185
msgid ""
"In addition, the following commands are replaced by constant text, as shown "
"below.  If any of these commands have non-empty arguments, as in "
"@code{@@TeX@{bad@}}, it is an error, and the result is unspecified.  In this "
"table, `(space)' means a space character and `(nothing)' means the empty "
"string.  The notation `U+@var{hhhh}' means Unicode code point @var{hhhh} (in "
"hex, as usual)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18189
msgid ""
"There are further transformations of many of these expansions to yield the "
"final file or other target name, such as space characters to @samp{-}, etc., "
"according to the other rules."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18191
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@(newline)}        @tab (space)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18192
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@(space)}          @tab (space)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18193
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@(tab)}            @tab (space)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18194
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@!}                @tab @samp{!}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18195
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@*}                @tab (space)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18196
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@-}                @tab (nothing)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18197
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@.}                @tab @samp{.}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18198
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@:}                @tab (nothing)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18199
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@?}                @tab @samp{?}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18200
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@@@}               @tab @samp{@@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18201
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@@{}               @tab @samp{@{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18202
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@@}}               @tab @samp{@}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18203
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@LaTeX}            @tab @samp{LaTeX}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18204
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@TeX}              @tab @samp{TeX}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18205
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@arrow}            @tab U+2192"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18206
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@bullet}           @tab U+2022"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18207
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@comma}            @tab @samp{,}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18208
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@copyright}        @tab U+00A9"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18209
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@dots}             @tab U+2026"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18210
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@enddots}          @tab @samp{...}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18211
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@equiv}            @tab U+2261"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18212
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@error}            @tab @samp{error-->}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18213
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@euro}             @tab U+20AC"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18214
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@exclamdown}       @tab U+00A1"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18215
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@expansion}        @tab U+21A6"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18216
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@geq}              @tab U+2265"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18217
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@leq}              @tab U+2264"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18218
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@minus}            @tab U+2212"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18219
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@ordf}             @tab U+00AA"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18220
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@ordm}             @tab U+00BA"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18221
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@point}            @tab U+22C6"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18222
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@pounds}           @tab U+00A3"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18223
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@print}            @tab U+22A3"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18224
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@questiondown}     @tab U+00BF"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18225
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@registeredsymbol} @tab U+00AE"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18226
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@result}           @tab U+21D2"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18227
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@textdegree}       @tab U+00B0"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18228
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@tie}              @tab (space)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18235
msgid ""
"Quotation mark @@-commands (@code{@@quotedblright@{@}} and the like), are "
"likewise replaced by their Unicode values.  Normal quotation "
"@emph{characters} (e.g., ASCII ` and ') are not altered.  @xref{Inserting "
"Quotation Marks}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18240
msgid ""
"Any @code{@@acronym}, @code{@@abbr}, @code{@@email}, and @code{@@image} "
"commands are replaced by their first argument.  (For these commands, all "
"subsequent arguments are optional, and ignored here.)  "
"@xref{@code{@@acronym}}, and @ref{@code{@@email}}, and @ref{Images}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18242
msgid "Accents are handled according to the next section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18244
msgid "Any other command is an error, and the result is unspecified."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18246
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Xref 8-bit Character Expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18247
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Cross-reference 8-bit Character Expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18248
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML cross-references @subentry 8-bit character expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18249
#, no-wrap
msgid "8-bit characters, in HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18250
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expansion of 8-bit characters in HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18251
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transliteration of 8-bit characters in HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18259
msgid ""
"Usually, characters other than plain 7-bit ASCII are transformed into the "
"corresponding Unicode code point(s) in Normalization Form@tie{}C, which uses "
"precomposed characters where available.  (This is the normalization form "
"recommended by the W3C and other bodies.)  This holds when that code point "
"is @code{0xffff} or less, as it almost always is."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18262
msgid ""
"These will then be further transformed by the rules above into the string "
"@samp{_@var{hhhh}}, where @var{hhhh} is the code point in hex."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18264
msgid "For example, combining this rule and the previous section:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18268
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node @@b@{A@} @@TeX@{@} @@u@{B@} @@point@{@}@@enddots@{@}\n"
"@result{} A-TeX-B_0306-_22C6_002e_002e_002e\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18275
msgid ""
"Notice: 1)@tie{}@code{@@enddots} expands to three periods which in turn "
"expands to three @samp{_002e}'s; 2)@tie{}@code{@@u@{B@}} is a `B' with a "
"breve accent, which does not exist as a pre-accented Unicode character, "
"therefore expands to @samp{B_0306} (B with combining breve)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18282
msgid ""
"When the Unicode code point is above @code{0xffff}, the transformation is "
"@samp{__@var{xxxxxx}}, that is, two leading underscores followed by six hex "
"digits.  Since Unicode has declared that their highest code point is "
"@code{0x10ffff}, this is sufficient.  (We felt it was better to define this "
"extra escape than to always use six hex digits, since the first two would "
"nearly always be zeros.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18294
msgid ""
"This method works fine if the node name consists mostly of ASCII characters "
"and contains only few 8-bit ones.  But if the document is written in a "
"language whose script is not based on the Latin alphabet (for example, "
"Ukrainian), it will create file names consisting almost entirely of "
"@samp{_@var{xxxx}} notations, which is inconvenient and all but unreadable.  "
"To handle such cases, @command{texi2any} offers the @option{--transliterate-"
"file-names} command line option.  This option enables @dfn{transliteration} "
"of node names into ASCII characters for the purposes of file name creation.  "
"The transliteration is based on phonetic principles, which makes the "
"generated file names more easily understandable."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18295
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normalization Form C, Unicode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18300
msgid ""
"For the definition of Unicode Normalization Form@tie{}C, see Unicode report "
"UAX#15, @uref{http://www.unicode.org/reports/tr15/}.  Many related documents "
"and implementations are available elsewhere on the web."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18302
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Xref Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18304
msgid "@nodedescription @file{htmlxref.cnf} and @file{htmlxref.d/*.cnf}."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18304
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Cross-reference Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18309
msgid "HTML Xref Mismatch"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18310
#, no-wrap
msgid "htmlxref.cnf"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18311
#, no-wrap
msgid "htmlxref.d/*.cnf"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18312
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML cross-references @subentry configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18313
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-reference configuration, for HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18314
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configuration, for HTML cross-manual references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18323
msgid ""
"For other manuals published on the World Wide Web to be able to have correct "
"cross-references to your manual, the @var{host} and @var{dir} parts of the "
"cross-reference need to be known by Texinfo converters when they produce "
"HTML for those other manuals.  Similarly, for your manual in HTML format to "
"have correct cross-references to other manuals, @command{texi2any} needs to "
"know how to construct the URLs for other manuals."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18331
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} reads a file named @file{htmlxref.cnf} and all the files "
"ending with the @file{.cnf} extension in the @file{htmlxref.d} directory to "
"gather information for cross-references to other manuals in HTML output.  "
"@file{htmlxref.cnf} and @file{htmlxref.d} are looked for in the following "
"directories, based on the @url{https://specifications.freedesktop.org/"
"basedir-spec/latest/, XDG Base Directory Specification} with defaults based "
"on installation directories:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18333
#, no-wrap
msgid "./"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18335
msgid "(the current directory)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18336
#, no-wrap
msgid "leading input file path directory"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18341
msgid ""
"If there is a leading directory and it is not the current directory.  For "
"example, if the input file is @file{some/dir/mymanual.texi}, "
"@file{htmlxref.cnf} is searched for in @file{some/dir} and files matching "
"@file{some/dir/htmlxref.d/*.cnf} are read too."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18342
#, no-wrap
msgid "./.texinfo/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18344
msgid "(under the current directory)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18345
#, no-wrap
msgid "@env{XDG_CONFIG_HOME}/texinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18347
msgid "(with @env{XDG_CONFIG_HOME} an environment variable)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18348
#, no-wrap
msgid "~/.config/texinfo/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18351
msgid ""
"(where @code{~} is the current user's home directory, only if "
"@env{XDG_CONFIG_HOME} is not set)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18352
#, no-wrap
msgid "@var{sysconfdir}/xdg/texinfo/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18355
msgid ""
"(where @var{sysconfdir} is the system configuration directory specified at "
"compile-time, e.g., @file{/usr/local/etc})"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18356
#, no-wrap
msgid "@env{XDG_CONFIG_DIRS}/texinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18359
msgid ""
"(for each directory in the @code{:} delimited @env{XDG_CONFIG_DIRS} "
"environment variable)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18364
#, no-wrap
msgid "@var{datadir}/texinfo/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18366
msgid "(specified at compile time, e.g., @file{/usr/local/share})"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18384
msgid ""
"All files found are used, with earlier entries overriding later ones.  The "
"Texinfo distribution includes files that are installed in "
"@file{@var{datadir}/texinfo/htmlxref.d}, in one of the last of the above "
"directories:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18386
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo_GNU.cnf"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18388
msgid "Handles many GNU manuals."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18388
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo_nonGNU.cnf"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18390
msgid "Free manuals of non GNU projects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18398
msgid ""
"You can use a local @file{htmlxref.cnf} to complete or correct the default "
"files from the Texinfo distribution.  This could be useful to correct "
"outdated data, or even to generate cross-references to local files for some "
"manuals.  Other software packages managing lists of manuals following the "
"HTML cross-references specification could install @file{.cnf} files in "
"@file{@var{datadir}/texinfo/htmlxref.d}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18403
msgid ""
"The @code{HTMLXREF_MODE} customization variable can be set to modify how the "
"files are found.  For instance, if set to @samp{none}, no external "
"information is used.  @code{HTMLXREF_FILE} sets the file name to something "
"else than @file{htmlxref.cnf}.  @xref{HTML Xref Configuration Customization}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18409
msgid ""
"The file is line-oriented.  Lines consisting only of whitespace are "
"ignored.  Comments are indicated with a @samp{#} at the beginning of a line, "
"optionally preceded by whitespace.  Since @samp{#} can occur in URLs (like "
"almost any character), it does not otherwise start a comment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18412
msgid ""
"Each non-blank non-comment line must be either a @dfn{variable assignment} "
"or @dfn{manual information}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18414
msgid "A variable assignment line looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18417
#, no-wrap
msgid "@var{varname} = @var{varvalue}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18424
msgid ""
"Whitespace around the @samp{=} is optional and ignored.  The @var{varname} "
"should consist of letters; case is significant.  The @var{varvalue} is an "
"arbitrary string, continuing to the end of the line.  Variables are then "
"referenced with @samp{$@{@var{varname}@}}; variable references can occur in "
"the @var{varvalue}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18426
msgid "A manual information line looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18429
#, no-wrap
msgid "@var{manual} @var{keyword} @var{urlprefix}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18437
msgid ""
"with @var{manual} the short identifier for a manual, @var{keyword} being one "
"of: @code{mono}, @code{node}, @code{section}, @code{chapter}, and "
"@var{urlprefix} described below.  Variable references can occur only in the "
"@var{urlprefix}.  For example (used in the canonical file):"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18445
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"G = https://www.gnu.org\n"
"GS = $@{G@}/software\n"
"hello mono    $@{GS@}/hello/manual/hello.html\n"
"hello chapter $@{GS@}/hello/manual/html_chapter/\n"
"hello section $@{GS@}/hello/manual/html_section/\n"
"hello node    $@{GS@}/hello/manual/html_node/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18447
#, no-wrap
msgid "monolithic manuals, for HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18450
msgid ""
"If the keyword is @code{mono}, @var{urlprefix} gives the host, directory, "
"and file name for @var{manual} as one monolithic file."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18451
#, no-wrap
msgid "split manuals, for HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18455
msgid ""
"If the keyword is @code{node}, @code{section}, or @code{chapter}, "
"@var{urlprefix} gives the host and directory for @var{manual} split into "
"nodes, sections, or chapters, respectively."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18462
msgid ""
"If @var{urlprefix} is omitted, the elements of the cross-references "
"correspond to cross-reference links among a collection of manuals located "
"side-by-side on a single host (@pxref{HTML Xref Link Basics}).  This could "
"be useful if you generate and publish a collection of manuals and prefer "
"linking to the generated manuals rather than to the versions found in cross-"
"references configurations shipped with Texinfo."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18469
msgid ""
"When @command{texi2any} is generating a link to another Texinfo manual, it "
"will prefer to use a line for the manual with the same splitting option as "
"the current output.  That is, when generating monolithic output (@option{--"
"no-split}), a @code{mono} URL will be preferred; when generating output that "
"is split by node, a @code{node} URL will be preferred, etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18473
msgid ""
"If no information line with the preferred splitting option is present for a "
"given manual, then other lines for that manual can be used if present.  Here "
"is the full search order for each splitting option:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18479
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"node    @result{} node,    section, chapter, mono\n"
"section @result{} section, chapter, node,    mono\n"
"chapter @result{} chapter, section, node,    mono\n"
"mono    @result{} mono,    chapter, section, node\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18481
#, no-wrap
msgid "--node-files@r{, and HTML cross-references}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18485
msgid ""
"These section- and chapter-level cross-manual references can succeed only "
"when the target manual was created using @option{--node-files}; this is the "
"default for split output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18491
msgid ""
"At present, the @file{Texinfo_GNU.cnf} and @file{Texinfo_nonGNU.cnf} files "
"distributed with GNU Texinfo serve as the main resource to locate Texinfo "
"HTML manuals in the World Wide Web.  Since they are installed in a location "
"used by @command{texi2any}, information on HTML manuals found in these files "
"will be used for cross-references by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18502
msgid ""
"If you have additions or corrections to the files distributed with Texinfo, "
"please email @email{bug-texinfo@@gnu.org} as usual.  If you publish a "
"Texinfo HTML manual on the World Wide Web, having an up-to-date location "
"listed in @file{Texinfo_GNU.cnf} or @file{Texinfo_nonGNU.cnf} should ensure "
"that all HTML manuals generated by @command{texi2any} use this location for "
"cross-references automatically.  You can get the latest versions from "
"@url{https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/@/texinfo/@/htmlxref.d/@/Texinfo_GNU.cnf} and "
"@url{https://ftpmirror.gnu.org/@/texinfo/@/htmlxref.d/@/"
"Texinfo_nonGNU.cnf}.  If you want to maintain a separate file distributed "
"with Texinfo, please email @email{bug-texinfo@@gnu.org} as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18504 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18506
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Output Customization"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18506
msgid "@nodedescription Using customization variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18514
msgid ""
"You can use many user-definable customization variables to influence the "
"HTML output.  @xref{HTML Customization Variables List} for the full list.  "
"The possibilities offered by the customization variables, ranging from "
"overall document structure and HTML language variant to formatting of "
"specific constructs, should cover most needs not already satisfied by CSS "
"customization (@pxref{HTML CSS})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18519
msgid ""
"If you ever need more control, you may be able to achieve this through the "
"use of initialization files, which are described in a separate manual "
"(@pxref{,,, texi2any_api, GNU Texinfo @command{texi2any} Output "
"Customization})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18520 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19697
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXI2HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18528
msgid ""
"If the @code{TEXI2HTML} customization variable is set, the generated HTML is "
"as compatible as possible with @command{texi2html} "
"(@pxref{@command{texi2html}}).  The effect of this variable is quite "
"unusual, as it does not directly modify the output, but sets a lot of other "
"customization variables, including some that may only be set in "
"initialization files and are described in the separate manual on "
"@command{texi2any} Output Customization.  Unset in the default case."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18530 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18531
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Output Structure Customization"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18537
msgid ""
"You can use customization variables to control the output of document titles "
"and tables of contents or other similar parts of documents.  Other variables "
"have an effect on how @command{texi2any} views the structure of a document "
"and how output is split into output files."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18538 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19691
#, no-wrap
msgid "SHOW_TITLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18539 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19748
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_TITLEPAGE_FOR_TITLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18545
msgid ""
"If @code{SHOW_TITLE} is @samp{undef}, the default, no title is output at the "
"start of the output.  If you set this variable, by default the contents of "
"@code{@@titlepage} (or output from @code{@@maketitle}) is used for the "
"title; unset @code{USE_TITLEPAGE_FOR_TITLE} to get a simple title string."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18546
#, no-wrap
msgid "NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18554
msgid ""
"By default, the HTML output is tailored for online viewing, with the Top "
"node being output as a top-level starting point for the reader.  You can set "
"@code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT} to remove the Top node, which results in output "
"that may be more similar to the format of a printed book.  By default, "
"setting @code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT} also outputs a title at the beginning of "
"the document, although you can override this by setting @code{SHOW_TITLE} to "
"0."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18555
#, no-wrap
msgid "FORMAT_MENU @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18564
msgid ""
"In each node, by default a list is output of subordinate sections for "
"navigation.  This corresponds to the @code{FORMAT_MENU} variable being set "
"to @samp{sectiontoc}.  To use menus instead to navigate in the document (as "
"in Info format; @pxref{Menus}), set @code{FORMAT_MENU} to @samp{menu}.  Set "
"@code{FORMAT_MENU} to @samp{menu_no_detailmenu} if you want menus but no "
"automatically generated @code{@@detailmenu} for the Top master menu.  If you "
"do not want either menus or subordinate sections list for navigation to be "
"output, set @code{FORMAT_MENU} to @samp{nomenu}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18565 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19436
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONTENTS_OUTPUT_LOCATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18570
msgid ""
"By default, the table of contents for the entire document is output at the "
"end of the @code{@@top} section, to have the main location for navigation in "
"the whole document early on.  This corresponds to the "
"@code{CONTENTS_OUTPUT_LOCATION} variable set to @samp{after_top}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18580
msgid ""
"You can have the table of contents output after the title (if "
"@code{SHOW_TITLE} is set) by setting @code{CONTENTS_OUTPUT_LOCATION} to "
"@samp{after_title}.  To output the table of contents at the end of the "
"document or to a separate file, if output is split, set "
"@code{CONTENTS_OUTPUT_LOCATION} to @samp{separate_element}.  You can also "
"set @code{CONTENTS_OUTPUT_LOCATION} to @samp{inline}: in this case, the "
"tables of contents are output where the corresponding @@-command, for "
"example @code{@@contents}, is used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18586
msgid ""
"You may find it useful to set @code{CONTENTS_OUTPUT_LOCATION} when "
"@code{FORMAT_MENU} is set to @samp{menu} in order to use menus for "
"navigation.  In this case, there should already be a master menu in the "
"@code{@@top} section (@pxref{Master Menu Parts}), and so the reader of your "
"manual may not need a table of contents at the same location."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18587
#, no-wrap
msgid "SPLIT @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18593
msgid ""
"By default, each node is output in a separate file.  You can change this "
"with the @option{--split} command-line option, which is equivalent to "
"setting the @code{SPLIT} variable.  @code{SPLIT} can take the values "
"@samp{chapter}, @samp{section}, or @samp{node}, or be set to an empty string "
"to indicate non-split output.  @xref{Splitting Output}."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18594
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_NODES @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18601
msgid ""
"Elementary units called @dfn{output units} are used for output, with each "
"output file containing the content for one or more output units, depending "
"on the value of @code{SPLIT}.  Output units contain the content associated "
"with a node or a sectioning command.  In typical Texinfo document sources, a "
"node command is almost always associated with an immediately following "
"sectioning command."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18614
msgid ""
"The customization variable @code{USE_NODES} determines whether the node or "
"the sectioning command is considered to be the main command.  By default, "
"nodes are used as the main component for the separation of output units.  "
"You can set @code{USE_NODES} to false to preferentially use sectioning to "
"decide where output units are separated.  When sections are the main "
"components of output units, ``isolated'' nodes not directly associated with "
"a sectioning command are associated with the following sectioning command, "
"while sectioning commands without nodes constitute output units.  "
"Conversely, when nodes are the main components of output units, isolated "
"sections not associated with nodes are associated with the previous node, "
"and isolated nodes are output units."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18615 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19739
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_NODE_DIRECTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18624
msgid ""
"By default, the @code{USE_NODES} setting also affects whether next, up and "
"prev links in node headers link to nodes or sections, with nodes used if "
"true, and sections used if false.  You can override this using the "
"@code{USE_NODE_DIRECTIONS} variable (default value is undefined).  Note that "
"this setting does not determine the link string, only where the links points "
"to; see @ref{Three Arguments, , xrefautomaticsectiontitle} for the link "
"string customization.  If nodes and sections are systematically associated, "
"this customization has no practical effect."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18625 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19472
#, no-wrap
msgid "DO_ABOUT"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18626 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19669
#, no-wrap
msgid "PROGRAM_NAME_IN_ABOUT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18632
msgid ""
"You can add a special @dfn{About} element explaining how to navigate by "
"setting @code{DO_ABOUT}, set to 0 in the default case (no About element).  "
"If @code{PROGRAM_NAME_IN_ABOUT} is also set, output the program name and "
"miscellaneous related information in the About special element; default "
"false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18633 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19643
#, no-wrap
msgid "MONOLITHIC"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18640
msgid ""
"In the case of non-split output, by default only one file is output which "
"contains any About elements (with @code{DO_ABOUT}) and tables of contents "
"elements (with @code{CONTENTS_OUTPUT_LOCATION} set to "
"@samp{separate_element}).  If you prefer such special elements to be "
"separate, set @code{MONOLITHIC} to 0 to output special elements to separate "
"files."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18642 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18643
#, no-wrap
msgid "File Names and Links Customization for HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18647
msgid ""
"There are customization variables to control output file names, and to "
"customize hyperlinks output within output files."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18650
#, no-wrap
msgid "PREFIX @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18651
#, no-wrap
msgid "SUBDIR @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18652
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXTENSION @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18653 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19422
#, no-wrap
msgid "CASE_INSENSITIVE_FILENAMES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18665
msgid ""
"You can specify the output file names with more control than merely the "
"command line option @option{--output} (@pxref{Invoking @command{texi2any}}). "
"The @code{PREFIX} customization variable overrides the base name of the file "
"given by @code{@@setfilename} or the file name and should not contain any "
"directory components.  To alter intermediate directories, use the "
"@code{SUBDIR} customization variable.  Finally, you may also override the "
"extension with the customization variable @code{EXTENSION}.  This variable "
"should be @code{undef} if no extension is to be added.  If you set "
"@code{CASE_INSENSITIVE_FILENAMES}, file names are constructed as if the "
"filesystem were case insensitive.  In that case, one file name is used for "
"all files differing only by case."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18666 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19705
#, no-wrap
msgid "TOP_FILE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18670
msgid ""
"Furthermore, the customization variable @code{TOP_FILE} overrides the output "
"file name for the top element.  This is, in general, only taken into account "
"when output is split."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18671 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19724
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_ACCESSKEY"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18679
msgid ""
"If @code{USE_ACCESSKEY} is set, the @code{accesskey} attribute is used to "
"provide keyboard shortcuts on some navigation hyperlinks.  @kbd{n} is used "
"for links to the next node or section, @kbd{p} for links to the previous "
"node or section, and @kbd{u} for up direction links.  In the default case, "
"this customization variable value is @code{undef}, and set automatically "
"based on output document split, to avoid setting @code{accesskey} to "
"multiple values in the same HTML page (@pxref{HTML Splitting})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18685
msgid ""
"There are customization variables that are specific to particular types of "
"link:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18687
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-reference command links"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18688 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19773
#, no-wrap
msgid "XREF_USE_NODE_NAME_ARG"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18698
msgid ""
"If the second argument of a cross-reference command is set, it is displayed "
"as hyperlink text (@pxref{Two Arguments}).  Otherwise the "
"@code{XREF_USE_NODE_NAME_ARG} customization variable is used to determine "
"the hyperlink text.  If set to@tie{}1, use the node name (first) argument in "
"cross-reference @@-commands for the text displayed as the hyperlink.  If set "
"to@tie{}0, use the node name if @code{USE_NODES} is set, otherwise the "
"section name.  If set to @samp{undef}, use the first argument in "
"preformatted environments, otherwise use the node name or section name "
"depending on @code{USE_NODES}.  The default is @samp{undef}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18699
#, no-wrap
msgid "Links to floats"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18700 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19768
#, no-wrap
msgid "XREF_USE_FLOAT_LABEL"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18704
msgid ""
"If you set @code{XREF_USE_FLOAT_LABEL} (default is off), the float label is "
"used instead of the type followed by the float number "
"(@pxref{@code{@@float}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18705
#, no-wrap
msgid "Links to nodes or sections for index entries"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18706 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19657
#, no-wrap
msgid "NODE_NAME_IN_INDEX"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18714
msgid ""
"In @code{@@printindex} formatting, two links are output: a link to the index "
"entry, and a link to the root @@-command containing the index entry.  The "
"@code{NODE_NAME_IN_INDEX} customization variable specifies whether the node "
"or section should be used for the link to the root @@-command.  If true, use "
"node names in index entries, otherwise use section names.  If undefined, use "
"the @code{USE_NODES} value to determine which root @@-command to prefer.  "
"Default is undefined."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18715
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menu links"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18716 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19661
#, no-wrap
msgid "NODE_NAME_IN_MENU"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18719
msgid ""
"Node names are used in menu entries links by default.  Set "
"@code{NODE_NAME_IN_MENU} to false to use section names instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18720
#, no-wrap
msgid "Table of contents links"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18721 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19683
#, no-wrap
msgid "SHORT_TOC_LINK_TO_TOC"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18726
msgid ""
"If a main Table of contents and a Short table of contents are both present, "
"the cross-references in the Short table of contents link to the "
"corresponding Table of Contents entries in the default case.  Set "
"@code{SHORT_TOC_LINK_TO_TOC} to 0 to link to the sectioning commands instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18727 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19701
#, no-wrap
msgid "TOC_LINKS"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18730
msgid ""
"If you set @code{TOC_LINKS}, links from headings to toc entries are created; "
"default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18731
#, no-wrap
msgid "Top node Up direction link"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18732 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19599
#, no-wrap
msgid "IGNORE_REF_TO_TOP_NODE_UP"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18738
msgid ""
"By default no Up reference is generated for the Top node.  You can set "
"@code{IGNORE_REF_TO_TOP_NODE_UP} so that any references to the Top Up node "
"(by default, @samp{(dir)}) appearing in other cross-references are also "
"ignored.  @code{IGNORE_REF_TO_TOP_NODE_UP} is not set in the default case.  "
"(@xref{TOP_NODE_UP}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18739 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19715
#, no-wrap
msgid "TOP_NODE_UP_URL"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18740
#, no-wrap
msgid "TOP_NODE_UP @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18747
msgid ""
"If the manual is referred to in a web page together with other manuals, it "
"may be relevant to link to that page.  Set @code{TOP_NODE_UP_URL} to the URL "
"used for Top node up references.  If @code{TOP_NODE_UP_URL} is set, the "
"value of @code{TOP_NODE_UP} is used for the hyperlink text, with "
"@samp{(dir)} as default.  @code{TOP_NODE_UP} can be used in attribute, so "
"should not contain any element."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18752
msgid ""
"For example, in the GNU project @url{https://www.gnu.org/manual/} collects "
"links to most GNU manuals; therefore @code{TOP_NODE_UP_URL} is best "
"specified as @code{/manual/} if the manual will be installed on "
"@code{www.gnu.org}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18754
msgid "@xref{First Node} for more about the Top node pointers."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18755
#, no-wrap
msgid "images links"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18756 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19573
#, no-wrap
msgid "IMAGE_LINK_PREFIX"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18760
msgid ""
"If @code{IMAGE_LINK_PREFIX} is set, the associated value is prepended to the "
"image file links; default unset.  This could be useful if image files are in "
"a specific subdirectory."
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18769
msgid "HTML Xref Configuration Customization"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18769
msgid ""
"Cross-references between HTML manuals are specified precisely (@pxref{HTML "
"Xref}).  Customization of manual locations is provided through the "
"@file{htmlxref.cnf} and and @file{htmlxref.d/*.cnf} files (@pxref{HTML Xref "
"Configuration})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18770 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19430
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHECK_HTMLXREF"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18777
msgid ""
"Default directories and file names are used for cross-reference target "
"manuals not found through HTML Xref Configuration (@pxref{HTML Xref Link "
"Basics}).  By default, a warning is given for each external manual not in "
"the HTML Xref configuration files.  If you do not want warnings about such "
"manuals, you should set @code{CHECK_HTMLXREF} to @samp{0}.  This could be "
"relevant, for example, if you know that manuals are installed locally."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18778 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19560
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTMLXREF_MODE"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18779 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19547
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTMLXREF_FILE"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18780 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19488
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXTERNAL_CROSSREF_SPLIT"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18781
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML cross-references @subentry configuration customization"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18800
msgid ""
"You can use customization variables to specify the HTML Xref Configuration "
"more precisely.  By default, the file name used for HTML Xref configuration "
"and the @file{htmlxref.d} directory are searched for in directories, files "
"in @file{htmlxref.d} with the @file{.cnf} extension and all the files used "
"for HTML Xref configuration found are used.  You can set the "
"@code{HTMLXREF_MODE} customization variable to modify how cross-references "
"to other manuals information is determined.  If @code{HTMLXREF_MODE} is set "
"to @samp{file}, the file name is directly used as the source of "
"information.  If @code{HTMLXREF_MODE} is set to @samp{none} no information "
"is used.  The default case is obtained with @code{HTMLXREF_MODE} not defined "
"or set to any other value.  The @code{HTMLXREF_FILE} customization variable "
"sets the file used for HTML Xref configuration to another value than the "
"default, @file{htmlxref.cnf}.  If @code{HTMLXREF_FILE} contains directories, "
"it is loaded if found, but is not searched for in directories.  By default, "
"the distant manual is considered to be split or monolithic based on the "
"splitting of the manual being output.  You can set it explicitly, instead, "
"by setting @code{EXTERNAL_CROSSREF_SPLIT}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18801
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-references customization, in HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18804
msgid ""
"There are also customization variables that modify various other aspects of "
"cross-references:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18806 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19711
#, no-wrap
msgid "TOP_NODE_FILE_TARGET"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18807
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can set the file name used for the Top node in cross-references by"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18810
msgid ""
"setting the @code{TOP_NODE_FILE_TARGET} customization variable value; "
"default is @file{index.html}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18811 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19494
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXTERNAL_DIR"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18812
#, no-wrap
msgid "You specify a base directory for external"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18814
msgid "manuals with @code{EXTERNAL_DIR}; in the default case, there is none."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18815 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19499
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXTERNAL_CROSSREF_EXTENSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18816
#, no-wrap
msgid "Similarly, you set the file extension for cross-references to other"
msgstr ""

#.  , which, if unset, is based on
#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18819
msgid "manuals with @code{EXTERNAL_CROSSREF_EXTENSION}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18828
msgid ""
"However, in general use of these will make cross-manual references "
"``invalid'' in the sense that the generated URL will not link to the "
"external manual, unless this manual was itself also produced using the "
"corresponding customization. It is therefore, in general, better to use HTML "
"Xref Configuration only."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18829 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19392
#, no-wrap
msgid "BASEFILENAME_LENGTH"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18834
msgid ""
"You can change the maximum length of a base file name for internal cross-"
"references by setting @code{BASEFILENAME_LENGTH}; by default, the base file "
"names are truncated to 245 characters."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18837 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18838
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customization of Navigation and Headers"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18840
#, no-wrap
msgid "HEADERS @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18845
msgid ""
"Headers and footers with a navigation panel are output in the default case.  "
"If you use @option{--no-headers}, or if the customization variable "
"@code{HEADERS} is unset, the navigation panel is only inserted at the "
"beginning of split files."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18846 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19735
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_LINKS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18851
msgid ""
"By default, @code{<link>} elements are generated in the HTML @code{<head>} "
"to specify relationships between the HTML page and other resources, for "
"example the Top node, the next node or the table of contents.  Unset "
"@code{USE_LINKS} to avoid those elements."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18852 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19678
#, no-wrap
msgid "SECTION_NAME_IN_TITLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18858
msgid ""
"The @code{<title>} and the document description in @code{<head>} are based "
"on @code{@@settitle} (@pxref{@code{@@settitle}}).  If the manual is split, "
"the node name is also added to this HTML title.  Set "
"@code{SECTION_NAME_IN_TITLE} to use the argument of the associated chapter "
"structuring command instead of the node name."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18859
#, no-wrap
msgid "OUTPUT_ENCODING_NAME @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18868
msgid ""
"By default, if an input encoding is set (typically through "
"@code{@@documentencoding}), this information is used to set the output "
"encoding name, otherwise the output encoding is based on the default "
"encoding.  A @samp{<meta>} tag is output, in the @samp{<head>} section of "
"the HTML, to specify the output encoding.  "
"@xref{@code{@@documentencoding}}.  To set the output encoding explicitly, "
"set @code{OUTPUT_ENCODING_NAME}.  The specified encoding should be a "
"normalized charset name usable in HTML, typically one of the preferred IANA "
"encoding names."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18869 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19761
#, no-wrap
msgid "WORDS_IN_PAGE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18879
msgid ""
"When output is split at nodes (@pxref{HTML Splitting}), the "
"@code{WORDS_IN_PAGE} customization variable value specifies the approximate "
"minimum page length at which a navigation panel is placed at the bottom of a "
"page.  It is not possible for you to calibrate this value very precisely for "
"exact results: this is because the count of words used for the check is "
"based on the HTML output for the node so far (including any navigation bar "
"at the top of the page), which yields a value somewhat greater than the "
"number of words that would be visible to the user in their web browser."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18882
msgid ""
"The appearance of the navigation panel is affected by the following "
"customization variables, all false in the default case:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18884 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19459
#, no-wrap
msgid "DATE_IN_HEADER"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18886
msgid "Put the document generation date in the header."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18887 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19515
#, no-wrap
msgid "HEADER_IN_TABLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18889
msgid "Use tables for header formatting rather than a simple @samp{<div>}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18890 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19570
#, no-wrap
msgid "ICONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18892
msgid "Use icons for the navigation panel."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18893 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19674
#, no-wrap
msgid "PROGRAM_NAME_IN_FOOTER"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18896
msgid ""
"If set, output the program name and miscellaneous related information in the "
"page footers."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18897 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19756
#, no-wrap
msgid "VERTICAL_HEAD_NAVIGATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18899
msgid "If set, a vertical navigation panel is used."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18901
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialization file, HTML icon direction buttons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18908
msgid ""
"Setting @code{ICONS} is necessary but not sufficient to get icons for "
"direction buttons, since no button image is specified in the default case.  "
"In addition, you need to set the @code{ACTIVE_ICONS} and "
"@code{PASSIVE_ICONS} customization variables.  You can only do this using an "
"initialization file (@pxref{Invoking @command{texi2any}}).  @xref{,,, "
"texi2any_api, GNU Texinfo @command{texi2any} Output Customization}."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18910 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18911
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Features Customization"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18913 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19753
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_XML_SYNTAX"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18914
#, no-wrap
msgid "DOCTYPE customization"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18915
#, no-wrap
msgid "DOCTYPE @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18921
msgid ""
"By default HTML is generated, but you can set @code{USE_XML_SYNTAX} in order "
"to generate XML compatible code.  The main difference is that @samp{/>} "
"instead of @samp{>} ends tags such as @code{<img>} or @code{<link>} that do "
"not have a closing tag (such tags create so-called @dfn{void elements})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18924
msgid ""
"To set the @dfn{DOCTYPE}, set the @code{DOCTYPE} customization variable.  "
"The default is the simple DTD-less DOCTYPE used for HTML5."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18926
msgid "You can set an XML compatible file beginning instead:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18930
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} --html my_manual.texi -c USE_XML_SYNTAX \\\n"
"   -c DOCTYPE='<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n"
"<!DOCTYPE html>'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18933
msgid "You could also set the DOCTYPE to HTML 4.01 Transitional:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18937
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} --html my_manual.texi -c DOCTYPE=\\\n"
"'<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01 Transitional//EN\"\n"
"  \"http://www.w3.org/TR/html4/loose.dtd\">'\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18939 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19728
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_ISO"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18940
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_NUMERIC_ENTITY @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18941
#, no-wrap
msgid "OUTPUT_CHARACTERS @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18950
msgid ""
"By default, entities are used for doubled single-quote characters "
"(@pxref{Inserting Quotation Marks}), and @samp{---} and @samp{--} "
"(@pxref{Conventions}).  Set @code{USE_ISO} to @samp{0} in the unlikely case "
"that you want a simpler output.  By default textual entities are used when "
"possible.  Set @code{USE_NUMERIC_ENTITY} to use numeric entities only.  Set "
"@code{OUTPUT_CHARACTERS} to output accented characters based on the output "
"encoding instead of entities."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18951 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19650
#, no-wrap
msgid "NO_CUSTOM_HTML_ATTRIBUTE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18957
msgid ""
"By default a custom attribute, as allowed by the standard, is used to "
"provide the target manual name in cross-references.  If it is not desirable, "
"for example to generate strict XHTML, you can set "
"@code{NO_CUSTOM_HTML_ATTRIBUTE} to prevent custom attributes being output."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18958 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19451
#, no-wrap
msgid "COPIABLE_LINKS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18966
msgid ""
"Copiable links are output for link targets for the definition commands "
"(@pxref{Definition Commands}), table commands (@pxref{Two-column Tables}) "
"where an index entry is defined and headings.  A link appears as a "
"`@U{00B6}' sign that appears when you hover the mouse pointer over the "
"heading text.  Unset @code{COPIABLE_LINKS} to prevent copiable links output."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18968 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18969
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customization of Inserted HTML Code"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18973
msgid ""
"There are variables to set the HTML code inserted at various points in the "
"output."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18974
#, no-wrap
msgid "CLOSE_QUOTE_SYMBOL @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18975
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPEN_QUOTE_SYMBOL @subentry @r{for HTML}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18978
msgid ""
"Opening quote and closing quotes needed, e.g.@: for @code{@@samp} output, "
"are set to:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18980
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{&lsquo;} and @code{&rsquo;}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18983
msgid ""
"By default, with @code{OPEN_QUOTE_SYMBOL} and @code{CLOSE_QUOTE_SYMBOL} "
"undefined."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18984
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{&#8216;} and @code{&#8217;}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18986
msgid "If you set @code{USE_NUMERIC_ENTITY}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18987
#, no-wrap
msgid "An opening and closing quote character"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18990
msgid ""
"If you set @code{OUTPUT_CHARACTERS} and the output encoding includes that "
"character."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18991
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{OPEN_QUOTE_SYMBOL} and @code{CLOSE_QUOTE_SYMBOL}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18993
msgid "If you set those customization variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18995 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19467
#, no-wrap
msgid "DEFAULT_RULE"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:18996 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19410
#, no-wrap
msgid "BIG_RULE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19001
msgid ""
"To change the HTML code for breaks (horizontal rule) inserted in various "
"contexts, set @code{DEFAULT_RULE}, which is used for most horizontal "
"separators output in the resulting HTML, and set @code{BIG_RULE} for the "
"wider separator sometimes used."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19003 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19543
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML_ROOT_ELEMENT_ATTRIBUTES"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19004 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19503
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXTRA_HEAD"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19006
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<head>} block, adding to"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19007 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19417
#, no-wrap
msgid "BODY_ELEMENT_ATTRIBUTES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19014
msgid ""
"You can set @code{HTML_ROOT_ELEMENT_ATTRIBUTES} to add attributes to the "
"@code{<html>} element.  You can define the variable @code{EXTRA_HEAD} to add "
"text within the @code{<head>} HTML element.  Similarly, the value of "
"@code{AFTER_BODY_OPEN} is added just after @code{<body>} is output.  These "
"variables are empty by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19015
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<body>} tag, attributes of"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19020
msgid ""
"You can set the attributes of the @code{<body>} element by defining the "
"customization variable @code{BODY_ELEMENT_ATTRIBUTES}.  By default, the "
"@samp{lang} attribute is set to the document language "
"(@pxref{@code{@@documentlanguage}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19021 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19665
#, no-wrap
msgid "PRE_BODY_CLOSE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19024
msgid ""
"You can define the variable @code{PRE_BODY_CLOSE} to add text just before "
"the HTML @code{</body>} element.  Nothing is added by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19027
msgid ""
"Similarly, the following variables allow for some useful control of the "
"formatting of the table of contents and the short table of contents:"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19029 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19399
#, no-wrap
msgid "BEFORE_TOC_LINES"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19031
msgid "Inserted before the table of contents text."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19032 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19382
#, no-wrap
msgid "AFTER_TOC_LINES"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19034
msgid "Inserted after the table of contents text."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19035 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19398
#, no-wrap
msgid "BEFORE_SHORT_TOC_LINES"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19037
msgid "Inserted before the short table of contents text."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19038 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19381
#, no-wrap
msgid "AFTER_SHORT_TOC_LINES"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19040
msgid "Inserted after the short table of contents text."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19045
msgid ""
"At the time of writing, the default values of these variables are set to "
"opening and closing tags for a @code{<div>} element enclosing the tables of "
"contents."
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19060
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"texinfo_set_from_init_file('HTML_ROOT_ELEMENT_ATTRIBUTES',\n"
"                           'xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"');\n"
"texinfo_set_from_init_file('NO_CUSTOM_HTML_ATTRIBUTE', 1);\n"
"texinfo_set_from_init_file('USE_XML_SYNTAX', 1);\n"
"texinfo_set_from_init_file('DOCTYPE', '<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>'.\"\\n\"\n"
"                                      .'<!DOCTYPE html>');\n"
"texinfo_set_from_init_file('USE_NUMERIC_ENTITY', 1);\n"
"texinfo_set_from_init_file('OUTPUT_ENCODING_NAME', 'utf-8');\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19064 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19065
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Customization of Specific Output"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19068
msgid "The output of specific constructs is customizable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19074
msgid ""
"In HTML, heading levels translate to @samp{<h@var{n}>} elements where "
"@var{n} is the heading level.  The following header levels are customizable:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19076 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19426
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHAPTER_HEADER_LEVEL"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19079 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19429
msgid ""
"Header formatting level used for chapter level sectioning commands; default "
"@samp{2}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19080 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19506
#, no-wrap
msgid "FOOTNOTE_END_HEADER_LEVEL"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19081 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19510
#, no-wrap
msgid "FOOTNOTE_SEPARATE_HEADER_LEVEL"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19085
msgid ""
"Header formatting level used for the footnotes header with the `end' "
"footnotestyle or for the `separate' footnotestyle; default @samp{4}.  "
"@xref{Footnote Styles}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19086 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19628
#, no-wrap
msgid "MAX_HEADER_LEVEL"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19090 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19632
msgid ""
"Maximum header formatting level used (higher header formatting level numbers "
"correspond to lower sectioning levels); default @samp{4}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19098
msgid "You may modify the appearance of various constructs by setting:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19100 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19462
#, no-wrap
msgid "DEF_TABLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19104 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19466
msgid ""
"If set, a @code{<table>} construction for @code{@@deffn} and similar @@-"
"commands is used (looking more like the @TeX{} output), instead of "
"definition lists; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19105 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19577
#, no-wrap
msgid "INDENTED_BLOCK_COMMANDS_IN_TABLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19108 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19580
msgid ""
"If set, use tables for indentation of indented block commands; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19109 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19581
#, no-wrap
msgid "INDEX_ENTRY_COLON"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19112 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19584
msgid ""
"Symbol used between the index entry and the associated node or section; "
"default is an empty string."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19113 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19633
#, no-wrap
msgid "MENU_ENTRY_COLON"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19116 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19636
msgid ""
"Symbol used between the menu entry and the description; default @samp{:}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19117 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19637
#, no-wrap
msgid "MENU_SYMBOL"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19122 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19642
msgid ""
"Symbol used in front of menu entries when node names are used for menu "
"entries formatting; default is undefined and set to @code{&bull;} if "
"@code{USE_NUMERIC_ENTITY} is not set, and to @code{&#8217;} if set."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19124 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19653
#, no-wrap
msgid "NO_NUMBER_FOOTNOTE_SYMBOL"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19128
msgid ""
"By default footnotes are numbered.  With @option{--no-number-footnotes} or "
"if @code{NUMBER_FOOTNOTES} is set to 0, a @samp{*} is used instead, or the "
"@code{NO_NUMBER_FOOTNOTE_SYMBOL} customization variable value, if set."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19131 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19132
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Customization for Math"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19134 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19533
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML_MATH"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19135
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML output @subentry math @subentry customization"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19143
msgid ""
"You can select various methods to render math in HTML (@pxref{Inserting "
"Math}).  This is controlled by the @code{HTML_MATH} customization variable.  "
"By default, the customization variable is unset and the HTML output is only "
"emphasized.  You may select other options in order to display properly "
"formatted mathematics.  For some of these options, if you set @option{--"
"iftex}, @code{@@tex} sections are converted to HTML, and if you set "
"@option{--iflatex} @code{@@latex} sections are converted to HTML."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19145
#, no-wrap
msgid "l2h"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19148
msgid ""
"Use the @command{latex2html} program to produce image files for mathematical "
"material."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19155
msgid ""
"@command{latex2html} will process @LaTeX{} math in math commands, including "
"@TeX{} math compatible with @LaTeX{}.  @command{latex2html} is used to "
"translate @code{@@tex} and @code{@@latex} sections to HTML if the "
"corresponding sections are not ignored.  Note that @command{latex2html} can "
"only process @LaTeX{}, including when processing @code{@@tex} sections."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19159
msgid ""
"Processing with @command{latex2html} should leave files in the output "
"directory, with @samp{-l2h} in their name, in particular a cache file to "
"avoid redoing translation to HTML if already done."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19161
msgid "@xref{@command{latex2html} Customization Variables}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19162
#, no-wrap
msgid "mathjax"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19167
msgid "MathJax scripts"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19167
msgid ""
"Inserts references in the output files to MathJax scripts to format "
"mathematics.  The MathJax option requires JavaScript to be enabled in the "
"browser to work."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19172
msgid ""
"MathJax handles @LaTeX{} math, including commonly used @TeX{} math "
"compatible with @LaTeX{}.  Some specific constructs (for example some uses "
"of @code{\\text}) are not supported, but this should not be a practical "
"issue."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19175
msgid ""
"If math commands are actually processed, a JavaScript license web label is "
"generated for MathJax scripts (@pxref{JavaScript license web labels})."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19177
msgid "@xref{MathJax Customization Variables}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19178
#, no-wrap
msgid "t4h"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19180
msgid ""
"Use the @command{tex4ht} program to produce HTML for mathematical material."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19187
msgid ""
"@command{tex4ht} will process @LaTeX{} math in math commands, including "
"@TeX{} math compatible with @LaTeX{}.  @command{tex4ht} is used to translate "
"@code{@@tex} and @code{@@latex} sections to HTML if the sections are not "
"ignored.  The @code{@@tex} sections are processed in @TeX{} mode, while the "
"@code{@@latex} sections are processed as @LaTeX{}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19190
msgid ""
"Processing with @command{tex4ht} should leave files in the output directory, "
"with @samp{_tex4ht} in their name."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19192
msgid "@xref{@command{tex4ht} Customization Variables}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19195 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19445
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONVERT_TO_LATEX_IN_MATH"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19201
msgid ""
"By default, with @code{CONVERT_TO_LATEX_IN_MATH} undefined, setting "
"@code{HTML_MATH} also sets @code{CONVERT_TO_LATEX_IN_MATH}.  In that case "
"Texinfo @@-commands inside @code{@@math} and @code{@@displaymath} are "
"converted to @LaTeX{}, before converting the @code{@@math} or "
"@code{@@displaymath} to HTML."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19203 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19204
#, no-wrap
msgid "MathJax Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19209
msgid ""
"This table lists the customization variables which can be used when MathJax "
"is being used, which will be the case when @code{HTML_MATH} is set to "
"@samp{mathjax}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19211
#, no-wrap
msgid "MATHJAX_CONFIGURATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19216
msgid ""
"Data to add to the global @samp{MathJax} configuration object.  Specify as a "
"comma-separated list of @code{@var{component}: @{ @var{name}: @var{value}, "
"@dots{} @}} pairs."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19218
msgid "For example, you could set @code{MATHJAX_CONFIGURATION} to"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19228
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"options: @{ enableMenu: false @},\n"
"loader: @{\n"
"    load: [\\'[tex]/physics\\'],\n"
"    versionWarnings: false\n"
"@},\n"
"tex: @{\n"
"  packages: @{\\'[+]\\': [\\'physics\\']@}\n"
"@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19235
msgid ""
"to disable the MathJax right-click menu, and to load the MathJax "
"@code{physics} extension. (See @uref{https://docs.mathjax.org/en/latest/"
"options/index.html, Configuring MathJax} in the MathJax documentation)."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19239
msgid ""
"If you override any of the defaults for this configuration output by "
"@command{texi2any} you should make sure that your new settings align with "
"the HTML output produced by @command{texi2any}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19240
#, no-wrap
msgid "MATHJAX_SCRIPT"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19245
msgid ""
"URL of the MathJax component file (e.g.@: @file{tex-svg.js}) you are using.  "
"@command{texi2any} provides a default value for this variable, but you are "
"encouraged to host this file yourself on your website so that you are not "
"dependent on others' hosting."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19246
#, no-wrap
msgid "MATHJAX_SOURCE"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19252
msgid ""
"A URL of the full source code in its preferred form for modification, or "
"instructions for obtaining such source code, for the component file named by "
"@code{MATHJAX_SCRIPT}.  `Preferred form for modification' means that this "
"should not be in a `minified' form.  Used in the license labels page "
"(@pxref{JavaScript license web labels})."
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19258
msgid ""
"Again, @command{texi2any} provides a default value for this variable, but "
"you are encouraged to host the source code for MathJax and its dependencies "
"yourself.  This is in order to make the source code available reliably, and "
"to reduce you and your users' dependence on others' distribution systems."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19261 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19262
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{latex2html} Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19269
msgid ""
"This table lists the customization variables which can be used when "
"@command{latex2html} is being used to convert @code{@@math}, "
"@code{@@displaymath}, @code{@@latex} and @code{@@tex} sections for HTML@.  "
"These customization variables are relevant only if @code{HTML_MATH} is set "
"to @samp{l2h}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19273 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19315
msgid ""
"To actually convert @code{@@tex} sections, @option{--iftex} should be used, "
"and to actually convert @code{@@latex} sections, @option{--iflatex} should "
"be used."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19275
#, no-wrap
msgid "L2H_CLEAN"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19278
msgid ""
"If set, the intermediate files generated in relation with "
"@command{latex2html} are removed; default true."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19279
#, no-wrap
msgid "L2H_FILE"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19282
msgid ""
"If set, the given file is used as @command{latex2html}'s init file; default "
"unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19283
#, no-wrap
msgid "L2H_HTML_VERSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19285
msgid "The HTML version used in the @command{latex2html} call; default unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19286
#, no-wrap
msgid "L2H_L2H"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19288
msgid ""
"The program invoked as @command{latex2html}; default is @code{latex2html}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19289
#, no-wrap
msgid "L2H_SKIP"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19295
msgid ""
"If set to a true value, the actual call to @command{latex2html} is skipped; "
"previously generated content is reused instead.  If set to 0, the cache is "
"not used at all.  If set to @samp{undef}, the cache is used for as many "
"@TeX{} fragments as possible and for any remaining the command is run.  The "
"default is @samp{undef}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19296
#, no-wrap
msgid "L2H_TMP"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19301
msgid ""
"Set the directory used for temporary files.  None of the file name "
"components in this directory name may start with @samp{.}; otherwise, "
"@command{latex2html} will fail (because of @command{dvips}).  The default is "
"the empty string, which means the current directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19304 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19305
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{tex4ht} Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19311
msgid ""
"This table lists the customization variables which can be used when "
"@command{tex4ht} is being used to convert @code{@@math}, "
"@code{@@displaymath}, @code{@@tex} and @code{@@latex} sections for HTML@.  "
"These customization variables are relevant only if @code{HTML_MATH} is set "
"to @samp{t4h}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19317
#, no-wrap
msgid "T4H_LATEX_CONVERSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19321
msgid ""
"If set, the conversion type used for @code{@@latex} sections.  Possibilities "
"are @samp{latex}, @samp{tex} and @samp{texi}.  Set to @samp{latex} if not "
"defined."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19322
#, no-wrap
msgid "T4H_MATH_CONVERSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19326
msgid ""
"If set, the conversion type used for @code{@@math} and @code{@@displymath}.  "
"Possibilities are @samp{latex}, @samp{tex} and @samp{texi}.  Set to "
"@samp{tex} if not defined."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19327
#, no-wrap
msgid "T4H_TEX_CONVERSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: vtable
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19331
msgid ""
"If set, the conversion type used for @code{@@tex} sections.  Possibilities "
"are @samp{latex}, @samp{tex} and @samp{texi}.  Set to @samp{tex} if not "
"defined."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19334 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19335
#, no-wrap
msgid "JavaScript Interface and Licenses"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19337 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19585
#, no-wrap
msgid "INFO_JS_DIR"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19338
#, no-wrap
msgid "JavaScript browsing interface for HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19347
msgid ""
"You can add an experimental JavaScript browsing interface to the HTML output "
"by setting @code{INFO_JS_DIR} value to the name of a directory in which to "
"place the code for this interface.  For example, @samp{texi2any --html -c "
"INFO_JS_DIR=js @var{manual}.texi} places files in a @samp{js} directory "
"under the output.  This interface provides some of the functionality of the "
"Info browsers in a web browser, such as keyboard navigation and index "
"lookup.  This only works with non-split HTML output."
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19349
msgid "JavaScript license web labels"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19349
#, no-wrap
msgid "JavaScript license web labels page"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19350 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19606
#, no-wrap
msgid "JS_WEBLABELS"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19351 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19607
#, no-wrap
msgid "JS_WEBLABELS_FILE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19364
msgid ""
"By default, a @dfn{JavaScript license web labels page} is set up to give "
"licensing information and source code for any JavaScript used by the HTML "
"output (see @uref{https://www.gnu.org/licenses/javascript-labels.html}).  To "
"avoid generating a JavaScript license web labels page, set "
"@code{JS_WEBLABELS} to @samp{omit}.  With @code{JS_WEBLABELS} set to "
"@samp{generate}, the default, generate a labels page at "
"@code{JS_WEBLABELS_FILE}, @file{js_licenses.html} in the default case, and "
"link to it in the HTML output files.  With @code{JS_WEBLABELS} set to "
"@samp{reference}, link to the labels file given by @code{JS_WEBLABELS_FILE} "
"in the output, and do not generate a labels file.  This last setting is "
"useful if you separately maintain a single labels file for a larger website "
"that includes your manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19367
msgid ""
"Labels files can be generated if @code{INFO_JS_DIR} is set, or if "
"@code{HTML_MATH} is set to @samp{mathjax} (@pxref{MathJax scripts})."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19369 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19370
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Customization Variables List"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19374
msgid "HTML Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19376
msgid ""
"This table lists the customization variables which apply to HTML output."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19378
#, no-wrap
msgid "AFTER_BODY_OPEN"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19380
msgid "Text added at the beginning of each HTML file; default unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19387
msgid ""
"Text output after the short table of contents for "
"@code{AFTER_SHORT_TOC_LINES} and after the table of contents for "
"@code{AFTER_TOC_LINES} if set; otherwise, a default string is used.  At the "
"time of writing, a @code{</div>} element is closed."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19391
msgid ""
"In general, you should set @code{BEFORE_SHORT_TOC_LINES} if "
"@code{AFTER_SHORT_TOC_LINES} is set, and you should set "
"@code{BEFORE_TOC_LINES} if @code{AFTER_TOC_LINES} is set."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19397
msgid ""
"The maximum length of a base file name for internal cross-references; "
"default 245."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19404
msgid ""
"If set, text output before the short table of contents for "
"@code{BEFORE_SHORT_TOC_LINES} and before the table of contents for "
"@code{BEFORE_TOC_LINES}, otherwise a default string is used.  At the time of "
"writing, a @code{<div ...>} element is opened."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19408
msgid ""
"In general you should set @code{AFTER_SHORT_TOC_LINES} if "
"@code{BEFORE_SHORT_TOC_LINES} is set, and you should set "
"@code{AFTER_TOC_LINES} if @code{BEFORE_TOC_LINES} is set."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19414
msgid ""
"Rule used after and before the top element and before special elements, but "
"not for footers and headers; default @code{<hr>}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19415
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<body>} text, customizing"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19416
#, no-wrap
msgid "lang@r{, HTML attribute}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19421
msgid ""
"The @code{<body>} attributes text.  By default, sets the HTML @code{lang} "
"attribute to the document language (@pxref{@code{@@documentlanguage}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19425
msgid ""
"Construct output file names as if the filesystem were case insensitive "
"(@pxref{HTML Splitting}); default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19435
msgid ""
"Check that manuals which are the target of external cross-references "
"(@pxref{Four and Five Arguments}) are present in @file{htmlxref.cnf} or "
"@file{htmlxref.d/*.cnf} (@pxref{HTML Xref Configuration}); default true."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19444
msgid ""
"If set to @samp{after_top}, output the contents at the end of the "
"@code{@@top} section.  If set to @samp{inline}, output the contents where "
"the @code{@@contents} and similar @@-commands are located.  If set to "
"@samp{separate_element} output the contents in separate elements, either at "
"the end of the document if not split, or in a separate file.  If set to "
"@samp{after_title} the tables of contents are output after the title; "
"default @samp{after_top}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19450
msgid ""
"If set, try to convert any Texinfo @@-commands inside @code{@@math} and "
"@code{@@displaymath} to @LaTeX{}, before converting the @code{@@math} or "
"@code{@@displaymath} to HTML.  Default @code{undef}.  If undefined, set if "
"@code{HTML_MATH} is set."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19458
msgid ""
"If set, output copiable links for the definition commands (@pxref{Definition "
"Commands}), table commands (@pxref{Two-column Tables}) where an index entry "
"is defined and headings.  A link appears as a `@U{00B6}' sign that appears "
"when you hover the mouse pointer over the heading text."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19461
msgid "Put the document generation date in the header; off by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19471
msgid ""
"Rule used between element, except before and after the top element, and "
"before special elements, and for footers and headers; default @code{<hr>}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19477
msgid ""
"If set to 0 never do an About special element; if set to 1 always do an "
"About special element; default 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19481
msgid ""
"If set to 0, do not generate the EPUB output file.  Default is set to 1."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19487
msgid ""
"If set, keep the directory containing the directories and files needed for "
"EPUB@.  The EPUB output file is a ZIP archive of this directory.  Default is "
"not defined.  Set if not defined and @code{TEST} or @code{DEBUG} is set. "
"@xref{EPUB Output File and Directory}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19493
msgid ""
"For cross-references to other manuals, this determines if the other manual "
"is considered to be split or monolithic.  By default, it is set based on the "
"value of @code{SPLIT}.  @xref{HTML Xref}, and @pxref{HTML Xref "
"Configuration}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19498
msgid ""
"Base directory for external manuals; default none.  It is better to use the "
"general external cross-reference mechanism (@pxref{HTML Xref Configuration}) "
"than this variable."
msgstr ""

#.   If unset,
#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19502
msgid "File extension for cross-references to other manuals."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19505
msgid "Additional text appearing within @code{<head>}; default unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19509
msgid ""
"Header formatting level used for the footnotes header with the `end' "
"footnotestyle; default @samp{4}.  @xref{Footnote Styles}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19514
msgid ""
"Header formatting level used for the footnotes header with the `separate' "
"footnotestyle; default @samp{4}.  @xref{Footnote Styles}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19518
msgid ""
"Use tables for header formatting rather than a simple @code{<div>} element; "
"default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19528
msgid ""
"If set, @code{@@example} blocks with language information as first argument "
"are highlighted in the HTML output.  It is also possible to specify a "
"default for the language with @code{HIGHLIGHT_SYNTAX_DEFAULT_LANGUAGE}.  "
"Syntax highlighting requires an external program to generate the highlighted "
"HTML.  The @code{HIGHLIGHT_SYNTAX} value allows to select a specific "
"program.  The possibilities are @code{source-highlight}, @code{highlight}, "
"@code{pygments}, with any other value being concatenated to the language to "
"generate the command-line for the external program (@pxref{Syntax "
"Highlighting})."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19532
msgid ""
"The default language used for syntax highlighting when there is no language "
"information."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19542
msgid ""
"Method to use to render @code{@@math} (@pxref{HTML Customization for "
"Math}).  This can be unset, set to @samp{mathjax} (@pxref{MathJax "
"Customization Variables}), set to @samp{l2h}, which uses "
"@command{latex2html} (@pxref{@command{latex2html} Customization Variables}), "
"or set to @samp{t4h}, which uses @command{tex4ht} (@pxref{@command{tex4ht} "
"Customization Variables}).  By default, setting @code{HTML_MATH} also sets "
"@code{CONVERT_TO_LATEX_IN_MATH}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19546
msgid ""
"Use that string for the @code{<html>} HTML document root element.  Default "
"undefined."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19553
msgid ""
"Set the file name used for cross-references to other manuals.  If not "
"defined, @file{htmlxref.cnf} is used (@pxref{HTML Xref Configuration}).  Not "
"defined in the default case.  If @code{TEST} is set, @code{HTMLXREF_MODE} is "
"set to the default and @code{HTMLXREF_FILE} is not defined, information on "
"cross-references to other manuals is not used."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19558
msgid ""
"If @code{HTMLXREF_MODE} is set to @samp{file} the file name is directly used "
"as the source of information.  Otherwise the file name is searched for in "
"directories, and all the files found are used (@pxref{HTML Xref "
"Configuration}).  @file{htmlxref.d/*.cnf} files are also used in that case."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19569
msgid ""
"How cross-references to other manuals information is determined.  If set to "
"@samp{none}, no information is used.  If set to @samp{file}, the information "
"is determined from a file path, @file{htmlxref.cnf} in the default case, or "
"the value of @code{HTMLXREF_FILE}.  If not defined (the default) or set to "
"any other value, search for the @code{HTMLXREF_FILE} file name and the "
"@file{htmlxref.d} directory in directories and use all the "
"@code{HTMLXREF_FILE} files and files in the @file{htmlxref.d} directory with "
"the @file{.cnf} extension (@pxref{HTML Xref Configuration})."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19572
msgid "Use icons for the navigation panel; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19576
msgid ""
"If set, the associated value is prepended to the image file links; default "
"unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19593
msgid ""
"(Experimental.)  Add a JavaScript browsing interface to the manual.  The "
"value of the variable is the directory to place the code for this interface, "
"so you would run the program as e.g.@: @samp{texi2any --html -c "
"INFO_JS_DIR=js @var{manual}.texi} to place files in a @samp{js} directory "
"under the output.  This provides some of the functionality of the Info "
"browsers in a web browser, such as keyboard navigation and index lookup.  "
"This only works with non-split HTML output."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19598
msgid ""
"The interface should provide an acceptable fallback in functionality if "
"JavaScript or web browser features are not available.  However, please be "
"cautious when using this option, in case you do make your documentation "
"harder to access for some of your users."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19601
msgid "Ignore references to @code{TOP_NODE_UP}, the up node for the Top node."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19605
msgid ""
"Put CSS directly in HTML elements rather than at the beginning of the "
"output; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19612
msgid ""
"Specify how to use a @dfn{JavaScript license web labels} page to give "
"licensing information and source code for any JavaScript used in the HTML "
"files for the manual.  (See @uref{https://www.gnu.org/licenses/javascript-"
"labels.html})."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19619
msgid ""
"With the value @samp{generate} (the default), generate a labels page at "
"@code{JS_WEBLABELS_FILE}, and link to it in the HTML output files.  Only do "
"this if actually referencing JavaScript files (either with @code{HTML_MATH} "
"set to @samp{mathjax}, or when using the experimental JS browsing interface "
"when @code{INFO_JS_DIR} is set).  With this setting, "
"@code{JS_WEBLABELS_FILE} must be a relative file name."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19625
msgid ""
"With the value @samp{reference}, link to the labels file given by "
"@code{JS_WEBLABELS_FILE} in the output, and do not generate a labels file.  "
"This setting is useful if you separately maintain a single labels file for a "
"larger website that includes your manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19627
msgid "With @samp{omit}, neither generate nor link to a labels file."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19646
msgid ""
"Output only one file including the table of contents.  Set by default, but "
"only relevant when the output is not split."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19649
msgid "Do not use CSS; default false.  @xref{HTML CSS}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19652
msgid "Do not output HTML with custom attributes in elements; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19656
msgid ""
"Symbol used for footnotes if @code{NUMBER_FOOTNOTES} is false.  Default is "
"@code{*}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19660
msgid ""
"If true, use node names in index entries, otherwise prefer section names.  "
"If undefined, use @code{USE_NODES} value in HTML.  Default is undefined."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19664
msgid ""
"If set, use node names in menu entries, otherwise prefer section names; "
"default true."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19668
msgid ""
"If set, the given text will appear at the footer of each HTML file; default "
"unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19673
msgid ""
"Used when an About element is output.  If set, output the program name and "
"miscellaneous related information in About special element; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19677
msgid ""
"If set, output the program name and miscellaneous related information in the "
"page footers; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19682
msgid ""
"If set, when output is split, use the argument of the chapter structuring "
"command (e.g., @code{@@chapter} or @code{@@section})  in the @code{<title>} "
"instead of the argument to @code{@@node}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19687
msgid ""
"If set, the cross-references in the Short table of contents links to the "
"corresponding Table of Contents entries, if a Table of Contents is output; "
"default true."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19690
msgid "Output the built-in default CSS rules on the standard output and exit."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19695
msgid ""
"If set, output the title at the beginning of the document; default "
"@samp{undef}.  If set to @samp{undef}, setting @code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT} "
"also sets @code{SHOW_TITLE} for HTML."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19696
#, no-wrap
msgid "compatibility, with @command{texi2html}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19700
msgid ""
"Generate HTML and try to be as compatible as possible with "
"@command{texi2html}; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19704
msgid "If set, links from headings to toc entries are created; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19710
msgid ""
"This file name may be used for the top-level file.  The extension is set "
"appropriately, if necessary.  This is used to override the default, and is, "
"in general, only taken into account when output is split, and for HTML@."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19714
msgid ""
"File name used for the Top node in cross-references; default is "
"@code{index.html}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19722
msgid ""
"A URL used for Top node up references; the default is @code{undef}, in that "
"case no Top node Up reference is generated.  For overriding the Up pointer "
"name in case @code{TOP_NODE_UP_URL} is set and for other formats, see "
"@code{TOP_NODE_UP} in @ref{Customization Variables for Multiple Formats}.  "
"@xref{File Names and Links Customization for HTML}.  For more about the Top "
"node pointers, @pxref{First Node}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19723
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{accesskey} @subentry customization variable for"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19727
msgid ""
"Use @code{accesskey} in cross-references; default @code{undef}. If "
"@code{undef}, set if the output is split."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19732
msgid ""
"Use entities for doubled single-quote characters (@pxref{Inserting Quotation "
"Marks}), and @samp{---} and @samp{--} (@pxref{Conventions}); default true."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19733
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<link>} HTML tag, in @code{<head>}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19734
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<head>} HTML tag, and @code{<link>}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19738
msgid ""
"Generate @code{<link>} elements in the HTML @code{<head>} output; default "
"true."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19747
msgid ""
"If true, use nodes to determine where next, up and prev link to in node "
"headers.  If false, use sections.  If undefined, use @code{USE_NODES} "
"value.  Default is undefined.  Note that this setting does not determine the "
"link string, only where the links points to; see @ref{Three Arguments, , "
"xrefautomaticsectiontitle} for the link string customization.  If nodes and "
"sections are systematically associated, this customization has no practical "
"effect."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19752
msgid ""
"Use the full @code{@@titlepage} (or output from @code{@@maketitle}) as the "
"title, not a simple title string; default true.  Only relevant if "
"@code{SHOW_TITLE} is set."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19755
msgid "Use XML/XHTML compatible syntax."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19758
msgid "If set, a vertical navigation panel is used; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19759
#, no-wrap
msgid "Navigation panel, bottom of page"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19760
#, no-wrap
msgid "Navigation footer"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19767
msgid ""
"When output is split by nodes, specifies the approximate minimum page length "
"at which a navigation panel is placed at the bottom of a page.  To avoid "
"ever having the navigation buttons at the bottom of a page, set this to a "
"sufficiently large number.  The default is 200."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19772
msgid ""
"If set, for the float name in cross-references, use the float label instead "
"of the type followed by the float number (@pxref{@code{@@float}}).  The "
"default is off."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19782
msgid ""
"Only relevant for cross-reference commands with no cross reference name "
"(second argument).  If set to@tie{}1, use the node name (first) argument in "
"cross-reference @@-commands for the text displayed as the hyperlink.  If set "
"to@tie{}0, use the node name if @code{USE_NODES} is set, otherwise the "
"section name.  If set to @samp{undef}, use the first argument in "
"preformatted environments, otherwise use the node name or section name "
"depending on @code{USE_NODES}.  The default is @samp{undef}."
msgstr ""

#. type: appendix
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19786 texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19788
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@-Command Details"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19788
msgid "@nodedescription Details of the Texinfo @@-commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19792
msgid ""
"Here are the details of @@-commands: information about their syntax, a list "
"of commands, and information about where commands can appear."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19794
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command Syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19795
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@-Command Syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19796
#, no-wrap
msgid "@sortas{at} @@-commands @subentry syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19797
#, no-wrap
msgid "Syntax, of @@-commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19798
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19801
msgid "Texinfo has the following types of @@-command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19803
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Brace commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19808
msgid ""
"These commands start with @@ followed by a letter or a word, followed by an "
"argument within braces.  For example, the command @code{@@dfn} indicates the "
"introductory or defining use of a term; it is used as follows: @samp{In "
"Texinfo, @@@@-commands are @@dfn@{mark-up@} commands.}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19809
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Line commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19815
msgid ""
"These commands occupy an entire line.  The line starts with @@, followed by "
"the name of the command (a word); for example, @code{@@center} or "
"@code{@@cindex}.  If no argument is needed, the word is followed by the end "
"of the line.  If there is an argument, it is separated from the command name "
"by a space.  Braces are not used."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19817
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Block commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19825
msgid ""
"These commands are written at the start of a line, with general text on "
"following lines, terminated by a matching @code{@@end} command on a line of "
"its own.  For example, @code{@@example}, then the lines of a coding example, "
"then @code{@@end example}.  Some of these block commands take arguments as "
"line commands do; for example, @code{@@enumerate A} opening an environment "
"terminated by @code{@@end enumerate}.  Here @samp{A} is the argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19826
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Symbol insertion commands with no arguments"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19833
msgid ""
"These commands start with @@ followed by a word followed by a left and "
"right- brace.  These commands insert special symbols in the document; they "
"do not take arguments.  Some examples: @code{@@dots@{@}} @result{} "
"@samp{@dots{}}, @code{@@equiv@{@}} @result{} @samp{@equiv{}}, "
"@code{@@TeX@{@}} @result{} `@TeX{}', and @code{@@bullet@{@}} @result{} "
"@samp{@bullet{}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19834
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Non-alphabetic commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19843
msgid ""
"The names of commands in all of the above categories consist of alphabetic "
"characters, almost entirely in lower-case.  Unlike those, the non-alphabetic "
"commands consist of an @@ followed by a punctuation mark or other character "
"that is not part of the Latin alphabet.  Non-alphabetic commands are almost "
"always part of text within a paragraph.  The non-alphabetic commands include "
"@code{@@@@}, @code{@@@{}, @code{@@@}}, @code{@@.}, @code{@@@kbd{SPACE}}, and "
"most of the accent commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19844
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Miscellaneous commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19852
msgid ""
"There are a handful of commands that don't fit into any of the above "
"categories; for example, the obsolete command @code{@@refill}, which is "
"always used at the end of a paragraph immediately following the final period "
"or other punctuation character.  @code{@@refill} takes no argument and does "
"not require braces.  Likewise, @code{@@tab} used in a @code{@@multitable} "
"block does not take arguments, and is not followed by braces."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19854
#, no-wrap
msgid "Braces and argument syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19864
msgid ""
"Thus, the alphabetic commands fall into classes that have different argument "
"syntaxes.  You cannot tell to which class a command belongs by the "
"appearance of its name, but you can tell by the command's meaning: if the "
"command stands for a glyph, it is in class 4 and does not require an "
"argument; if it makes sense to use the command among other text as part of a "
"paragraph, the command is in class 1 and must be followed by an argument in "
"braces.  The non-alphabetic commands, such as @code{@@:}, are exceptions to "
"the rule; they do not need braces."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19868
msgid ""
"The purpose of having different syntax for commands is to make Texinfo files "
"easier to read, and also to help the GNU Emacs paragraph and filling "
"commands work properly."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19870
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command List"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19871
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@-Command List"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19872
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alphabetical @@-command list"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19873
#, no-wrap
msgid "List of @@-commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19874
#, no-wrap
msgid "@sortas{at} @@-commands @subentry list of"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19875
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reference to @@-commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19880
msgid ""
"Here is an alphabetical list of the @@-commands in Texinfo.  Square "
"brackets, @t{[}@w{ }@t{]}, indicate optional arguments; an ellipsis, "
"@samp{@dots{}}, indicates repeated text."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19882
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@@var{whitespace}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19885
msgid ""
"An @code{@@} followed by a space, tab, or newline produces a normal, "
"stretchable, interword space.  @xref{Multiple Spaces}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19886
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@!"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19889
msgid ""
"Produce an exclamation point that ends a sentence (usually after an end-of-"
"sentence capital letter).  @xref{Ending a Sentence}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19890
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@\""
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19891
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@'"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19894
msgid ""
"Generate an umlaut or acute accent, respectively, over the next character, "
"as in @\"o and @'o.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19895
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@&"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19896
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ampchar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19898
msgid "Generate an ampersand.  @xref{Inserting an Ampersand}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19901
msgid "Force a line break.  @xref{Line Breaks}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19902
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@,@{@var{c}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19905
msgid ""
"Generate a cedilla accent under @var{c}, as in @,{c}.  @xref{Inserting "
"Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19908
msgid ""
"Insert a discretionary hyphenation point.  @xref{@code{@@- @@hyphenation}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19909
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19912
msgid ""
"Produce a period that ends a sentence (usually after an end-of-sentence "
"capital letter).  @xref{Ending a Sentence}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19913
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19915
msgid "Produces no output, but allows a line break.  @xref{Line Breaks}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19916
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@:"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19920
msgid ""
"Tell printed output processors to refrain from inserting extra whitespace "
"after an immediately preceding period, question mark, exclamation mark, or "
"colon.  @xref{Not Ending a Sentence}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19921
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@="
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19924
msgid ""
"Generate a macron (bar) accent over the next character, as in @=o.  "
"@xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19925
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@?"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19928
msgid ""
"Produce a question mark that ends a sentence (usually after an end-of-"
"sentence capital letter).  @xref{Ending a Sentence}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19929
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@@@"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19930
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@atchar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19932
msgid "Insert an at sign, @samp{@@}.  @xref{Inserting an Atsign}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19933
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@\\"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19934
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@backslashchar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19938
msgid ""
"Insert a backslash, @samp{\\}; @code{@@backslashchar@{@}} works anywhere, "
"while @code{@@\\} works only inside @code{@@math}.  @xref{Inserting a "
"Backslash}, and @ref{Inserting Math}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19939
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@^"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19940
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@`"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19944
msgid ""
"Generate a circumflex (hat) or grave accent, respectively, over the next "
"character, as in @^o and @`e.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19945
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@@{"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19946
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@lbracechar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19948
msgid "Insert a left brace, @samp{@{}.  @xref{Inserting Braces}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19949
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19950
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@rbracechar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19952
msgid "Insert a right brace, @samp{@}}.  @xref{Inserting Braces}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19953
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@~"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19956
msgid ""
"Generate a tilde accent over the next character, as in @~N.  @xref{Inserting "
"Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19957
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@AA@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19958
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@aa@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19961
msgid ""
"Generate the uppercase and lowercase Scandinavian A-ring letters, "
"respectively: @AA{}, @aa{}.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19965
msgid ""
"Indicate a general abbreviation, such as `Comput.'.  @xref{@code{@@abbr}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19969
msgid ""
"Indicate an acronym in all capital letters, such as `NASA'.  "
"@xref{@code{@@acronym}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19970
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@AE@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19971
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ae@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19974
msgid ""
"Generate the uppercase and lowercase AE ligatures, respectively: @AE{}, "
"@ae{}.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19975
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@afivepaper"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19977
msgid "Change page dimensions for the A5 paper size.  @xref{A4 Paper}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19978
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@afourlatex"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19979
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@afourpaper"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19980
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@afourwide"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19982
msgid "Change page dimensions for the A4 paper size.  @xref{A4 Paper}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19986
msgid ""
"Make the command @samp{@@@var{new}} a synonym for the existing command "
"@samp{@@@var{existing}}.  @xref{@code{@@alias}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19987
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@allowcodebreaks @var{true-false}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19990
msgid ""
"Control breaking at @samp{-} and @samp{_} in printed output.  "
"@xref{@code{@@allowcodebreaks}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19991
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@anchor@{@var{name}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19994
msgid ""
"Define @var{name} as the current location for use as a cross-reference "
"target.  @xref{@code{@@anchor}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19995
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendix @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19998
msgid ""
"Begin an appendix.  The title appears in the table of contents.  "
"@xref{@code{@@unnumbered @@appendix}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:19999
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsec @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20000
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsection @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20005
msgid ""
"Begin an appendix section within an appendix.  The section title appears in "
"the table of contents.  @code{@@appendixsection} is a longer spelling of the "
"@code{@@appendixsec} command.  @xref{@code{@@unnumberedsec @@appendixsec "
"@@heading}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20006
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsubsec @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20009
msgid ""
"Begin an appendix subsection.  The title appears in the table of contents.  "
"@xref{@code{@@unnumberedsubsec @@appendixsubsec @@subheading}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20010
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsubsubsec @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20013
msgid ""
"Begin an appendix subsubsection.  The title appears in the table of "
"contents.  @xref{@code{@@subsubsection}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20014
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@arrow@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20017
msgid ""
"Generate a right arrow glyph: @samp{@arrow{}}.  Used by default for "
"@code{@@click}.  @xref{Click Sequences}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20023
msgid ""
"Keep the argument as is.  Used following @code{@@table}, @code{@@ftable}, "
"and @code{@@vtable} to print the table's first column without highlighting "
"(``as is'').  @xref{@code{@@asis}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20024
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@author @var{author}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20027
msgid ""
"Set a manual author in the title page.  @xref{@code{@@title @@subtitle "
"@@author}}.  Set a quotation author in @code{@@quotation}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@quotation}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20028
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@b@{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20030
msgid "Set @var{text} in a @b{bold} font, if possible.  @xref{Fonts}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20031
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@bullet@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20034
msgid ""
"Generate a large round dot, @bullet{}, or the closest possible thing to "
"one.  Often used with @code{@@itemize}.  @xref{@code{@@bullet}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20035
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@bsixpaper"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20037
msgid "Change page dimensions for the B6 paper size.  @xref{A4 Paper}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20038
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@bye"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20041
msgid ""
"Stop processing a file.  The processors do not see anything in the input "
"file following @code{@@bye}.  @xref{Ending a File}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20042
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@c @var{comment}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20046
msgid ""
"Begin a comment in Texinfo.  The rest of the line does not appear in any "
"output.  A synonym for @code{@@comment}.  @kbd{DEL} also starts a comment.  "
"@xref{Comments}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20047
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@caption"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20050
msgid ""
"Define the full caption for a @code{@@float}.  @xref{@code{@@caption "
"@@shortcaption}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20055
msgid ""
"Highlight an example or quotation by drawing a box with rounded corners "
"around it, if possible.  Pair with @code{@@end cartouche}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@cartouche}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20056
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@center @var{line-of-text}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20059
msgid ""
"Center the line of text following the command.  @xref{@code{@@titlefont "
"@@center @@sp}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20060
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@centerchap @var{line-of-text}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20062
msgid ""
"Like @code{@@chapter}, but centers the chapter title.  "
"@xref{@code{@@chapter}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20063
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@chapheading @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20066
msgid ""
"Print an unnumbered chapter-like heading, but omit from the table of "
"contents.  @xref{@code{@@majorheading @@chapheading}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20067
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@chapter @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20070
msgid ""
"Begin a numbered chapter.  The chapter title appears in the table of "
"contents.  @xref{@code{@@chapter}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20071
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@cindex @var{entry}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20074
msgid ""
"Add @var{entry} to the index of concepts.  @xref{Index Entries, , Defining "
"the Entries of an Index}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20078
msgid ""
"Highlight the name of a book or other reference that has no companion Info "
"file.  @xref{@code{@@cite}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20085
msgid ""
"Unset @var{flag}, preventing the Texinfo formatting commands from formatting "
"text between subsequent pairs of @code{@@ifset @var{flag}} and @code{@@end "
"ifset} commands, and preventing @code{@@value@{@var{flag}@}} from expanding "
"to the value to which @var{flag} is set.  @xref{@code{@@set @@clear "
"@@value}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/upstream/texinfo.texi:20086
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@click@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
